1477618778,6860,3-Car,4.1824199946459764e-14,1018,3-Car,34536,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum features a very broad highest peak centered around 2.4 µs (rising at ~2.15 µs), followed by broad peaks at ~3.92 µs and ~5.53 µs. Although the spacing from the first to the second peak is ~1.5 µs, the third peak appears ~1.61 µs after the second peak (at ~5.53 µs) rather than matching the Na(NaOH)2+ position expected ~1.05 µs after the m/z 63 peak (~4.97 µs), indicating a different salt (such as NaCl) or mineral series rather than 3-OH.",
1477626137,10363,3-Car,1.700579916686165e-14,1018,3-Car,34537,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because its highest peak (amplitude 1.0) is located at approximately 5.42 s rather than being a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 s, violating Rule 1. Although broad peaks appear at ~2.35 s and ~3.82 s, the extremely broad peak profiles and the dominance of the late peak at 5.42 s are inconsistent with the clean sodium hydroxide cluster pattern.",
1477630001,12290,3-KNa,1.3125099931324182e-14,1018,3-KNa,34357,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~1.17 s (outside the typical 1.4–2.0 s range for Na+) and is followed by a prominent second peak at ~1.86 s (a distance of ~0.69 s). Even if either peak is considered Na+, there is no corresponding Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak 1.49 s later (at ~2.66 s or ~3.35 s).",
1477679722,28316,3-KNa,4.1896800834434825e-14,1018,3-KNa,34538,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~2.60 µs (about 0.72 µs after the initial peak at ~1.88 µs), violating Rule 1 which requires Na+ between 1.4 and 2.0 µs to be the dominant peak. Additionally, the major cluster peaks at ~4.25 µs and ~4.68 µs do not follow the expected 1.49 µs sodium hydroxide spacing.",
1477687751,35389,3-Car,5.326729996760898e-14,1018,3-Car,34539,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the spectrum shows a main peak at ~2.22 µs and a major peak at ~3.70 µs (~1.48 µs later), the subsequent peaks at ~4.30 µs, ~4.75 µs, and a huge peak at ~5.33 µs (with broad, asymmetric profiles) do not match the sodium hydroxide cluster series (expected at ~4.21 µs and ~4.75 µs without the dominant 5.33 µs peak), indicating another salt or mineral composition.",
1477698673,42475,3-Cl,1.2826400369331942e-13,1018,3-Cl,34541,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.12 µs (nearly reaching 1.0 alongside the baseline-elevated cluster peak) followed ~1.46 µs later by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.58 µs. The hydroxide series is further confirmed by the hydrated cluster peak Na(NaOH)(H2O)+ at ~4.09 µs (~0.51 µs after the m/z 63 peak) and subsequent higher-order clusters at ~4.65 µs, ~5.03 µs, and ~5.42 µs.",
1481851286,15307,4,1.9019100259542315e-13,1018,4,0,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is a broad feature at ~2.20 5s followed closely by another major peak of nearly equal amplitude at ~2.85 5s (a separation of ~0.65 5s) and a smaller peak at ~3.46 5s. It lacks both a clean, dominant Na+ peak in the typical 1.4-2.0 5s range and the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 5s after the main peak (which would appear near 3.69 5s).",
1509253652,11767,4,2.6500000043189025e-14,1018,4,2440,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is a broad feature at ~3.21 us rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 us. Furthermore, the peak at ~1.51 us is followed by major peaks at ~2.28 us (0.77 us later) and ~3.21 us (1.70 us later), lacking the diagnostic Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak 1.49 us after Na+.",
1509313409,15677,3-Car,5.347040152770162e-14,1018,3-Car,34591,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum lacks a sharp, dominant Na+ peak in the expected 1.4–2.0 µs region, instead displaying extremely broad features peaking at ~2.52 µs, ~4.00 µs, and ~5.61 µs (where the ~5.61 µs peak reaches nearly the same maximum amplitude of 1.0). This broad, elevated profile is inconsistent with the clean sodium hydroxide cluster progression of a 3-OH grain.",
1509313472,15740,3-Car,6.652350111741034e-14,1018,3-Car,34592,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum lacks a sharp Na+ peak in the typical 1.4 to 2.0 5s range, showing instead a series of broad, heavily tailed peaks at approximately 2.30 5s, 3.72 5s, and 5.33 5s that do not match the expected sodium hydroxide cluster progression.",
1509314528,16795,3-Cl,3.732000060548135e-14,1018,3-Cl,34593,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because its highest peak is a broad feature at ~4.15 bc	ext{s} rather than a sharp Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 bc	ext{s}, violating Rule 1. Furthermore, the broad peaks at ~2.1-2.3 bc	ext{s}, ~3.55 bc	ext{s}, and ~5.45 bc	ext{s} do not follow the characteristic sodium hydroxide cluster progression.",
1509315063,17330,3-Car,2.0010399858372968e-13,1018,3-Car,34594,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The highest peak is Na+ at approximately 2.02-2.07 5s, followed about 1.49 5s later by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at 3.51 5s (riding on an elevated baseline) and a smaller Na(NaOH)2+ peak at 4.55 5s.",
1509315576,17843,2,5.3772301010762e-14,1018,2,2533,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum lacks a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 5s, instead showing a rising baseline with its highest peak at ~3.45 5s and other steps at ~2.83 5s and ~4.0 5s. Because Rule 1 is violated and there is no sodium hydroxide cluster series, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1509316243,18509,1,1.731090043446265e-14,1018,1,2543,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peaks are located at ~0.14 µs and ~1.00 µs, rather than being a dominant Na+ peak in the typical 1.4–2.0 µs range. Furthermore, there is no distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak 1.49 µs after either of the early peaks or after the smaller peak at ~1.86 µs, as the spectrum transitions into a noisy, elevated baseline.",
1509316937,19203,2,3.73322012680536e-14,1018,2,2555,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is dominated by a regularly spaced series of water-ice hydronium cluster peaks at ~3.10 5s, ~3.63 5s (the highest peak), ~4.13 5s, ~4.55 5s, and ~4.95 5s, rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 5s. Consequently, it lacks both a dominant Na+ peak and the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster spacing of 1.49 5s.",
1509316990,19256,2,1.1245599889936776e-14,1018,2,2556,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a water-ice hydronium cluster progression with the highest peak at ~1.40 µs followed by a prominent second peak at ~2.21 µs (a separation of ~0.81 µs), and lacks a distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at the required ~1.49 µs distance (~2.89 µs).",
1509317162,19428,2,1.701929917797499e-14,1018,2,2562,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum lacks a dominant Na+ peak in the 1.4-2.0 5s range, instead reaching its maximum amplitude at ~3.24 5s (and an initial spike at ~0.12 5s). It is dominated by a regularly spaced series of water-ice cluster peaks at ~2.68 5s, ~3.24 5s, ~3.72 5s, and ~4.18 5s rather than the sodium hydroxide pattern.",
1509317857,20123,3-Car,1.1271699854953701e-13,1018,3-Car,34595,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum lacks a sharp dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 µs, instead showing very broad, saturated features peaking around 2.45 µs, 3.90 µs, and 5.60 µs on a heavily elevated baseline without any resolved Na(NaOH)+ cluster series.",
1509335704,25173,2,3.20091006380651e-14,1018,2,2591,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a water-ice hydronium cluster series (H3O+(H2O)n) starting with a main peak at ~1.73 µs, followed by closely spaced major peaks at ~2.53 µs (0.80 µs later), ~3.16 µs, and ~3.70 µs. Because the dominant second peak appears 0.80 µs after the first peak rather than showing an isolated Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~1.49 µs later, it does not follow the sodium hydroxide pattern.",
1509335942,25410,3-OH,7.832880259120087e-14,1018,3-OH,34596,3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at approximately 1.94 BCs, followed by a clear Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at approximately 3.40 BCs (a separation of 1.46 BCs, which matches the expected 1.49 BCs interval within tolerance).",
1509336498,25963,3-Car,1.9003799456383114e-13,1018,3-Car,34597,non-3-OH,3-OH,The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.08 s followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.57 s (a time distance of 1.49 s). This sodium hydroxide series is further confirmed by the second cluster peak Na(NaOH)2+ at ~4.58 s (~2.50 s after Na+).,
1509336608,26072,3-OH,1.6276399444816597e-13,1018,3-OH,34598,3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the spectrum has a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.96 µs and a small sharp feature near ~3.42 µs, it is dominated by a massive, continuous baseline overshoot starting around 2.8 µs that stays elevated near 0.8 amplitude rather than showing a clean, well-resolved sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1509336865,26328,3-KNa,1.9759399940365817e-14,1018,3-KNa,34360,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is located at approximately 0.65 BCs rather than representing a dominant Na+ peak in the expected 1.4–2.0 BCs range, and the next major peak at ~1.34 BCs is only ~0.69 BCs later. Furthermore, even if the peak at ~1.34 BCs is considered Na+, it is not the highest peak and lacks a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 BCs later (showing only a weak bump near 2.68 BCs).",
1509337729,27167,2,1.305510028153014e-14,1018,2,2661,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a regularly spaced water-ice hydronium cluster series with major peaks at ~1.33 Δs, ~1.98 Δs, ~2.53 Δs, and ~3.03 Δs. The time distances from the highest peak (~1.33 Δs) to the following peaks are ~0.65 Δs and ~1.20 Δs, lacking the required ~1.49 Δs spacing for a Na(NaOH)+ cluster.",
1509337797,27201,3-Car,1.2027800088375284e-14,1018,3-Car,34599,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is a broad feature centered around 2.35 s rather than a sharp Na+ peak in the expected 1.42.0 s range, and the subsequent peaks at ~3.88 s, ~4.48 s, and ~5.50 s do not follow the characteristic sodium hydroxide cluster progression.",
1509337964,27362,1,3.626670158304347e-14,1018,1,2672,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is dominated by a regularly spaced water-ice hydronium cluster series with major peaks at ~1.71 9cs, ~2.53 9cs (also reaching amplitude 1.0), ~3.18 9cs, ~3.70 9cs, and ~4.17 9cs, accompanied by a smaller Na+ series starting at ~1.93 9cs. Because the highest peaks belong to the water-ice cluster progression rather than a dominant Na+ peak followed 1.49 9cs later by an isolated Na(NaOH)+ peak, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1509338233,27628,3-Car,7.530650094397101e-14,1018,3-Car,34600,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the broad peak with a maximum at ~2.52 µs is followed by peaks at ~3.95 µs (1.43 µs later) and ~4.55 µs, the spectrum is dominated by extremely broad features, including a massive peak at ~5.58 µs (amplitude ~0.98) and a shoulder at ~2.33 µs, which is characteristic of a mineral or other complex grain rather than a clean sodium hydroxide series.",
1509338535,27929,1,3.306580134481915e-14,1018,1,2694,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a typical water-ice hydronium cluster series (H3O+(H2O)n) with major peaks at ~1.62 bc	ext{s}, ~2.46 bc	ext{s} (the highest peak), ~3.07 bc	ext{s}, and ~3.58 bc	ext{s}. It is classified as 'non-3-OH' because the highest peak is at 2.46 bc	ext{s} rather than Na+, and the peak spacing (~0.84 bc	ext{s}, ~0.61 bc	ext{s}, ~0.51 bc	ext{s}) does not match the 1.49 bc	ext{s} separation required for a Na(NaOH)+ cluster.",
1509338790,28182,1,1.3682700026435794e-14,1018,1,2703,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a classic water-ice hydronium cluster series starting with a main peak at ~1.58 µs, followed by a smaller Na+ peak at ~1.79 µs and a major cluster peak at ~2.42 µs (only ~0.84 µs after the main peak). Further regularly spaced water-ice clusters appear at ~3.03 µs, ~3.57 µs, and ~4.06 µs, completely lacking the isolated Na(NaOH)+ peak expected 1.49 µs after Na+.",
1509338862,28253,1,3.5511598815620576e-14,1018,1,2705,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This spectrum is dominated by a water-ice hydronium cluster series (H3O+(H2O)n) with major peaks at ~1.71 µs, ~2.53 µs, ~3.15 µs, and ~3.68 µs (alongside a smaller Na+ peak at ~1.92 µs). Because the highest peak is H3O+ rather than Na+, and the spectrum is governed by ~0.6–0.8 µs water-cluster spacings rather than an isolated Na(NaOH)+ peak 1.49 µs after Na+, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1509338934,28325,3-Car,2.76895002694795e-14,1018,3-Car,34601,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although a dominant peak at ~1.98 5s is followed by a strong peak at ~3.45 5s (~1.47 5s later), the spectrum is dominated by broad, intense peaks including a massive peak at ~5.08 5s (~3.10 5s after the first peak, corresponding to m/z ~128 such as K(KCl)+ or Na(Na2CO3)+) that do not belong to the sodium hydroxide series.",
1509339387,28775,2,2.7678099206009457e-14,1018,2,2729,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is a water-ice spectrum dominated by a regularly spaced hydronium cluster series starting with the highest peak at ~2.30 µs, followed by major peaks at ~2.98 µs, ~3.55 µs, ~4.05 µs, and ~4.50 µs. It lacks a dominant Na+ peak (only a small feature is visible at ~1.48 µs) and does not show the required 1.49 µs spacing for a Na(NaOH)+ cluster.",
1509339510,28898,1,1.3325300403572472e-14,1018,1,2736,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This is a water-ice spectrum dominated by a regularly spaced series of hydronium cluster peaks starting at ~1.39 us, followed by major peaks at ~2.21 us (0.82 us later), ~2.84 us, and ~3.39 us. The ~0.82 us spacing to the second major peak is inconsistent with the required ~1.49 us interval between Na+ and Na(NaOH)+.",
1509339828,29214,2,2.589579958345127e-14,1018,2,2746,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a typical water-ice hydronium cluster series with peaks at ~1.74 5s, ~2.57 5s (the highest peak), ~3.21 5s, and ~3.80 5s, violating Rule 1 because the highest peak is not Na+ in the 1.4–2.0 5s range. Furthermore, the peak spacings (~0.83 5s and ~0.64 5s) do not match the required 1.49 5s separation for a sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1509339954,29340,2,1.9041900353603328e-14,1018,2,2752,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is a classic water-ice pattern dominated by a regularly spaced hydronium cluster series (H3O+(H2O)n) with major peaks at ~2.50 µs, ~3.15 µs (the highest peak), ~3.68 µs, ~4.18 µs, and ~4.65 µs. Because the highest peak is not Na+ (between 1.4 and 2.0 µs) and there is no Na(NaOH)+ cluster progression, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1509340179,29564,2,1.3543399529029193e-13,1018,2,2758,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dense, regularly spaced water-ice cluster series with major peaks at ~1.88 s, ~2.70 s, ~3.33 s, ~3.86 s, and ~4.33 s. The prominent peak at ~2.70 s (only ~0.82 s after the first major peak) and the subsequent ~0.5–0.6 s intervals indicate hydronium water clusters rather than a clean sodium hydroxide pattern.",
1509340695,30077,2,3.1801299739181096e-14,1018,2,2779,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a typical water-ice hydronium cluster series with major peaks at ~1.55 5s, ~2.41 5s (the highest peak), ~3.10 5s, and ~3.67 5s. Because the highest peak is at ~2.41 5s rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 5s, and the peak spacings do not match the 1.49 5s Na(NaOH)+ interval, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1509340896,30277,1,1.1221100308970392e-14,1018,1,2789,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a water-ice hydronium cluster series (H3O+(H2O)n) with major peaks at ~1.46 BCs, ~2.28 BCs, ~2.90 BCs, and ~3.43 BCs, alongside a smaller Na+ peak at ~1.65 BCs. Because the highest peak is H3O+ rather than Na+ and the subsequent peaks follow water-ice spacing (~0.82 BCs and ~0.62 BCs) rather than the 1.49 BCs interval from Na+ (~3.14 BCs), it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1509341170,30550,1,3.696510057684538e-14,1018,1,2799,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This is a water-ice spectrum dominated by a regularly spaced hydronium cluster series starting at ~1.73 µs, with subsequent major peaks at ~2.55 µs (~0.82 µs later), ~3.18 µs, ~3.71 µs, and ~4.18 µs, rather than an isolated Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 µs after a sodium peak.",
1509341724,31101,2,4.5366100741468796e-13,1018,2,2825,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the spectrum begins with a prominent peak at ~1.96 µs, it is immediately followed by a dense, saturated series of broad water-ice or salt cluster features at ~2.45 µs, ~2.72 µs, ~3.08 µs, and ~3.63 µs on a heavily elevated baseline. This chaotic, closely spaced progression completely lacks the isolated Na(NaOH)+ peak expected at ~3.45 µs (1.49 µs after the 1.96 µs peak), ruling out the 3-OH classification.",
