1509345901,35188,3-K,4.5980800682807535e-14,1018,3-K,34605,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak at ~2.48 5s is not followed by a major Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 5s later (~3.97 5s); instead, the next dominant salt cluster peak appears ~2.08 5s later at ~4.56 5s (followed by another at ~6.00 5s), which is characteristic of sodium chloride (NaCl) clusters rather than sodium hydroxide.",
1509346739,36016,2,2.6376700845189005e-14,1018,2,3056,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is dominated by a regularly spaced water-ice cluster series with major peaks at ~2.40 9cs, ~3.12 9cs (the highest peak), ~3.67 9cs, ~4.13 9cs, and ~4.57 9cs. Because the highest peak is at 3.12 9cs rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 9cs followed by a Na(NaOH)+ peak 1.49 9cs later, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1509346970,36244,3-Cl,2.279390055610203e-14,1018,3-Cl,34606,non-3-OH,3-OH,"Although shifted to later flight times, the spectrum exhibits a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.40 s followed ~1.49 s later by a Na(NaOH)+ peak at ~3.89 s, and a hydrated cluster peak at ~4.39 s (~0.50 s after the m/z 63 peak), matching the 3-OH series.",
1509347289,36560,1,1.4741600477753865e-14,1018,1,3080,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a classic water-ice hydronium cluster series starting with a main peak at ~1.58 µs, followed by major peaks at ~2.41 µs (+0.83 µs), ~3.02 µs (+1.44 µs), and ~3.57 µs (+1.99 µs). Because the second dominant peak appears only ~0.83 µs after the first peak rather than showing an isolated Na(NaOH)+ cluster ~1.49 µs after a Na+ peak, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1509347292,36563,1,1.4021700399618857e-14,1018,1,3081,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a water-ice hydronium cluster series starting with the highest peak at ~1.63 µs, followed by regularly spaced peaks at ~2.45 µs (only 0.82 µs later), ~3.08 µs, ~3.62 µs, and ~4.10 µs. Because it lacks a Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 µs after a dominant Na+ peak, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1509347614,36881,1,2.76895002694795e-14,1018,1,3093,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the highest peak is Na+ at ~1.83 us (preceded by H3O+ at ~1.62 us), the spectrum is dominated by a regularly spaced water-ice cluster series with peaks at ~2.44 us, ~3.08 us, and ~3.60 us. It lacks the diagnostic Na(NaOH)+ peak expected ~1.49 us after Na+ (at ~3.32 us), where there is instead a trough.",
1509348262,37521,1,1.3206099998004216e-14,1018,1,3137,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~1.54 µs (H3O+) rather than Na+ (which is the second peak at ~1.74 µs), and the spectrum is dominated by a regularly spaced hydronium-water cluster series at ~1.54, ~2.37, ~2.99, and ~3.53 µs. Furthermore, there is no Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak about 1.49 µs after the Na+ peak (around 3.23 µs).",
1509348306,37564,1,3.725570064038938e-14,1018,1,3140,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This spectrum is a classic water-ice profile dominated by a regularly spaced hydronium cluster series starting at ~1.70 us, followed by major peaks at ~2.52 us, ~3.16 us, ~3.70 us, and ~4.16 us. The second major peak appears ~0.82 us after the base peak rather than at the ~1.49 us interval required for a Na(NaOH)+ cluster.",
1509348357,37615,3-Cl,2.294129953551733e-14,1018,3-Cl,34607,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is a broad feature centered at approximately 2.40 bc	ext{s} (outside the typical 1.42.0 bc	ext{s} range for Na+), and it is followed by a regularly spaced series of broad water-ice cluster peaks at ~3.28 bc	ext{s} (~0.88 bc	ext{s} later), ~3.92 bc	ext{s} (~1.52 bc	ext{s} later), and ~4.50 bc	ext{s} rather than a clean sodium hydroxide cluster pattern.",
1509348405,37662,2,2.1252600441762533e-14,1018,2,3145,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum represents a water-ice grain dominated by a regularly spaced hydronium cluster series with major peaks at ~1.70 5s, ~2.64 5s, ~3.28 5s (the highest peak), ~3.81 5s, and ~4.33 5s. Because the highest peak is at ~3.28 5s rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 5s, it violates Rule 1 and is classified as non-3-OH.",
1509348670,37922,1,2.2354800370311297e-14,1018,1,3161,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a typical water-ice hydronium cluster series starting with a main peak at ~1.65 5s, followed by major peaks at ~2.48 5s, ~3.10 5s, and ~3.63 5s. Because the next major peak appears ~0.83 5s after the initial peak rather than at the ~1.49 5s interval required for Na(NaOH)+, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1509349103,38344,2,2.9594599340598826e-14,1018,2,3174,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a classic water-ice hydronium cluster series (H3O+(H2O)n) with major peaks at ~1.83 bc	ext{s}, ~2.68 bc	ext{s}, ~3.32 bc	ext{s}, ~3.92 bc	ext{s}, and ~4.42 bc	ext{s}. It is classified as non-3-OH because the highest peak is at ~2.68 bc	ext{s} rather than an initial Na+ peak, and the regular ~0.6–0.85 bc	ext{s} spacing is characteristic of water clusters rather than sodium hydroxide.",
1509351193,40390,1,3.192269988931337e-14,1018,1,3270,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This spectrum shows a classic water-ice hydronium cluster series starting with a main peak at ~1.68 µs, followed by a nearly equally high peak at ~2.50 µs (a distance of ~0.82 µs) and further regularly spaced clusters at ~3.13 µs, ~3.67 µs, and ~4.13 µs. It lacks the isolated Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak expected ~1.49 µs after a Na+ peak.",
1509351209,40406,2,2.78406007828743e-14,1018,2,3271,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a typical water-ice hydronium cluster series with major peaks at ~1.98 µs, ~2.60 µs (the highest peak), ~3.25 µs, ~3.90 µs, and ~4.40 µs. Because the highest peak is not Na+ in the 1.4-2.0 µs range and the peaks are spaced by ~0.5-0.65 µs rather than the required 1.49 µs for Na(NaOH)+, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1509351293,40488,3-Car,4.256080012618284e-14,1018,3-Car,34608,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is a broad feature at ~2.40 µs rather than a sharp Na+ peak in the typical 1.4–2.0 µs range, and although a prominent peak follows ~1.43 µs later at ~3.83 µs, the spectrum is dominated by another massive broad peak at ~5.48 µs (~3.08 µs after the first peak) which does not match the sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1509351739,40914,5,2.079950049541958e-14,1018,5,3295,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.75 s followed closely by a strong K+ peak at ~2.43 s (a time distance of ~0.68 s). It is classified as 'non-3-OH' because it completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak expected ~1.49 s after the Na+ peak (around 3.24 s).,
1509357202,43675,1,1.608959920320046e-14,1018,1,3325,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a water-ice hydronium cluster series starting with the highest peak at ~1.61 s (preceded by a smaller peak at ~1.38 s) and followed by regularly spaced peaks at ~2.20 s, ~2.83 s, and ~3.38 s. It lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 s after the main peak (which would appear around 3.10 s), ruling out the '3-OH' pattern.",
1509380601,55202,5,1.964599916938741e-14,1018,5,34513,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant peak at ~2.03 s (preceded by a small peak at ~1.31 s), but completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 s later (around 3.52 s). Because there are no subsequent hydroxide cluster peaks after the main peak, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1511732906,27370,3-Car,1.2706499636922896e-14,1018,3-Car,34609,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the highest peak at ~2.00 Δs is followed by a prominent peak ~1.50 Δs later at ~3.50 Δs, the subsequent major peaks at ~4.10 Δs (0.60 Δs after the 3.50 Δs peak) and ~5.13 Δs indicate that this spectrum is dominated by sodium chloride clusters (Na(NaCl)+ at m/z 81 is ~1.99 Δs after Na+, or the peak at 5.13 Δs is a higher mass salt cluster) rather than the sodium hydroxide series.",
1511733380,27819,3-OH,1.0786099932050958e-13,1018,3-OH,34610,3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.96 BCs followed by a distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.45 BCs, which is 1.49 BCs later and matches the required sodium hydroxide pattern.",
1511733538,27969,3-K,9.350620321438297e-14,1018,3-K,34611,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is a broad double-peaked feature around 2.66-2.72 s (well outside the typical 1.4-2.0 s range for Na+), and the next major peaks at ~4.33 s and ~4.81 s follow ~1.64 s and ~2.12 s later, which correspond to other salt clusters (likely Na(NaCl)+ at m/z 81 rather than Na(NaOH)+ at 1.49 s).",
1511735196,29525,3-Cl,4.602869734665616e-13,1018,3-Cl,34612,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The highest peak is a double-peaked Na+ feature at approximately 2.02-2.12 s, followed about 1.49 s later by the characteristic Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.56 s. A secondary hydrated cluster peak Na(NaOH)(H2O)+ is also clearly visible at ~4.08 s (~0.52 s after the m/z 63 peak), confirming the 3-OH signature despite the elevated baseline.",
1511735241,29568,3-Cl,1.4720199343308538e-13,1018,3-Cl,34613,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.98 s followed by a clear Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.47 s, which matches the required 1.49 s spacing. This hydroxide pattern is further supported by the hydrated cluster peak Na(NaOH)(H2O)+ at ~3.98 s (~0.51 s after the m/z 63 peak).",
1511735287,29611,3-KNa,2.2765699441156147e-14,1018,3-KNa,34362,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a prominent peak at ~1.13 s and its highest peak at ~1.84 s, followed only by an elevated, noisy baseline starting near 2.6 s. It completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak about 1.49 s after the main peak (expected around 3.33 s).",
1511737455,31620,3-KNa,1.9343999736439257e-14,1018,3-KNa,34614,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although there is a dominant peak at ~1.45 s (consistent with Na+) and a small peak ~1.47 s later at ~2.92 s, the spectrum is dominated after Na+ by a much stronger peak at ~2.13 s (only ~0.68 s after the main peak, likely K+). Because the second-largest peak is K+ rather than a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster, the spectrum does not show a sodium hydroxide series.",
1511737622,31776,3-KNa,8.639870232012709e-14,1018,3-KNa,34615,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the highest peak is Na+ at ~1.98 µs, the next dominant peak appears at ~2.65 µs (only ~0.67 µs later, corresponding to K+) rather than a dominant Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.47 µs, indicating a spectrum dominated by other salts alongside a smaller peak at ~3.48 µs.",
1511737930,32063,3-KNa,3.89463987318997e-14,1018,3-KNa,34616,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.50 BCs, followed by a prominent K+ peak at ~2.19 BCs and a distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~2.99 BCs (a diagnostic time distance of 1.49 BCs after Na+). This clear 1.49 BCs spacing satisfies the required rules for the 3-OH class.",
1511739515,33530,5-Na,3.4689699029977206e-14,1018,5-Na,34839,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum features a single dominant Na+ peak at ~1.41 cs followed by a flat, elevated baseline near 0.62 amplitude, completely lacking the diagnostic Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak expected ~1.49 cs later (around 2.90 cs).",
1511740094,34063,3-KNa,2.281850008695619e-14,1018,3-KNa,34617,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~2.46 s rather than the initial peak at ~1.77 s (a spacing of ~0.69 s), and the spectrum is dominated by a water-ice or potassium cluster series (~3.26 s, ~3.74 s, ~4.14 s, ~4.52 s) rather than a clean sodium hydroxide pattern.",
1511752503,44407,4,2.0685500025114517e-14,1018,4,3331,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~1.94 s, followed by a prominent peak at ~2.63 s (only ~0.69 s later, consistent with a K+ or water-ice cluster peak), and there is no Na(NaOH)+ peak at the expected ~3.43 s position (1.49 s after the main peak).",
1514090930,32369,3-Car,3.735530155059112e-14,1018,3-Car,34618,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although a dominant peak at ~1.90 µs is followed ~1.49 µs later by a major peak at ~3.39 µs, the third major peak at ~5.01 µs (a 1.62 µs interval) and the broad, sawtooth-tailed peak shapes indicate a sodium chloride cluster series (Na(NaCl)n+ at m/z 81 and 139) rather than a sodium hydroxide series.",
1514101242,34326,4,4.1069299111691493e-13,1018,4,3365,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because its highest peak is a broad, multi-peaked feature around 2.2-2.35 s rather than a dominant, narrow Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 s. Instead of a sodium hydroxide cluster series, it displays a complex mineral-like profile with prominent peaks at ~0.37 s, ~1.45 s, ~1.67 s, ~2.97 s, and ~4.80 s.",
1514107726,34932,4,1.324930037238008e-14,1018,4,3370,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~1.81 5s (likely Na+ or H3O+), followed by a prominent second peak at ~2.49 5s (a distance of ~0.68 5s, consistent with K+ or a water cluster), and completely lacks the characteristic Na(NaOH)+ peak expected ~1.49 5s later at ~3.30 5s.",
1514128504,40684,3-Cl,2.943190125209022e-14,1018,3-Cl,34619,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although there is a strong Na+ peak at ~1.90 µs and a peak at ~3.37 µs (~1.47 µs later), the highest peak in the spectrum is at ~3.88 µs (reaching 1.00 amplitude, ~1.98 µs after Na+, corresponding to Na(NaCl)+ at m/z 81) along with a strong Na(NaCl)2+ peak at ~5.22 µs, indicating a sodium chloride-dominated spectrum rather than a 3-OH spectrum.",
1514128709,40886,2,4.3199699460011454e-13,1018,2,3403,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because it displays a dense, overlapping water-ice or complex cluster series with peaks at ~1.9 bc	ext{s}, ~2.0 bc	ext{s}, ~2.4 bc	ext{s}, ~2.75 bc	ext{s}, ~2.95 bc	ext{s}, ~3.4 bc	ext{s}, and ~4.05 bc	ext{s} on an elevated baseline, rather than an isolated Na+ peak followed by a clean Na(NaOH)+ cluster 1.49 bc	ext{s} later.",
1514129064,41235,1,1.0621699984944728e-14,1018,1,3417,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a water-ice pattern dominated by a regularly spaced series of hydronium cluster peaks at approximately 1.50 µs, 1.71 µs, 2.31 µs, 2.98 µs, 3.50 µs, 3.98 µs, and 4.39 µs. Because the highest peak at 1.50 µs is part of a water-ice cluster progression (H3O+) rather than an isolated Na+ peak with a Na(NaOH)+ cluster 1.49 µs later, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1514129425,41590,3-Car,2.7828999819628705e-14,1018,3-Car,34620,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.93 bcs followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.42 bcs (a distance of 1.49 bcs), satisfying the core rules for a 3-OH classification. This hydroxide series is further supported by secondary peaks at ~4.00 bcs (m/z 81) and ~4.45 bcs (m/z 103).",
1514129692,41848,3-OH,2.495569939933717e-13,1018,3-OH,34621,3-OH,3-OH,"The highest peak is a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.09 bcS (with a shoulder at ~1.98 bcS), followed by a distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.51 bcS (~1.42-1.53 bcS later) and a faint secondary cluster peak near ~4.55 bcS (~2.46-2.57 bcS after Na+), which matches the sodium hydroxide cluster pattern despite the elevated baseline.",
1514131632,43670,3-OH,6.235670074912492e-13,1018,3-OH,34622,3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although there is a sharp feature near 2.07 µs, the spectrum suffers from a severe baseline jump that remains saturated near 0.9 amplitude across the entire recording, lacking a well-resolved Na+ and Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak series.",
1514132933,44932,3-Car,2.5809500478653213e-14,1018,3-Car,34623,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although a dominant peak at ~2.03 s is followed by a peak at ~3.53 s (~1.50 s later), the subsequent prominent peaks at ~4.15 s and ~5.17 s (distances of ~2.12 s and ~3.14 s after the main peak) do not match the sodium hydroxide series, indicating a chloride/target-rich salt spectrum instead.",
1514133940,45927,1,1.9041900353603328e-14,1018,1,3480,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a classic water-ice hydronium cluster series (H3O+(H2O)n) with regularly spaced peaks at ~1.48 µs, ~2.30 µs, ~2.93 µs, ~3.46 µs (highest peak), ~3.92 µs, and ~4.35 µs. Because the highest peak is at ~3.46 µs rather than Na+ and the peaks follow water-cluster spacings (~0.5-0.8 µs) instead of the 1.49 µs Na(NaOH)+ interval, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1514134239,46218,3-K,2.412870081416451e-14,1018,3-K,34624,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.01 bc	ext{s}, but lacks a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at the required 1.49 bc	ext{s} interval (~3.50 bc	ext{s}). Instead, the main secondary peak appears much later at ~4.10 bc	ext{s} (about 2.09 bc	ext{s} after Na+, consistent with Na(NaCl)+ or hydrated clusters without the primary m/z 63 hydroxide peak).",
1514136002,47916,2,2.0306999964502144e-14,1018,2,3511,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This spectrum is classified as non-3-OH because it shows a regularly spaced water-ice hydronium cluster series with major peaks at ~1.56 5s, ~2.43 5s (the highest peak), ~3.07 5s, and ~3.63 5s, rather than a dominant Na+ peak followed 1.49 5s later by an isolated Na(NaOH)+ cluster.",
1514136654,48565,1,5.138340043709354e-14,1018,1,3523,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a classic water-ice hydronium cluster series starting with a main peak at ~1.76 s (H3O+) followed by a smaller Na+ peak at ~1.98 s, and then a dense, regularly spaced series of water cluster peaks at ~2.58 s, ~3.23 s, ~3.77 s, ~4.25 s, and ~4.66 s. Because the highest peak is H3O+ rather than Na+ and the spectrum is dominated by water-ice clusters instead of an isolated Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 s after Na+, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1514136702,48613,2,4.568719873449846e-14,1018,2,3525,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is not Na+ (which is only a minor peak near 1.68 µs), but rather a water-ice cluster peak at 3.20 µs. The spectrum is dominated by a regularly spaced H3O+(H2O)n hydronium cluster series with major peaks at 1.68, 2.55, 3.20, 3.75, 4.25, and 4.72 µs.",
1514137459,49368,2,1.7803599171089743e-14,1018,2,3535,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This spectrum is a water-ice spectrum dominated by a regularly spaced hydronium cluster series with major peaks at ~1.63 5s, ~1.85 5s, ~2.43 5s, ~3.05 5s, ~3.60 5s, and ~4.06 5s. It lacks an isolated Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 5s after a dominant Na+ peak.",
1514138247,50129,2,3.5041299018250677e-14,1018,2,3538,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because the highest peak is at ~3.10 Ss rather than being a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 Ss. Instead of the sodium hydroxide cluster pattern, it shows a classic water-ice hydronium cluster series with regularly spaced peaks at ~1.65 Ss, ~2.50 Ss, ~3.10 Ss, ~3.63 Ss, ~4.14 Ss, and ~4.55 Ss.",
1514138881,50728,2,1.2652399642581764e-14,1018,2,3540,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is dominated by a regularly spaced series of water-ice cluster peaks at ~2.75 µs, ~3.28 µs (highest peak), ~3.78 µs, ~4.18 µs, and ~4.58 µs. It lacks a dominant Na+ peak in the 1.4-2.0 µs range and does not follow the 1.49 µs spacing of the sodium hydroxide series.",
1514139281,51112,1,1.898740055971109e-14,1018,1,3543,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is a water-ice profile dominated by a regularly spaced H3O+(H2O)n cluster series with major peaks at approximately 1.63 µs, 2.44 µs (0.81 µs after the main peak), 3.06 µs, 3.63 µs, and 4.13 µs. Because the main peak is H3O+ (with a small Na+ peak at ~1.86 µs) and no isolated Na(NaOH)+ peak follows ~1.49 µs after the highest peak, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1514139426,51256,2,3.4795398577399175e-14,1018,2,3547,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is a water-ice spectrum dominated by a regularly spaced hydronium cluster series with major peaks at ~1.67 µs, ~2.50 µs (the highest peak), ~3.16 µs, ~3.80 µs, and ~4.30 µs. Because the highest peak is at ~2.50 µs rather than Na+ and the spectrum shows water-ice cluster spacings (~0.64-0.83 µs) instead of an isolated Na(NaOH)+ peak 1.49 µs after Na+, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1514139581,51411,2,6.560890204601946e-14,1018,2,3552,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~3.20 µs rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 µs, and the spectrum is dominated by a regularly spaced series of water-ice cluster peaks at ~2.55, 3.20, 3.74, 4.22, 4.66, and 5.08 µs rather than a sodium hydroxide series.",
1514139637,51467,3-Car,2.005079994182521e-13,1018,3-Car,34625,non-3-OH,3-OH,"Despite an elevated baseline shift, the spectrum clearly exhibits the sodium hydroxide cluster series: a strong Na+ peak at ~2.11 bc	ext{s} (reaching ~0.98 amplitude), followed ~1.46 bc	ext{s} later by the Na(NaOH)+ peak at ~3.57 bc	ext{s} (reaching 1.0 due to the rising baseline), and the second cluster Na(NaOH)2+ at ~4.59 bc	ext{s} (~2.48 bc	ext{s} after Na+).",
1514140056,51885,2,4.6678599977282784e-14,1018,2,3561,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because the highest peak is at ~3.12 µs rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 µs. Instead of a sodium hydroxide progression, it displays a classic water-ice hydronium cluster series with regularly spaced peaks at ~2.46, 3.12, 3.68, 4.14, 4.58, and 4.98 µs.",
1514140459,52287,4,1.6354599965962002e-12,1018,4,3571,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~0.42 s rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 s. Additionally, the spectrum shows a complex, saturated mineral/organic profile between 1.4 and 4.0 s and a peak at ~5.0 s, lacking the clean Na(NaOH)+ cluster pattern.",
1514141143,52964,1,1.9559700064589354e-14,1018,1,3583,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a classic water-ice hydronium cluster series starting with the highest peak at ~1.36 s (with a smaller Na+ peak at ~1.60 s), followed by regularly spaced cluster peaks at ~2.18 s, ~2.82 s, and ~3.36 s. It is classified as 'non-3-OH' because the highest peak is not Na+ and the subsequent peak spacings (~0.82 s, ~0.64 s, ~0.54 s) reflect water-ice clusters rather than the required ~1.49 s spacing for Na(NaOH)+.",
1514141705,53523,1,1.4278300560660075e-14,1018,1,3589,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a water-ice hydronium cluster series starting with the highest peak at ~1.30 bc	ext{s}, followed by major peaks at ~2.12 bc	ext{s} (a distance of ~0.82 bc	ext{s}), ~2.74 bc	ext{s}, and ~3.28 bc	ext{s}. This regular water-ice spacing does not match the required ~1.49 bc	ext{s} interval from Na+ to a dominant Na(NaOH)+ cluster.",
1514142343,54158,3-Cl,3.9164299651646764e-14,1018,3-Cl,34626,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the spectrum displays broad, overlapping features with maxima around 2.08 s, 3.55 s, and 4.10 s, the peak at 1.9–2.08 s is extremely broad and complex rather than a clean, narrow Na+ peak, and the overall profile of broad, unresolved humps (also at ~1.58 s and ~5.40 s) does not match the well-resolved sodium hydroxide cluster pattern.",
1514144503,55946,2,3.702880084261069e-14,1018,2,3624,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because its highest peak is at ~3.58 Ts rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 Ts. Instead of a sodium hydroxide progression, it displays a regularly spaced water-ice cluster series with major peaks at ~2.40 Ts, ~3.02 Ts, ~3.58 Ts, ~4.07 Ts, and ~4.50 Ts.",
1514146363,57459,1,2.3108400501285764e-14,1018,1,3629,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a water-ice hydronium cluster progression with the highest peak (H3O+) at ~1.14 9cs and subsequent peaks at ~1.35 9cs (Na+), ~1.96 9cs, ~2.60 9cs, and ~3.14 9cs. It lacks both a dominant Na+ peak as the base peak and the diagnostic Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 9cs after Na+ (expected around 2.84 9cs).",
1514147095,58115,1,1.3178700176226434e-14,1018,1,3636,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~0.77 µs (not in the expected 1.4-2.0 µs range for Na+), and the spectrum shows a water-ice hydronium cluster series with peaks at ~0.77 µs, ~1.60 µs, ~2.22 µs, and ~2.78 µs rather than a Na(NaOH)+ cluster ~1.49 µs after Na+.",
1514147722,58690,4,7.436640279273599e-14,1018,4,3640,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is a broad feature at ~2.80 5s rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 5s. Additionally, the complex mineral/organic pattern with peaks at ~0.25, ~1.35, ~1.60, ~2.08, ~3.34, and ~4.43 5s does not match the sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1514149161,60053,3-Cl,1.3858399562464985e-13,1018,3-Cl,34627,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum lacks a dominant, well-resolved Na+ peak in the typical 1.4-2.0 5s range, instead showing a broad, elevated feature peaking around 2.6 5s followed by other broad peaks near 4.1 5s, 4.6 5s, and 5.9 5s. Because it does not exhibit a clean Na+ peak and the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak 1.49 5s later, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1514149309,60198,2,3.900779845618027e-14,1018,2,3648,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum lacks a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 5s, instead reaching its maximum amplitude at ~3.65 5s as part of a dense, regularly spaced series of peaks (~3.15, 3.65, 4.15, 4.55, 4.95 5s) spaced by ~0.4-0.5 5s.",
1514149669,60552,2,1.652469969941426e-14,1018,2,3652,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is dominated by a regularly spaced series of broad water-ice cluster peaks at approximately 2.15, 2.83, 3.36 (the highest peak), 3.88, and 4.35 µs. Because the highest peak is at 3.36 µs rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 µs, and it lacks the 1.49 µs spacing of the Na(NaOH)+ series, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1514151324,62187,2,1.921179991622949e-14,1018,2,3661,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a classic water-ice pattern dominated by a regularly spaced hydronium cluster series at ~2.18 µs, ~2.82 µs (the highest peak), ~3.38 µs, ~3.88 µs, and ~4.35 µs. Because the highest peak is not Na+ in the 1.4-2.0 µs range and the peak spacing is ~0.5-0.65 µs rather than the diagnostic 1.49 µs sodium hydroxide interval, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1514157783,238,3-K,1.9035999922092754e-14,1018,3-K,34363,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The dominant peak is at ~1.30 bc, and there is no corresponding Na(NaOH)+ peak at ~2.79 bc (1.49 bc later). Instead, the next prominent peak appears at ~3.38 bc (a separation of ~2.08 bc), which does not match the sodium hydroxide cluster pattern.",
1514157932,386,2,1.001829980193554e-13,1018,2,3691,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because the highest peak is located at approximately 3.55 s rather than being a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 s. Furthermore, the profile is dominated by a regularly spaced series of water-ice cluster peaks at ~2.90 s, ~3.55 s, ~4.12 s, ~4.60 s, and ~5.05 s, completely lacking the diagnostic Na(NaOH)+ pattern.",
1514157970,424,1,4.1559600406264677e-14,1018,1,3692,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a water-ice hydronium cluster series with major peaks at ~1.46 BCs, ~1.65 BCs, ~2.28 BCs, and ~2.92 BCs rather than a sodium hydroxide pattern. Although the highest peak is at ~1.65 BCs, the next dominant peak appears at ~2.28 BCs (0.63 BCs later) instead of the ~1.49 BCs separation required for an isolated Na(NaOH)+ cluster.",
1514158122,576,2,1.7738799795372073e-13,1018,2,3694,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because it is dominated by a regularly spaced water-ice cluster series with highest peaks at ~2.92 s, ~3.59 s, and ~4.14 s, rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 s. Furthermore, it lacks the isolated Na(NaOH)+ peak separated by 1.49 s from a main Na+ peak.",
1514159817,2266,2,2.0443499323952175e-13,1018,2,3714,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as non-3-OH because the highest peaks occur at approximately 3.57 µs and 4.10 µs rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 µs. Furthermore, it exhibits a regularly spaced series of water-ice cluster peaks (around 2.10, 2.91, 3.57, 4.10, 4.60, and 5.01 µs) on an elevated baseline rather than the isolated Na(NaOH)+ pattern.",
1514160424,2871,2,2.7178200689330703e-14,1018,2,3722,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a classic water-ice hydronium cluster series with major peaks at ~2.03 bc	ext{s}, ~2.93 bc	ext{s}, ~3.58 bc	ext{s} (the highest peak), and ~4.13 bc	ext{s}. Because the highest peak is not Na+ (located between 1.4 and 2.0 bc	ext{s}) and it lacks the diagnostic Na(NaOH)+ spacing of ~1.49 bc	ext{s}, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1514161994,4435,3-Cl,1.58671005886157e-14,1018,3-Cl,34628,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although a peak appears at ~3.83 Ss (~1.46 Ss after the broad main peak at ~2.37 Ss), the spectrum is dominated by a larger peak at ~4.30 Ss (~1.93 Ss after Na+, corresponding to Na(NaCl)+ at m/z 81) and another at ~5.62 Ss (~3.25 Ss after Na+, corresponding to Na(NaCl)2+ at m/z 139), indicating a sodium chloride/carbonate salt pattern rather than a 3-OH series.",
1514162372,4811,1,3.967470137687147e-14,1018,1,3745,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is located at approximately 0.77 µs rather than in the typical 1.4–2.0 µs range for Na+, and is followed by a water-ice cluster progression at ~1.61 µs (0.84 µs later) and ~2.26 µs. There is no Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 µs after the main peak or after the 1.61 µs peak.",
1514164142,6105,3-Car,1.1955500066503089e-13,1018,3-Car,34629,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.03 µs, followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.50 µs (a separation of ~1.47 µs, matching the expected 1.49 µs rule). This sodium hydroxide series is further confirmed by the second hydroxide cluster peak Na(NaOH)2+ at ~4.52 µs (~2.49 µs after Na+).",
1514168555,8847,3-Car,6.96832999289021e-14,1018,3-Car,34630,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum lacks a sharp, dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 5s, showing instead a steep baseline rise at ~2.2 5s into a broad, saturated plateau peaking around 2.5–2.7 5s. There are no well-resolved sodium hydroxide cluster peaks following at the required ~1.49 5s interval.",
1514168606,8898,1,3.33135991394725e-14,1018,1,3788,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is a water-ice grain dominated by a regularly spaced hydronium cluster series (H3O+(H2O)n) at ~1.70 s, ~2.52 s, ~3.15 s, ~3.68 s, and ~4.16 s, along with a smaller Na+ peak at ~1.91 s. Because the highest peak is H3O+ (~1.70 s) rather than Na+ and there is no Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 s after Na+ (around 3.40 s), it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1514168797,9088,3-OH,1.951219947334687e-13,1018,3-OH,34631,3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.96 s followed by a clear Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.42 s, which is 1.46 s later and well within the expected 1.49 s (0.1 s) interval for the '3-OH' class, despite the elevated baseline shift.",
1514169120,9409,3-Car,1.1762400102045042e-14,1018,3-Car,34632,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Instead of narrow salt-cluster peaks, the spectrum displays extremely broad, noisy humps centered around ~2.1 µs, ~3.4 µs, and ~5.3 µs. This broad profile lacks a sharp dominant Na+ peak and the well-resolved Na(NaOH)+ cluster series required for a '3-OH' classification.",
1514171216,11490,1,1.9041900353603328e-14,1018,1,3823,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a typical water-ice hydronium cluster series starting with the highest peak at ~1.61 cs (H3O+) and a smaller Na+ peak at ~1.82 cs, followed by regularly spaced cluster peaks at ~2.42 cs, ~3.05 cs, ~3.58 cs, and ~4.06 cs. It lacks both a dominant Na+ peak and the required Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 cs after Na+ (which would be near 3.31 cs).",
1514171355,11627,3-Cl,2.5841299789559034e-14,1018,3-Cl,34633,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although a peak appears at ~3.83 s (about 1.44 s after the broad main peak at ~2.39 s), the spectrum is dominated by an extremely broad, taller peak at ~4.40 s (~2.01 s after the main peak) and another at ~5.72 s, which represents a chloride salt (NaCl) series rather than the sodium hydroxide (NaOH) pattern.",
1514174876,14810,1,1.6171200663273044e-14,1018,1,3875,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a typical water-ice hydronium cluster series (H3O+(H2O)n) with major peaks at ~1.54 µs (H3O+, not Na+, with a small Na+ peak at ~1.75 µs), ~2.36 µs, ~2.98 µs, and ~3.51 µs. Because the highest peak is not Na+ and the subsequent peaks follow water-cluster spacings (~0.82 µs, ~0.62 µs, ~0.53 µs) rather than the sodium hydroxide series, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1514175830,15731,3-OH,1.318989947644844e-13,1018,3-OH,34634,3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.04 s followed by a distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.46 s (a distance of ~1.42 s, within the 1.49  0.1 s rule), and a small Na(NaOH)2+ peak at ~4.48 s (~2.44 s after Na+), superposed on an elevated baseline.",
1514176569,16315,2,9.604690225659476e-14,1018,2,3886,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at approximately 2.66 5s rather than being a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 5s. Instead of an isolated sodium hydroxide pattern, the spectrum shows a dense series of broad water-ice cluster peaks at ~1.79 5s, ~2.02 5s, ~2.66 5s, ~3.27 5s, and ~3.88 5s.",
1514176678,16423,2,8.327470250911809e-14,1018,2,3891,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as non-3-OH because the highest peak is at approximately 3.22 µs rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 µs. Instead of a sodium hydroxide progression, it displays a regularly spaced water-ice cluster series (H3O+(H2O)n) with major peaks at approximately 1.77 µs, 2.56 µs, 3.22 µs, 3.76 µs, and 4.25 µs.",
1514176889,16633,3-KNa,1.0415699878106588e-13,1018,3-KNa,34635,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.98 bc	ext{s} (with a split/spike at 2.04 bc	ext{s}), followed by a distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.48 bc	ext{s} later at ~3.46 bc	ext{s}. This sodium hydroxide signature is further supported by a secondary hydrated cluster peak at ~3.99 bc	ext{s} (~0.53 bc	ext{s} after the m/z 63 peak), despite the elevated baseline.",
1514176893,16637,1,4.092929947329023e-14,1018,1,3895,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This is a water-ice spectrum dominated by a regularly spaced H3O+(H2O)n cluster series with major peaks at approximately 1.72 5s, 2.54 5s, 3.18 5s, 3.72 5s, and 4.19 5s. Although a small Na+ peak appears at ~1.93 5s, it is not the highest peak and lacks a corresponding Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 5s later (around 3.42 5s).",
1514177597,17336,1,2.38050003971077e-14,1018,1,3918,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This spectrum is a classic water-ice pattern dominated by a regularly spaced hydronium cluster series starting at ~1.67 us, followed by major peaks at ~2.49 us (a distance of ~0.82 us), ~3.12 us, and ~3.67 us. It is classified as 'non-3-OH' because it lacks the isolated Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak expected ~1.49 us after a Na+ peak.",
1514178032,17766,3-Cl,5.876390005024948e-14,1018,3-Cl,34636,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum does not show a clean dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 5s, instead featuring a broad, heavily tailing doublet peaking at ~2.18 5s and another co-dominant peak reaching 1.0 amplitude at ~4.18 5s, which is inconsistent with the sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1514178834,18561,3-P,1.6026800180491026e-14,1018,3-P,34637,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although there is a dominant peak around 1.88-1.99 bc	ext{s} and a strong peak at ~3.42 bc	ext{s} (~1.43-1.54 bc	ext{s} later), the initial peak is a broad, split doublet (1.88 bc	ext{s} and 1.99 bc	ext{s}, characteristic of H3O+ and Na+) and the later peak at ~6.13 bc	ext{s} indicates a different salt or mineral composition (such as NaCl cluster at ~3.42 bc	ext{s} where 3.42 - 1.43 = 1.99 bc	ext{s} from an earlier offset, or another non-hydroxide species) rather than a clean 3-OH series.",
1514179092,18815,2,2.0145199730917628e-14,1018,2,3944,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This spectrum shows a regularly spaced water-ice hydronium cluster series starting at ~1.58 s, followed by major peaks at ~2.44 s (0.86 s later), ~3.10 s, and ~3.67 s, rather than an isolated Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 s after a dominant Na+ peak.",
1514179211,18932,3-Cl,3.4993001199598237e-14,1018,3-Cl,34638,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is a broad feature at ~4.42 BCs rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 BCs, violating Rule 1. Even if the large peak at ~2.40 BCs is considered as a shifted Na+ peak, the subsequent peak at ~3.86 BCs (~1.46 BCs later) is overshadowed by the much larger peak at ~4.42 BCs, which does not match the 3-OH dominance pattern.",
1514179689,19404,3-K,1.9041900353603328e-14,1018,3-K,34639,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~2.25 µs, and the next major peak appears at ~4.30 µs, giving a time distance of ~2.05 µs rather than the required ~1.49 µs for a Na(NaOH)+ cluster (expected around 3.74 µs). This ~2.0 µs spacing corresponds to a sodium chloride Na(NaCl)n+ progression (with peaks at ~2.25, ~4.30, and ~5.77 µs) rather than sodium hydroxide.",
1514180281,19991,3-Car,4.1184798491500016e-14,1018,3-Car,34640,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a broad, asymmetric peak complex reaching maximum amplitude at ~2.08 µs with major subsequent broad peaks at ~3.42 µs (1.34 µs later) and ~5.03 µs (1.61 µs after the second peak). This broad, sawtooth-like peak profile and spacing (especially the 5.03 µs peak which does not match m/z 81 or m/z 103) do not follow the narrow sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1514180669,20374,1,3.093069894720239e-14,1018,1,3981,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This is a classic water-ice spectrum dominated by a regularly spaced hydronium cluster series (H3O+(H2O)n) with major peaks at ~1.69 5s, ~2.53 5s, ~3.18 5s, ~3.70 5s, and ~4.18 5s. Even considering the minor Na+ peak at ~1.90 5s, it is not the highest peak and lacks a corresponding Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak 1.49 5s later (around 3.39 5s).",
1514180988,20690,3-Cl,6.023459996843533e-14,1018,3-Cl,34641,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.01 µs, followed ~1.47 µs later by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.48 µs. This sodium hydroxide pattern is further confirmed by a strong hydrated cluster peak Na(NaOH)(H2O)+ at ~3.98 µs (0.50 µs after the m/z 63 peak).",
1514181428,21125,5,3.157510128468273e-14,1018,5,4007,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.93 s followed closely by a strong K+ peak at ~2.57 s (a distance of ~0.64 s), but completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak expected ~1.49 s after Na+ (around 3.42 s).",
1514181548,21243,3-Car,5.770079916254597e-14,1018,3-Car,34642,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum lacks a sharp, dominant Na+ peak in the expected 1.4-2.0 µs range, instead showing broad, saw-tooth-shaped features peaking around 2.31 µs and 2.58 µs (highest peak), followed by other broad structures at ~3.76-4.0 µs and ~5.4-5.6 µs that do not match the characteristic sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1514181922,21612,1,1.7609499877160525e-14,1018,1,4021,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a typical water-ice hydronium cluster series starting with a main peak at ~1.62 µs, followed by regularly spaced peaks at ~2.45 µs, ~3.08 µs, ~3.60 µs, and ~4.08 µs. Because the second major peak is ~0.83 µs after the first rather than showing an isolated Na(NaOH)+ cluster ~1.49 µs later, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1514182779,22457,2,4.556809912585093e-14,1018,2,4036,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This spectrum is dominated by a regularly spaced water-ice hydronium cluster series (H3O+(H2O)n) with major peaks at ~1.70 9cs, ~2.53 9cs, ~3.21 9cs, ~3.78 9cs, and ~4.30 9cs. The highest peaks are at ~2.53 9cs and ~3.21 9cs rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 9cs, violating the rules for '3-OH'.",
1514183850,23511,3-KNa,2.1574600016661255e-13,1018,3-KNa,34643,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at approximately 2.78 us rather than the initial peak at 2.06 us, violating Rule 1. Furthermore, the spectrum displays a regularly spaced water-ice cluster series (with peaks at ~2.06, 2.78, 3.55, 3.98, 4.41, and 4.86 us) rather than the characteristic sodium hydroxide pattern.",
1514183929,23588,3-Cl,3.5209499432784647e-14,1018,3-Cl,34644,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum has a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.90 cs followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.48 cs later at ~3.38 cs. This sodium hydroxide pattern is further supported by optional cluster peaks at ~3.90 cs (m/z 81, ~0.52 cs after m/z 63) and ~4.41 cs (m/z 103, ~1.03 cs after m/z 63).",
1514184246,23900,3-KNa,6.805049823340251e-14,1018,3-KNa,34645,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the highest peak is at approximately 1.77 µs (Na+), the next major peak appears at approximately 2.43 µs (only 0.66 µs later, consistent with K+ or water-ice clusters) on a strongly rising baseline, with a smaller peak at 3.22 µs, so the spectrum is dominated by other species rather than a clean sodium hydroxide series.",
1514184828,24470,3-Car,1.7837600428845246e-13,1018,3-Car,34646,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum lacks a clean, narrow Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 s, instead showing a broad, saturated double-peaked feature starting around 2.43 s and 2.71 s, followed by broad humps at ~4.08 s and ~5.72 s that do not match the diagnostic 1.49 s Na(NaOH)+ spacing.",
1514186105,25710,1,1.0772299901867701e-14,1018,1,4102,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a classic water-ice pattern dominated by a regularly spaced hydronium cluster series starting with the highest peak at ~0.83 s, followed by peaks at ~1.46 s, ~2.00 s, ~2.50 s, ~2.92 s, and ~3.30 s. Because the highest peak is not Na+ (expected around 1.4-2.0 s) and the peak spacings (~0.5-0.6 s) do not match the required 1.49 s interval for Na(NaOH)+, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1514186160,25762,1,2.8897501389403904e-14,1018,1,4106,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a classic water-ice pattern dominated by a regularly spaced hydronium cluster series with major peaks at ~1.69 µs, ~2.51 µs (the highest peak), ~3.16 µs, ~3.70 µs, ~4.18 µs, and ~4.60 µs. Because the highest peak is not Na+ (which appears as a smaller peak at ~1.90 µs) and there is no isolated Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 µs after Na+, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1489003352,14561,4,2.7519400807077786e-14,1018,4,2,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because its highest peak is a broad feature at ~3.25 µs rather than a dominant Na+ peak in the expected 1.4–2.0 µs range (where only minor peaks at ~1.28 µs and ~1.52 µs appear). Furthermore, the complex pattern of mineral or organic peaks at ~0.16 µs, ~2.28 µs, ~3.25 µs, and ~4.52 µs does not match the required 1.49 µs sodium hydroxide cluster spacing.",
1489004979,15566,3-Car,1.1783400589906318e-13,1018,3-Car,34542,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the broad highest peak at ~2.25 µs is followed by a peak ~1.47 µs later at ~3.72 µs, the spectrum is dominated by a massive, broad peak at ~5.35 µs (~3.10 µs after the first peak) and lacks the sharp, narrow peak profile of a sodium hydroxide series, indicating a mineral or alternative salt composition.",
1489008582,18071,3-Car,1.4239400403150831e-13,1018,3-Car,34543,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.03 Δs, followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.51 Δs (a time distance of ~1.48 Δs). This sodium hydroxide series is further confirmed by the second cluster peak Na(NaOH)2+ at ~4.56 Δs (~2.53 Δs after Na+).",
1489009845,18970,3-Car,4.0472901180650667e-14,1018,3-Car,34544,non-3-OH,3-OH,The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.96 µs followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.48 µs later at ~3.44 µs. This sodium hydroxide series is further supported by the second hydroxide cluster Na(NaOH)2+ at ~4.48 µs (~2.52 µs after Na+).,
1489014539,22285,4,1.2011199936674995e-14,1018,4,10,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~1.82 s, followed by a prominent second peak at ~2.49 s (only ~0.67 s later, corresponding to K+ or a hydronium cluster). Crucially, there is no Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at the required ~1.49 s distance (~3.31 s), ruling out the '3-OH' label.",
1489027270,25095,4,1.4099099729240113e-14,1018,4,25,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~1.81 s, followed by major peaks at ~2.50 s (0.69 s later) and ~3.05 s (1.24 s later), consistent with a water-ice or potassium-rich spectrum. It completely lacks the diagnostic Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak expected ~1.49 s after the main peak (at ~3.30 s).",
1489029600,25226,4,2.571110066117068e-14,1018,4,28,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is a broad feature at ~3.20 s rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 s (such as the smaller peak at ~1.50 s), violating Rule 1. Furthermore, the spectrum displays a complex mineral/organic pattern (with peaks at ~0.15, 1.25, 1.50, 2.30, 3.20, and 4.46 s) rather than the characteristic sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1489030138,25262,4,2.627600014740855e-13,1018,4,29,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a complex mineral or organic pattern with major peaks at ~0.33 s, ~1.45 s, ~1.70 s, ~2.18 s (the highest peak), ~2.85 s, and ~4.68 s. Because the highest peak is not an isolated Na+ peak and there is no Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak following ~1.49 s after a dominant Na+ peak, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1489031041,25314,4,4.829400022791398e-14,1018,4,32,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~0.18 µs (with a secondary major peak at ~3.26 µs) rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 µs, violating Rule 1. Furthermore, the peaks at ~1.30 µs, ~1.54 µs, ~2.30 µs, ~3.26 µs, and ~4.52 µs represent a complex organic or mineral pattern rather than the required 1.49 µs Na(NaOH)+ spacing.",
1489031361,25335,4,4.731570089075779e-14,1018,4,34,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because the highest peaks are at ~0.21 us and ~3.31 us rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 us. Furthermore, it displays a mineral or organic peak pattern (with major features at ~1.31 us, ~2.30 us, ~3.31 us, and ~4.56 us, very similar to reference 1587421738) rather than the required 1.49 us sodium hydroxide cluster spacing.",
1489032520,25440,4,1.830610045060882e-13,1018,4,40,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is a broad mineral or organic feature at ~3.42 µs rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 µs, violating Rule 1. Furthermore, relative to the candidate peak at ~1.63 µs, there is no narrow Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak 1.49 µs later (~3.12 µs), with the spectrum instead dominated by peaks at ~0.30 µs, ~2.38 µs, ~3.42 µs, and ~4.68 µs.",
1489033352,25514,4,5.477950111207851e-14,1018,4,42,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because its highest peak is a broad feature at ~3.32 µs (nearly matched by a sharp H+ peak at ~0.22 µs) rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 µs. Instead of a sodium hydroxide cluster series, it exhibits a complex mineral or organic profile with multiple peaks at ~1.32 µs, ~1.58 µs, ~2.33 µs, ~3.32 µs, and ~4.57 µs.",
1489034301,25605,5,4.841639987692402e-14,1018,5,49,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum consists almost entirely of instrumental noise, with its highest spike at ~0.14 µs and only a minor peak at ~1.54 µs. It lacks both a dominant Na+ peak and the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 µs later (at ~3.03 µs).",
1489037230,25867,4,3.5331099482692474e-13,1018,4,67,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because its highest peak is a broad mineral/organic feature at ~3.53 us rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 us. Furthermore, it displays a complex multi-peak mineral pattern (with peaks at ~0.36 us, ~1.45 us, ~1.68 us, and ~4.82 us) rather than the clean 1.49 us sodium hydroxide cluster spacing.",
1489037350,25879,Noise,8.377880230921522e-14,1018,Noise,72,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum consists entirely of continuous, high-amplitude instrumental noise across the 0 to 6.4 5s range, with a random spike reaching 1.0 at ~0.3 5s. It completely lacks a coherent Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 5s and the corresponding Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak 1.49 5s later.",
1489058807,31121,1,1.852129967406732e-13,1018,1,249,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This is a water-ice spectrum dominated by a regularly spaced hydronium cluster series starting with the highest peak at ~1.25 µs, followed by major peaks at ~2.08 µs (0.83 µs later), ~2.71 µs (1.46 µs later), and ~3.25 µs. Because the dominant progression consists of closely spaced water-ice clusters rather than an isolated Na+ peak followed ~1.49 µs later by a Na(NaOH)+ peak, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1489059753,32063,2,7.080260314672182e-14,1018,2,288,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum lacks a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 6s, reaching its maximum amplitude instead at approximately 3.73 6s. It is dominated by a regularly spaced series of broad water-ice cluster peaks at ~2.45 6s, ~3.08 6s, ~3.73 6s, ~4.22 6s, and ~4.65 6s, rather than the sodium hydroxide cluster pattern.",
1489060119,32428,1,1.9459299555285407e-14,1018,1,302,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a typical water-ice hydronium cluster series starting with the highest peak at ~0.62 5s, followed by regularly spaced peaks at ~1.44 5s, ~2.08 5s, and ~2.63 5s. It lacks both a dominant Na+ peak in the expected 1.4–2.0 5s range and the diagnostic Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 5s later.",
1489086373,51964,3-Car,8.307859744116977e-14,1018,3-Car,34545,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows an extremely broad, saturated feature peaking around 2.13 9cs followed by slow, wavy baseline undulations peaking near 3.70 9cs and 5.45 9cs, rather than sharp, well-resolved Na+ and Na(NaOH)+ peaks separated by 1.49 9cs.",
1489086994,52576,3-OH,2.62194996616949e-13,1018,3-OH,34546,3-OH,3-OH,"Despite the elevated baseline shift, the spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.08 s followed ~1.47 s later by a distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.55 s. A secondary Na(NaOH)2+ cluster peak is also visible at ~4.58 s (~2.50 s after Na+), confirming the sodium hydroxide series.",
1489088347,53927,3-Car,2.6294298769574675e-13,1018,3-Car,34547,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a broad double-peaked feature around 2.04-2.16 s followed by a sustained, high baseline near 0.8 amplitude with minor features at ~3.65 s and ~4.64 s, lacking a clean, isolated Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 s after a sharp Na+ peak.",
1489088584,54163,1,1.7828500245673125e-14,1018,1,554,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a water-ice hydronium cluster series starting with the highest peak at ~1.63 s (H3O+) followed by a major peak at ~2.45 s (0.82 s later) and another at ~3.08 s (1.45 s after the first peak, rather than a clean Na+ and Na(NaOH)+ pair, as evidenced by the dominant intermediate water cluster at ~2.45 s and small Na+ peak at ~1.83 s).",
1489088775,54354,5,5.087469955402692e-14,1018,5,565,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a broad double-peaked feature near 1.90–2.02 9cs followed closely by a prominent K+ peak at ~2.64 9cs (a distance of ~0.62–0.74 9cs), and completely lacks the diagnostic Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak expected ~1.49 9cs after Na+ (around 3.39–3.51 9cs).",
1489088850,54429,1,6.42322973238782e-14,1018,1,570,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This is a classic water-ice spectrum dominated by a regularly spaced hydronium cluster series (H3O+(H2O)n) with major peaks at ~1.76 µs, ~2.58 µs, ~3.21 µs, ~3.75 µs, and ~4.22 µs. The first interval is ~0.82 µs rather than the ~1.49 µs spacing required for a Na(NaOH)+ cluster.",
1489089053,54631,Noise,1.9857200058521693e-14,1018,Noise,585,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is a sharp spike near 0.12 µs rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 µs, and the remainder of the spectrum consists entirely of instrumental noise with no Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak.",
1489089332,54909,1,1.214220035823145e-14,1018,1,607,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~1.06 s (too early for Na+, likely H3O+), followed by a water-ice hydronium cluster series at ~1.88 s and ~2.53 s (time distances of ~0.82 s and ~1.47 s from the first peak, rather than a Na(NaOH)+ cluster ~1.49 s after a Na+ peak in the 1.4-2.0 s range).",
1489089375,54952,2,2.222020005872901e-14,1018,2,611,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is located at approximately 2.98 6s rather than being a dominant Na+ peak in the 1.4–2.0 6s range. The spectrum shows a series of broad, closely spaced cluster peaks around 2.50 6s, 2.98 6s, 3.52 6s, and 4.05 6s, lacking the characteristic 1.49 6s spacing of the sodium hydroxide series.",
1489089481,55058,2,1.1833000298198688e-14,1018,2,620,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a series of peaks at approximately 0.45 µs, 1.30 µs (highest peak), 1.94 µs, and 2.50 µs, which corresponds to a water-ice cluster progression rather than a sodium hydroxide series. Even if the peak at 1.30 µs were Na+, the next major peak follows only 0.64 µs later at 1.94 µs, lacking the required Na(NaOH)+ peak about 1.49 µs after the main peak (around 2.79 µs).",
1489090468,56043,5,1.3811100056844178e-14,1018,5,682,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows two prominent peaks at approximately 1.20 µs and 1.92 µs (separated by only ~0.72 µs, typical of Na+ and K+), and completely lacks a Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at the required 1.49 µs interval after either peak (around 2.69 µs or 3.41 µs).",
1489090696,56270,1,1.427170047993507e-14,1018,1,697,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a regularly spaced water-ice hydronium cluster series starting with the highest peak at ~1.37 µs, followed by major peaks at ~2.19 µs (+0.82 µs), ~2.82 µs, ~3.35 µs, and ~3.81 µs, rather than the required Na+ and Na(NaOH)+ pattern separated by ~1.49 µs.",
1489091035,56608,2,5.291550007955996e-14,1018,2,714,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This spectrum is dominated by a dense series of broad water-ice/salt cluster peaks at approximately 1.85 5s, 2.30 5s, 2.80 5s, 3.35 5s, and 3.95 5s. Instead of an isolated Na+ peak followed ~1.49 5s later by Na(NaOH)+ on a clean baseline, the major peaks are spaced roughly 0.45–0.60 5s apart, which is characteristic of a hydronium-water cluster series rather than the sodium hydroxide pattern.",
1489091121,56693,3-Car,3.9740498896214185e-14,1018,3-Car,34548,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is dominated by a broad double peak reaching its maximum at ~2.28 5s (with an earlier shoulder at ~2.03 5s) rather than a clean, dominant Na+ peak. Furthermore, the subsequent peaks at ~3.57 5s (~1.29 5s after the main peak) and ~5.19 5s do not match the expected 1.49 5s spacing and cluster progression of the sodium hydroxide series.",
1489091818,57387,3-Cl,4.679220064803674e-14,1018,3-Cl,34549,non-3-OH,3-OH,The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at 1.99 s followed 1.49 s later by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at 3.48 s. This sodium hydroxide signature is further confirmed by the hydrated cluster peak at 4.00 s (0.52 s after m/z 63) and the second hydroxide cluster at 4.52 s (1.04 s after m/z 63).,
1489092599,58162,2,1.53737997809697e-13,1018,2,779,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is a water-ice spectrum dominated by a regularly spaced hydronium cluster series with major peaks at ~2.05 9cs, ~2.93 9cs (the highest peak), ~3.60 9cs, and ~4.15 9cs. Because the highest peak is at ~2.93 9cs rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 9cs followed 1.49 9cs later by Na(NaOH)+, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1489093159,58717,1,1.1413199758111142e-14,1018,1,810,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a classic water-ice hydronium cluster series with major peaks at ~1.08 bc	ext{s}, ~1.91 bc	ext{s} (highest peak), ~2.54 bc	ext{s}, ~3.07 bc	ext{s}, and ~3.54 bc	ext{s}. Even if the peak at 1.91 bc	ext{s} were Na+, there is no peak at ~3.40 bc	ext{s} (1.49 bc	ext{s} later), ruling out the 3-OH sodium hydroxide pattern.",
1489093842,59391,1,1.615909995058857e-14,1018,1,852,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is a sharp spike at ~0.14 5s rather than Na+, and the modest peak at ~1.44 5s is followed by a weak feature at ~2.25 5s (~0.81 5s later) and noise instead of a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 5s later (around 2.93 5s).",
1489094177,59720,1,1.5881500148719023e-14,1018,1,867,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a regularly spaced water-ice hydronium cluster series starting at ~1.54 5s, followed by major peaks at ~2.35 5s (a distance of ~0.81 5s), ~2.98 5s, ~3.51 5s, and ~3.99 5s, rather than the required Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 5s after a dominant Na+ peak.",
1489094594,60130,1,2.3412600525830884e-14,1018,1,892,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This spectrum shows a typical water-ice hydronium cluster series starting with a dominant peak at ~1.63 5s, followed by regularly spaced peaks at ~2.48 5s, ~3.13 5s, ~3.66 5s, and ~4.10 5s. Because the next major peak appears ~0.85 5s after the initial peak rather than the ~1.49 5s distance required for Na(NaOH)+, it is classified as 'non-3-OH'.",
1489095249,60770,2,1.0371400054965188e-14,1018,2,920,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a noisy hydronium/water-ice cluster progression with major peaks at ~1.25 5s, ~2.10 5s (highest peak), ~2.80 5s, and ~3.40 5s. It lacks both a clean dominant Na+ peak in the typical range and the diagnostic Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 5s after the main peak.",
1489095315,60833,3-Car,4.828290070817316e-14,1018,3-Car,34550,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum lacks a narrow, dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 s, instead showing a very broad, double-peaked feature between 2.0 and 2.8 s (maxima at ~2.20 s and ~2.45 s), followed by broad peaks at ~3.76 s and ~5.35 s that do not match the sharp sodium hydroxide cluster pattern.",
1489095427,60941,1,2.0842699175729548e-14,1018,1,926,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This spectrum is dominated by a water-ice hydronium cluster series (peaks at ~1.67 µs, ~2.50 µs, ~3.13 µs, and ~3.63 µs) along with a likely Na+ peak at ~1.88 µs. Because the highest peak is H3O+ at ~1.67 µs rather than Na+, and there is no Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 µs after the ~1.88 µs peak (at ~3.37 µs), it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1489096588,62056,3-P,2.5162599393978476e-14,1018,3-P,34551,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although a prominent peak appears at 3.68 µs (about 1.46 µs after the main peak at 2.22 µs), the main peak is a broad, split complex at 2.22 µs and 2.34 µs rather than a clean, narrow Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 µs. This split peak structure and late onset indicate a non-3-OH composition.",
1489097075,62520,1,1.7340600797725175e-14,1018,1,1028,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This spectrum shows a typical water-ice hydronium cluster series starting with a main peak at ~1.57 s, followed by regularly spaced cluster peaks at ~2.38 s (only ~0.81 s later), ~3.01 s, ~3.54 s, and ~4.00 s. Because the peak spacing after the main peak does not match the ~1.49 s interval required for an isolated Na(NaOH)+ cluster, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1489097863,63267,1,1.1093299977888663e-14,1018,1,1069,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a typical water-ice hydronium cluster series (H3O+(H2O)n) with the highest peak at ~0.84 6s, followed by regularly spaced peaks at ~1.48 6s, ~2.01 6s, ~2.48 6s, and ~2.90 6s. It lacks a dominant Na+ peak and the required 1.49 6s spacing to a Na(NaOH)+ cluster.",
1489097920,63320,5,3.722509903407098e-14,1018,5,1072,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a Na+ peak at ~1.47 5s, but the highest peak is a K+ peak at ~2.18 5s (~0.71 5s later), violating Rule 1. Furthermore, there is no Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 5s after the Na+ peak (around 2.96 5s).",
1489098134,63521,1,2.2718899176754452e-14,1018,1,1085,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This is a classic water-ice spectrum dominated by a regularly spaced hydronium cluster series with major peaks at ~1.61 µs, ~2.43 µs (the highest peak), ~3.05 µs, ~3.58 µs, and ~4.06 µs. Because the highest peak is a water-ice cluster at ~2.43 µs rather than Na+, and the peak spacing (~0.82 µs, ~0.62 µs, ~0.53 µs) does not match the ~1.49 µs sodium hydroxide progression, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1489098346,63718,2,1.5901700190445144e-14,1018,2,1101,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This is a water-ice spectrum dominated by a regularly spaced series of hydronium cluster peaks at approximately 1.43 9cs, 2.28 Γcs, 2.92 Γcs, 3.49 Γcs, and 3.98 Γcs. The highest peaks at ~2.28 Γcs and ~2.92 Γcs are separated by ~0.64 Γcs rather than the ~1.49 Γcs distance required for a Na+ to Na(NaOH)+ cluster pattern.",
1489098738,64082,5,1.7491799566941857e-14,1018,5,1113,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant peak at approximately 1.52 µs followed closely by a second major peak at 2.20 µs (a separation of only 0.68 µs), and completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak about 1.49 µs after the main peak (around 3.01 µs).",
1489099150,64461,5,1.0414399682532553e-14,1018,5,1139,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows only a single dominant peak at approximately 0.68 bcs (well outside the typical 1.4–2.0 bcs range for Na+) and completely lacks any subsequent cluster peaks, including the required Na(NaOH)+ peak about 1.49 bcs later.",
1489100098,65330,2,3.131199929873839e-14,1018,2,1187,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is a water-ice pattern dominated by a regularly spaced hydronium cluster series with major peaks at ~1.60 9cs, ~2.43 9cs, ~3.15 9cs (the highest peak), ~3.70 9cs, and ~4.20 9cs. Because the highest peak is at ~3.15 9cs rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 9cs, it violates Rule 1 and is classified as non-3-OH.",
1489100851,473,5,1.2910099421795107e-13,1018,5,1236,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is not the initial peak at ~2.02 µs (likely Na+ or H3O+), but rather a broad double-peaked feature reaching maximum amplitude at ~2.87 µs (~0.85 µs later). Furthermore, there is no Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at the required ~1.49 µs distance after the ~2.02 µs peak (expected around 3.51 µs).",
1489101408,963,3-Car,5.1621799554164155e-14,1018,3-Car,34552,non-3-OH,3-OH,The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.94 5s followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 5s later at ~3.43 5s. This sodium hydroxide pattern is further confirmed by the second hydroxide cluster peak Na(NaOH)2+ at ~4.47 5s (~2.53 5s after Na+).,
1489101738,1254,2,1.620049953291857e-14,1018,2,1288,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although there is a dominant peak at ~1.72 BCs, the next major peak occurs at ~2.70 BCs (a distance of ~0.98 BCs, consistent with water-ice clusters rather than NaOH), and there is no prominent Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 BCs later at ~3.21 BCs.",
1489102733,2112,3-Cl,6.821579840712508e-14,1018,3-Cl,34553,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although there is a broad peak at ~2.16 s and peaks at ~3.58 s and ~4.13 s, the peak at ~4.13 s is nearly equal in amplitude (0.99) to the initial broad Na+/K+ complex and dominates the mid-spectrum (likely Na(NaCl)+ or another salt/Rh+), rather than showing the clean, monotonically decreasing Na(NaOH)n+ hydroxide cluster series typical of 3-OH spectra.",
1489103125,2444,3-Cl,6.989570055550287e-13,1018,3-Cl,34554,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a double peak around 2.10–2.22 5s followed by a severe baseline overshoot that remains near 0.82 amplitude across the rest of the recording. It lacks a distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at the expected 1.49 5s interval after the main peak (around 3.59–3.71 5s), showing only minor bumps on the elevated baseline that match a water-ice hydronium series (at ~2.10, 2.90, 3.63, and 4.15 5s).",
1489110224,3046,3-Car,5.317839877759696e-14,1018,3-Car,34555,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although a peak appears at ~3.67 µs (about 1.49 µs after the maximum at ~2.18 µs), the main feature at ~2.18 µs is an extremely broad, heavily tailing continuum rather than a narrow Na+ peak, and the subsequent broad feature at ~5.30 µs (~3.12 µs after the main peak) does not match the sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1489111914,3343,1,1.0768000362627438e-14,1018,1,1398,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This is a water-ice spectrum dominated by a hydronium cluster series with major peaks at ~1.57 µs, ~2.38 µs, and ~3.03 µs. If the ~1.76 µs peak is Na+, the spectrum lacks a corresponding Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 µs later at ~3.25 µs.",
1489113651,3652,1,1.7340600797725175e-14,1018,1,1401,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This spectrum shows a water-ice hydronium cluster series starting with the highest peak at ~1.63 9̦s, followed by major peaks at ~2.44 9̦s (~0.81 9̦s later) and ~3.07 9̦s (~1.44 9̦s later, with further clusters at ~3.60 9̦s). The prominent peak at ~2.44 9̦s is characteristic of water-ice clusters rather than the isolated Na(NaOH)+ pattern expected ~1.49 9̦s after Na+.",
1489115292,3865,3-Cl,6.587270198711234e-14,1018,3-Cl,34556,non-3-OH,3-OH,"Although the broad initial peak complex has a shoulder at ~2.34 Us and reaches maximum amplitude at ~2.46 Us, it is followed by prominent peaks at ~3.85 Us and ~4.36 Us. Taking the ~2.36 Us feature as a time-shifted Na+ peak, the subsequent peaks lie ~1.49 Us and ~2.00 Us later, matching the exact spacing of the Na(NaOH)+ (m/z 63) and Na(NaOH)(H2O)+ (m/z 81) hydroxide cluster series.",
1495337551,63674,1,1.2298899759407601e-14,1018,1,1464,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a classic water-ice hydronium cluster series (H3O+(H2O)n) with major peaks at ~1.58 µs, ~2.41 µs (the highest peak), ~3.03 µs, ~3.57 µs, and ~4.07 µs. Because the highest peak is at ~2.41 µs rather than Na+ and the spacing between the first two peaks is ~0.83 µs instead of the ~1.49 µs required for Na(NaOH)+, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1495340127,704,1,1.2618599639854528e-14,1018,1,1512,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This spectrum is dominated by a regularly spaced water-ice hydronium cluster series with major peaks at ~1.22 5s, ~2.04 5s (the highest peak), ~2.68 5s, ~3.21 5s, ~3.71 5s, and ~4.14 5s. It is classified as non-3-OH because the highest peak is a water-ice cluster rather than Na+, and the peak spacings (~0.5 to 0.8 5s) do not match the required 1.49 5s interval for a Na(NaOH)+ cluster.",
1495341318,1895,1,1.0531900092975669e-14,1018,1,1531,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This spectrum is dominated by a regularly spaced water-ice hydronium cluster series starting at ~1.56 µs, with subsequent major peaks at ~2.38 µs (0.82 µs later), ~3.00 µs, ~3.54 µs, ~4.02 µs, and ~4.45 µs. Even though a peak at ~3.00 µs lies ~1.44 µs after the first peak, the prominent ~2.38 µs peak and regular water-cluster progression show that this is a water-ice grain rather than a sodium hydroxide series.",
1495342049,2623,Noise,1.0315899745755655e-13,1018,Noise,1543,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows periodic, square-wave-like instrumental oscillations spaced roughly every 0.6 ΗΑs across the entire recording, reaching maximum amplitude at ~4.68 ΗΑs. It completely lacks a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 ΗΑs and the diagnostic Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak 1.49 ΗΑs later.",
1496913395,4329,2,4.200310008118345e-14,1018,2,1587,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dense, regularly spaced series of broad water-ice cluster peaks at approximately 1.73 µs, 2.22 µs, 2.57 µs, 3.23 µs, and 3.85 µs, rather than an isolated Na+ peak followed 1.49 µs later by a clean Na(NaOH)+ cluster.",
1496913632,4566,2,2.8105200323069388e-14,1018,2,1589,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a classic water-ice pattern dominated by a regularly spaced hydronium cluster series (H3O+(H2O)n) with major peaks at ~1.70 µs, ~2.53 µs (the highest peak), ~3.18 µs, ~3.85 µs, and ~4.33 µs. It lacks both a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 µs and the characteristic Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak 1.49 µs later.",
1496951872,17580,4,3.1215898328674704e-14,1018,4,1593,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because its highest peak is located at ~3.25 s rather than representing a dominant Na+ peak in the expected 1.42.0 s range. Instead, the spectrum displays a complex mineral/organic pattern with peaks at ~0.18 s, ~1.28 s, ~1.54 s, ~2.32 s, ~3.25 s, and ~4.52 s, lacking the characteristic 1.49 s spacing of a sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1498471387,47442,3-Car,3.553819903829615e-14,1018,3-Car,34557,non-3-OH,3-OH,The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.00 µs followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.48 µs (a separation of ~1.48 µs). This sodium hydroxide series is further confirmed by the second hydroxide cluster peak Na(NaOH)2+ at ~4.52 µs (~2.52 µs after the Na+ peak).,
1498471787,47802,3-KNa,2.3142800203339656e-14,1018,3-KNa,34558,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~2.08 s (preceded by a strong peak at ~1.37 s), and the next major peak is at ~2.88 s, which is ~0.80 s after the highest peak rather than the required ~1.49 s for Na(NaOH)+. Even if the ~1.37 s peak were Na+, it is not the highest peak in the spectrum, violating Rule 1.",
1498472699,48642,3-Cl,9.684049758927268e-14,1018,3-Cl,34559,non-3-OH,3-OH,The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.03 µs followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.53 µs (1.50 µs later). This diagnostic pattern is further supported by a hydrated hydroxide cluster peak Na(NaOH)(H2O)+ at ~4.05 µs (0.52 µs after the m/z 63 peak).,
1498472876,48806,3-Cl,7.7425797706792e-14,1018,3-Cl,34560,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the spectrum shows a peak at ~2.38 s (with a smaller peak at ~2.22 s) and a secondary peak ~1.51 s later at ~3.89 s, the subsequent cluster pattern is dominated by massive, broad peaks at ~4.41 s and ~5.75 s rather than a clean sodium hydroxide series, indicating a different salt (such as NaCl) or mineral composition.",
1498475331,51113,3-Car,1.8358600230306e-13,1018,3-Car,34561,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum lacks a clean, dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 µs; instead, it features a broad double-peaked structure starting at ~2.22 µs and reaching its maximum at ~2.52 µs, followed by broad peaks around ~3.83 µs and ~5.56 µs that do not match the narrow sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1498478705,54303,3-Car,6.714069675662487e-14,1018,3-Car,34562,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at approximately 2.15 s (split with a peak at 2.05 s), followed about 1.49 s later by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.64 s. Additional hydroxide cluster peaks appear at ~4.25 s and ~5.30 s, confirming the 3-OH classification.",
1498480402,55914,3-K,2.2478799217525748e-14,1018,3-K,34358,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum has a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.88 9cs, but lacks a clear, prominent Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 9cs later (~3.37 9cs); instead, the main cluster peak appears at ~3.95 9cs (~2.07 9cs after Na+, consistent with Na(NaCl)+ at m/z 81), indicating a chloride-dominated salt grain rather than a 3-OH grain.",
1498480546,56051,3-Car,4.8028401188841136e-14,1018,3-Car,34563,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant, saturated Na+ peak complex centered near 2.23 µs (with split maxima at 2.18 and 2.28 µs), followed approximately 1.49 µs later by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at 3.72 µs.",
1498483449,58900,2,5.271630164728827e-14,1018,2,1644,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This spectrum shows a water-ice hydronium cluster series with major peaks at ~2.03 µs, ~2.85 µs, ~3.48 µs, and ~4.10 µs (almost identical to reference 1498483996). Even though there is a peak at ~3.48 µs (~1.45 µs after the 2.03 µs peak), the presence of a nearly equal-amplitude peak at ~2.85 µs (~0.82 µs after the first peak) confirms this is a regularly spaced water-ice series rather than a sodium hydroxide pattern.",
1498484072,59523,3-KNa,6.280340017570524e-14,1018,3-KNa,34564,non-3-OH,3-OH,"Although there is a strong potassium (K+) peak at 2.82 s (0.68 s after the dominant Na+ peak at 2.14 s), the spectrum clearly exhibits the diagnostic Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at 3.62 s (1.48 s after Na+), followed by the hydrated Na(NaOH)(H2O)+ peak at 4.11 s (+1.97 s) and a subsequent cluster at 4.50 s.",
1498485882,61333,1,2.040690072436721e-14,1018,1,1687,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is a classic water-ice pattern dominated by a regularly spaced hydronium cluster series (peaks at ~1.48, 2.33, 2.93, 3.46, 3.95, 4.38, and 4.78 µs), with the highest peaks at ~2.93 and ~3.46 µs rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 µs.",
1498486025,61476,1,2.6644400525971043e-14,1018,1,1689,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This is a water-ice spectrum dominated by a regularly spaced series of hydronium cluster peaks starting at ~1.65 5s, followed by major peaks at ~2.47 5s, ~3.10 5s, ~3.64 5s, and ~4.12 5s. The second major peak is ~0.82 5s after the first rather than the ~1.49 5s distance required for a Na(NaOH)+ cluster.",
1498486542,61993,2,7.746530332345195e-14,1018,2,1700,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is a classic water-ice spectrum dominated by a regularly spaced hydronium cluster series (H3O+(H2O)n) with major peaks at ~1.72 µs, ~2.55 µs (the highest peak), ~3.23 µs, ~3.80 µs, and ~4.28 µs. Because the highest peak is not Na+ (m/z 23) and the spectrum follows a water-ice spacing rather than the sodium hydroxide pattern, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1498486682,62132,3-KNa,1.4431499344071813e-13,1018,3-KNa,34565,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~2.72 s rather than the initial peak at ~2.01 s, and the spectrum is dominated by a regularly spaced series of peaks (~2.01, ~2.72, ~3.48, ~4.00, ~4.41, and ~4.82 s) characteristic of water-ice or another salt series rather than an isolated Na(NaOH)+ cluster progression.",
1498486879,62328,2,1.3549399910427543e-14,1018,2,1707,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the spectrum has a dominant peak at ~1.96 µs, the subsequent major peaks appear at ~2.88 µs (0.92 µs later), ~3.52 µs (1.56 µs later, a minor peak in a water-ice series), and ~4.10 µs, forming a regularly spaced water-ice cluster progression (H3O+(H2O)n) rather than an isolated Na(NaOH)+ pattern.",
1498487099,62546,2,1.9948100246289235e-14,1018,2,1715,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as non-3-OH because the highest peak is at ~3.58 5s rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 5s. Instead of a sodium hydroxide series, it displays a regularly spaced water-ice cluster progression with major peaks at ~2.03 5s, ~2.95 5s, ~3.58 5s, ~4.14 5s, ~4.64 5s, ~5.08 5s, and ~5.48 5s.",
1498489218,64464,3-OH,2.2906500372725513e-13,1018,3-OH,34566,3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.12 6s, followed by a clear Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.57 6s (~1.45 6s later) and a smaller Na(NaOH)2+ peak at ~4.62 6s (~2.50 6s after Na+) riding on an elevated baseline.",
1498489740,64860,3-K,2.7656699765630025e-14,1018,3-K,34567,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~2.28 5s, and the next major peaks follow at ~3.92 5s (1.64 5s later) and ~4.37 5s (2.09 5s later, likely Na(NaCl)+), lacking the required prominent Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 5s after Na+.",
1498491309,391,3-OH,1.4776300029471084e-13,1018,3-OH,34568,3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak reaching maximum amplitude at ~2.14 9cs, followed ~1.49 9cs later by a strong Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.63 9cs. This sodium hydroxide series is further confirmed by the second hydroxide cluster peak Na(NaOH)2+ at ~4.66 9cs (~2.52 9cs after the Na+ peak).",
1498499019,3701,3-Car,1.9005899759279125e-14,1018,3-Car,34571,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The highest peak is Na+ at approximately 2.27 5s (shifted later due to a larger t0 offset), followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at 3.76 5s, which is exactly 1.49 5s later. Although the peak at 5.38 5s is unusually large (likely due to target or higher-mass cluster ions), the core 1.49 5s spacing between Na+ and Na(NaOH)+ clearly satisfies the 3-OH criteria.",
1498504101,4952,3-Car,6.046609746105172e-14,1018,3-Car,34572,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is a broad feature at ~2.43 5s (outside the typical 1.4–2.0 5s range for sharp Na+), followed by equally broad peaks at ~3.88 5s and ~5.50 5s. Although the spacing between the first two peaks is ~1.45 5s, the third major peak at ~5.50 5s (3.07 5s after the first peak) does not match the sodium hydroxide cluster series (expected at ~1.99 5s or ~2.53 5s after Na+).",
1500076010,45088,4,1.261500019028583e-12,1018,4,1722,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a complex mineral-like profile with multiple broad peaks at ~0.42 BCs, ~1.63 BCs, ~2.22 BCs (the highest peak), ~2.53 BCs, ~3.20 BCs, ~3.77 BCs, and ~5.06 BCs, rather than a dominant, isolated Na+ peak followed by a clean sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1500077099,45459,4,6.656430100041369e-14,1018,4,1723,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because its highest peak is located at ~0.25 bc	ext{s} (likely H⁺) rather than being a dominant Na⁺ peak in the 1.4–2.0 bc	ext{s} range, violating Rule 1. Instead of a sodium hydroxide cluster series, it displays a mineral or organic profile with major peaks at ~1.35 bc	ext{s}, ~1.60 bc	ext{s}, ~2.38 bc	ext{s}, ~3.34 bc	ext{s}, and ~4.60 bc	ext{s}.",
1501671551,17857,4,2.2377599447932772e-13,1018,4,1730,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as non-3-OH because it shows a complex mineral/organic pattern with a broad base peak at ~2.21 9̨s rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 9̨s. Furthermore, it features multiple non-hydroxide peaks at ~0.33 9̨s, ~1.43 9̨s, ~1.65 9̨s, ~2.90 9̨s, ~3.46 9̨s, and ~4.73 9̨s, lacking the clean 1.49 9̨s spacing of the Na(NaOH)+ cluster series.",
1501674339,18083,4,7.449850198543162e-13,1018,4,1732,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because the highest peak is a broad complex reaching maximum amplitude at ~3.02 us rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 us. Furthermore, it displays a complex mineral/organic profile with prominent peaks at ~0.41 us, ~1.43 us, ~1.67 us, and ~2.34 us, completely lacking the isolated Na(NaOH)+ cluster pattern.",
1503217821,9553,2,1.979709968278221e-14,1018,2,1748,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a water-ice hydronium cluster series starting with the highest peak at ~1.83 s, followed by another major peak of nearly equal height at ~2.65 s (only ~0.82 s later) and broad clusters at ~3.35 s and ~3.95 s. Because the dominant progression is a water-ice series rather than an isolated Na(NaOH)+ cluster ~1.49 s after Na+, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1503220894,12610,2,3.598330129955113e-13,1018,2,1766,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows an initial peak at approximately 2.22 5s followed by a regularly spaced series of broad water-ice cluster peaks at ~3.05 5s, ~3.75 5s, and ~4.35 5s on a heavily elevated baseline, completely lacking the isolated Na(NaOH)+ peak expected ~1.49 5s after a Na+ peak.",
1503221287,13003,1,5.88610987750128e-14,1018,1,1769,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a water-ice hydronium cluster series starting with the highest peak at ~1.76 s (plus a Na+ peak at ~2.00 s), followed by major water-cluster peaks at ~2.61 s (0.85 s after the first peak) and ~3.26 s. Because the highest peak is not Na+ and the subsequent peaks follow a water-ice spacing rather than the 1.49 s Na(NaOH)+ interval, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1503221793,13509,2,5.557719947235293e-14,1018,2,1771,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This spectrum is dominated by a regularly spaced water-ice hydronium cluster series (H3O+(H2O)n) with major peaks at ~1.88 µs, ~2.12 µs, ~2.85 µs (reaching maximum amplitude of 1.0), ~3.53 µs, ~4.10 µs, and ~4.52 µs. It lacks an isolated Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak 1.49 µs after the initial peak at 1.88 µs (which would appear at ~3.37 µs, where a trough is located instead).",
1503254278,28998,4,3.9570500738952963e-13,1018,4,1786,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as non-3-OH because the highest peak is a broad feature at ~2.29 6s rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 6s. Furthermore, it exhibits a complex mineral-like profile with prominent peaks at ~0.38 6s, ~1.45 6s, ~1.67 6s, ~2.98 6s, and ~4.82 6s, lacking the characteristic 1.49 6s sodium hydroxide cluster spacing.",
1503257279,29174,4,1.619080032804615e-13,1018,4,1790,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as non-3-OH because the highest peak is a broad feature at ~3.42 BCs rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 BCs. Furthermore, the peak at ~1.63 BCs is not followed by a distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak 1.49 BCs later (~3.12 BCs), displaying instead a mineral or organic profile with major peaks at ~0.30 BCs, ~1.40 BCs, ~2.37 BCs, and ~4.68 BCs.",
1503257335,29175,4,6.514419944236502e-14,1018,4,1791,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~0.25 µs (H+ or C+), not Na+ (which is smaller or part of the mineral/organic peaks around ~1.62 µs), violating Rule 1. Furthermore, the broad peak at ~3.33 µs (~1.71 µs after the 1.62 µs peak) and the peak at ~4.60 µs represent a mineral or organic spectrum rather than the sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1503258247,29224,4,1.0014599962021933e-13,1018,4,1796,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is a broad mineral or organic peak at ~3.38 5s rather than Na+ in the 1.4–2.0 5s range, and there is a very strong early peak at ~0.28 5s. Furthermore, the peak near ~1.63 5s is not followed by an isolated Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 5s later, showing instead a mineral-rich pattern with prominent peaks at ~1.38 5s, ~2.38 5s, ~3.38 5s, and ~4.64 5s.",
1503260302,29312,4,1.711819976133594e-13,1018,4,1801,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as non-3-OH because the highest peak is at ~0.33 µs rather than Na+ in the 1.4–2.0 µs range, and it is dominated by broad organic or mineral peaks at ~3.42 µs and ~4.70 µs without a sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
