1503261617,29377,4,3.117810033043643e-14,1018,4,1803,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is a broad mineral or organic peak at ~3.20 5s rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 5s, violating Rule 1. Instead of a sodium hydroxide series, the spectrum shows multiple mineral peaks at ~0.16 5s, ~1.25 5s, ~1.50 5s, ~2.26 5s, ~3.20 5s, and ~4.45 5s.",
1503262147,29405,4,1.798020045839458e-14,1018,4,1804,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because its highest peak is located at ~3.15 µs rather than being a dominant Na+ peak in the expected 1.4-2.0 µs range. Furthermore, the peaks at ~1.22 µs, ~1.47 µs, ~2.24 µs, ~3.15 µs, and ~4.42 µs do not follow the required 1.49 µs spacing for a sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1503262174,29407,4,1.0128699704588413e-14,1018,4,1805,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is located at approximately 3.12 µs rather than in the expected 1.4–2.0 µs range for Na+, violating Rule 1. Furthermore, the next major peak at ~4.40 µs follows by ~1.28 µs rather than the required 1.49 µs spacing for a sodium hydroxide cluster pattern.",
1506224477,19277,3-P,2.443069889185995e-13,1018,3-P,34573,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a broad double-peaked feature between 2.11 and 2.23 s with an elevated baseline tail rather than a clean dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 s. Although a peak appears at 3.59 s (~1.48 s after the 2.11 s shoulder), the subsequent peaks at 5.14 s, 5.90 s, and 6.32 s do not match the sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1506224828,19628,3-Car,4.1088999065165555e-14,1018,3-Car,34574,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.98 BCs, followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.45 BCs (a distance of ~1.47 BCs, matching the expected 1.49 BCs interval). This sodium hydroxide series is further confirmed by the second hydroxide cluster peak Na(NaOH)2+ at ~4.50 BCs (~2.52 BCs after Na+).",
1506225047,19847,3-Cl,8.094690011600097e-14,1018,3-Cl,34575,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at approximately 1.93 s, followed about 1.46 s later by a clear Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at 3.39 s. This sodium hydroxide pattern is further confirmed by the hydrated cluster peak Na(NaOH)(H2O)+ at 3.90 s (0.51 s after the m/z 63 peak).",
1506225048,19848,2,9.152449848351396e-14,1018,2,1903,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is dominated by a dense, regularly spaced series of broad water-ice and salt cluster peaks at approximately 1.88 9cs, 2.28 9cs, 2.72 9cs (the highest peak, violating Rule 1), 3.33 9cs, and 3.95 9cs. Because the base peak is at 2.72 9cs rather than a clean Na+ peak and the spectrum lacks an isolated Na(NaOH)+ progression, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1506225311,20111,3-K,8.747309923921517e-14,1018,3-K,34576,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is a broad double peak around 2.65-2.80 s rather than a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.00 s, violating Rule 1. Furthermore, there is no Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.49 s (1.49 s after the 2.00 s peak), with the subsequent major peaks appearing much later at ~4.35 s and ~4.87 s.",
1506225413,20213,1,1.8386200290672512e-14,1018,1,1925,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This is a water-ice spectrum dominated by a regularly spaced series of H3O+(H2O)n cluster peaks at ~1.60 9cs, ~2.43 Δs, ~3.05 Δs, ~3.57 Δs, and ~4.03 Δs, with the highest peaks at ~2.43 Δs and ~3.05 Δs rather than Na+ at ~1.80 Δs. It lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ peak about 1.49 Δs after Na+.",
1506225494,20294,1,2.3247000502444985e-14,1018,1,1929,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This spectrum is dominated by a regularly spaced water-ice hydronium cluster series with major peaks at ~1.67 µs, ~2.50 µs, ~3.12 µs, ~3.65 µs, and ~4.12 µs, alongside a smaller Na+ peak at ~1.88 µs. Because the highest peak is H3O+ rather than Na+ and the subsequent peaks follow a water-cluster spacing (~0.83 µs, ~0.62 µs) instead of the characteristic 1.49 µs Na(NaOH)+ interval, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1506225495,20295,1,2.079950049541958e-14,1018,1,1930,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the highest peak is at ~1.70 µs, the next dominant peak appears at ~2.52 µs (only ~0.82 µs later), which is characteristic of a water-ice hydronium cluster series (with further peaks at ~1.91 µs and ~3.14 µs) and broad clusters at ~4.45 µs, ~4.82 µs, and ~5.20 µs rather than a dominant Na(NaOH)+ cluster ~1.49 µs after Na+.",
1506225546,20346,Noise,6.084270186192814e-14,1018,Noise,1934,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum consists entirely of instrumental noise with a maximum amplitude near 0.1 Us and chaotic fluctuations from 0.7 Us to 6.4 Us, completely lacking a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 Us or a corresponding Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak 1.49 Us later.",
1506225564,20364,3-OH,2.218989965732665e-13,1018,3-OH,34577,3-OH,3-OH,"Despite the elevated baseline overshoot, the spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak complex centered around 2.07 µs followed by a distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at 3.56 µs (a distance of 1.49 µs) and a smaller Na(NaOH)2+ peak at 4.62 µs (2.55 µs after Na+), fulfilling the criteria for 3-OH.",
1506225610,20410,3-Cl,3.93550006493916e-14,1018,3-Cl,34578,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The highest peak is Na+ at approximately 2.04 s, followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at 3.50 s (a time distance of 1.46 s, matching the expected 1.49 s spacing). This sodium hydroxide signature is further supported by a strong peak at 4.02 s (0.52 s after the m/z 63 peak, corresponding to m/z 81) and a smaller peak at 4.55 s (1.05 s after the m/z 63 peak, corresponding to m/z 103).",
1506225818,20618,1,2.9380899704270144e-14,1018,1,1952,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dense, regularly spaced series of water-ice hydronium cluster peaks starting at ~1.72 µs (H3O+) with a minor Na+ peak at ~1.94 µs, followed by major peaks at ~2.55 µs, ~3.18 µs, and ~3.71 µs. Because the highest peak is H3O+ rather than Na+ and the spectrum is dominated by water-ice clusters rather than an isolated Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 µs after Na+, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1506226083,20883,1,1.0919000079101515e-14,1018,1,1970,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This is a water-ice spectrum dominated by a regularly spaced series of hydronium-water cluster peaks at approximately 1.25 s, 2.08 s (the highest peak), 2.70 s, 3.22 s, 3.68 s, and 4.12 s. The highest peak is not Na+, and the spectrum lacks the diagnostic 1.49 s spacing between Na+ and a Na(NaOH)+ cluster.",
1506226373,21173,3-OH,2.3686001077161123e-13,1018,3-OH,34579,3-OH,3-OH,"Despite the strong baseline shift, the spectrum exhibits a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.06 bc	ext{s} followed by a clear Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 bc	ext{s} later at ~3.55 bc	ext{s} and a smaller Na(NaOH)2+ peak at ~4.58 bc	ext{s} (~2.52 bc	ext{s} after Na+), matching the 3-OH pattern.",
1506226823,21623,3-Cl,9.061830197895984e-14,1018,3-Cl,34580,non-3-OH,3-OH,The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.00 µs followed ~1.48 µs later by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.48 µs. This sodium hydroxide series is further confirmed by the hydrated cluster peak Na(NaOH)(H2O)+ at ~4.00 µs (0.52 µs after the m/z 63 peak).,
1506227127,21927,1,4.929460024850549e-14,1018,1,2019,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This spectrum is dominated by a regularly spaced water-ice hydronium cluster series with major peaks at ~1.73 µs, ~2.56 µs (0.83 µs after the main peak), ~3.20 µs, ~3.75 µs, and ~4.25 µs. Because the dominant pattern comes from water clusters rather than a clean Na+ and Na(NaOH)+ sequence separated by ~1.49 µs, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1506227583,22383,3-Cl,6.18008994131801e-14,1018,3-Cl,34581,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the highest peak is at ~1.98 ͢s (preceded by a smaller H3O+ peak at ~1.78 ͢s) with subsequent peaks at ~3.42 ͢s (1.44 ͢s later) and ~3.95 ͢s (1.97 ͢s later, or 0.53 ͢s after 3.42 ͢s), the spectrum is dominated by a massive, broad underlying hump between 2.5 and 5.5 ͢s with a peak at ~3.95 ͢s (Na(NaCl)+ at m/z 81) and ~5.30 ͢s (m/z 139, Na(NaCl)2+), which indicates a chloride-dominated salt spectrum rather than a clean sodium hydroxide series.",
1506229779,24332,3-KNa,1.3631100642761546e-13,1018,3-KNa,34582,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The highest peak is Na+ at approximately 2.09 µs, followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ peak at 3.56 µs (1.47 µs after Na+, within the 1.49 ± 0.1 µs rule). The sodium hydroxide series continues with a strong Na(NaOH)2+ peak at 4.58 µs (1.02 µs after the m/z 63 peak and 2.49 µs after Na+).",
1506231212,25290,4,4.8951999138263647e-14,1018,4,2078,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because it displays a complex mineral/organic pattern with prominent early peaks at ~0.22 µs (H+) and ~1.35 µs (C+), and its highest peak is a broad double-peaked feature at ~2.05–2.22 µs rather than an isolated Na+ peak. Furthermore, even if the peak at ~2.05 µs were considered Na+, it lacks a Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 µs later (at ~3.54 µs), instead showing peaks at ~2.71 µs, ~3.29 µs, and ~4.55 µs.",
1506231511,25355,4,1.6028499328583218e-13,1018,4,2081,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is dominated by a broad peak complex at ~2.19 µs, a prominent early peak at ~0.32 µs, and subsequent peaks at ~2.83 µs (a distance of ~0.64 µs) and ~4.66 µs. It lacks both a clean dominant Na+ peak in the typical 1.4-2.0 µs range and any Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 µs after the main peak (which would be expected at ~3.68 µs).",
1506231882,25427,4,4.5381200967226087e-13,1018,4,2084,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as non-3-OH because the highest peaks are broad mineral/organic complexes at ~2.2-2.3 µs and ~2.96 µs rather than a dominant, narrow Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 µs. Furthermore, it displays prominent peaks at ~0.38 µs, ~1.43 µs, ~1.65 µs, and ~4.80 µs, completely lacking the clean 1.49 µs spacing of the sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1506232244,25490,4,2.311749932920517e-14,1018,4,2086,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak of the spectrum is located at ~3.20 s rather than being a dominant Na+ peak in the expected 1.4–2.0 s range (where smaller peaks appear at ~1.25 s and ~1.50 s), violating Rule 1. Furthermore, the peak spacing does not match the characteristic 1.49 s sodium hydroxide cluster series, showing instead a mineral or organic-like pattern with major peaks at ~1.25, ~1.50, ~2.28, ~3.20, and ~4.45 s.",
1506232321,25504,4,2.9757500717014773e-14,1018,4,2087,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum has its highest peak at ~2.00 µs, preceded by strong peaks at ~0.18 µs and ~1.28 µs, and followed by major peaks at ~2.66 µs (+0.66 µs) and ~3.23 µs (+1.23 µs). It lacks the characteristic Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak expected ~1.49 µs after the main peak (~3.49 µs), indicating a mineral or non-hydroxide composition.",
1506233441,26246,3-OH,3.837479921504905e-13,1018,3-OH,34584,3-OH,3-OH,"Despite a strong baseline overshoot after the dominant Na+ peak at ~2.03 µs, a clear Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak is visible at ~3.50 µs (about 1.47 µs later), along with a weak secondary Na(NaOH)2+ feature near ~4.55 µs (~2.52 µs after Na+), satisfying the 3-OH criteria.",
1506240050,29874,5,4.139170153545993e-14,1018,5,2113,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.04 s followed closely by a strong K+ peak at ~2.69 s (only ~0.65 s later). It completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak expected ~1.49 s after the sodium peak (around 3.53 s), confirming a non-3-OH classification.",
1506241044,30724,2,2.2904799191754248e-14,1018,2,2125,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a classic water-ice hydronium cluster series (H3O+(H2O)n) with major peaks at ~1.70 BCs, ~2.57 BCs (the highest peak), ~3.25 BCs, and ~3.83 BCs. Because the highest peak is at ~2.57 BCs rather than being a dominant Na+ peak at the start of a sodium hydroxide progression, it violates the core rules for '3-OH'.",
1506241569,31160,3-KNa,2.4452299587267648e-14,1018,3-KNa,34585,non-3-OH,3-OH,The spectrum has a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.76 µs followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 µs later at ~3.25 µs (along with a K+ peak at ~2.45 µs). This hydroxide pattern is further supported by subsequent cluster peaks at ~3.72 µs (m/z 81) and ~4.28 µs (m/z 103).,
1506241698,31272,5,3.755780002322531e-14,1018,5,2131,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.94 s, it is immediately followed by a broad K+ peak complex around 2.60–2.73 s (~0.66–0.79 s later). It completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.43 s (1.49 s after Na+).",
1506244885,33794,2,6.78571985385755e-14,1018,2,2165,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a water-ice hydronium cluster series with major peaks at ~1.92 5s, ~2.80 5s (the highest peak), ~3.46 5s, and ~4.03 5s. Because the highest peak is at ~2.80 5s rather than Na+ and the spectrum is dominated by closely spaced water clusters instead of an isolated Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 5s after Na+, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1506250000,37412,3-Cl,1.0515899810008625e-13,1018,3-Cl,34586,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.03 s followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.51 s (a time distance of 1.48 s). This sodium hydroxide series is further confirmed by additional cluster peaks at ~4.02 s (m/z 81, 0.51 s after m/z 63) and ~4.55 s (m/z 103, 1.04 s after m/z 63).",
1506250096,37483,3-K,1.6589399464057332e-14,1018,3-K,34359,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum has a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.60 µs, but lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ peak about 1.49 µs later (at ~3.09 µs). Instead, the only distinct secondary peak appears at ~3.70 µs (~2.10 µs after Na+, likely Na(NaCl)+ at m/z 81 without m/z 63), ruling out the 3-OH class.",
1506250784,37523,4,8.999000004374091e-14,1018,4,2236,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is located at approximately 0.28 µs (with another nearly equal broad peak at ~3.37 µs), rather than a dominant Na+ peak in the 1.4–2.0 µs range. Furthermore, the spectrum exhibits a complex mineral or organic pattern with broad peaks at ~2.40 µs, ~3.37 µs, and ~4.65 µs instead of a sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1506291382,41934,3-Car,1.3961500412804778e-13,1018,3-Car,34587,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The highest peak is a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.94 µs, followed by a Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.42 µs (a distance of ~1.48 µs, matching the expected 1.49 µs rule) despite the rising baseline. A small secondary peak at ~4.45 µs (~2.51 µs after Na+) also aligns with the Na(NaOH)2+ position.",
1506294897,42098,5,1.0768000362627438e-14,1018,5,2347,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum features a highest peak at ~1.16 s (likely a shifted Na+ peak) followed by a second major peak at ~1.84 s (a separation of ~0.68 s, corresponding to K+), and completely lacks any Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 s after either peak (at ~2.65 s or ~3.33 s).",
1506298659,42239,5,3.9117099587693965e-14,1018,5,2376,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum features a broad highest peak around 2.02 s followed by another major peak at ~2.70 s (only ~0.68 s later, typical of K+ or water clusters). It lacks a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at the required ~1.49 s interval (~3.51 s), confirming a non-3-OH classification.",
1506304493,42414,5,7.528209961882651e-14,1018,5,2401,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a strong Na+ peak at ~1.98 5s, but the highest peak is a broad K+ peak complex reaching maximum amplitude at ~2.78 5s (about 0.80 5s after Na+). Furthermore, there is no Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.47 5s (~1.49 5s after Na+), violating both required rules for a 3-OH classification.",
1506304548,42416,3-K,3.1125299684636384e-14,1018,3-K,34588,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The dominant peak is located unusually late at approximately 2.46 s, and no peak appears at the expected 1.49 s interval for Na(NaOH)+ (around 3.95 s). Instead, the subsequent cluster peaks appear at approximately 4.13 s, 4.57 s, and 4.98 s (distances of ~1.67 s, ~2.11 s, and ~2.52 s after the main peak), indicating a different salt composition such as NaCl/Na2CO3 rather than sodium hydroxide.",
1506306997,42482,3-Cl,1.3279599587936314e-13,1018,3-Cl,34589,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.90 s followed by a Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.38 s (a time distance of 1.48 s), despite an elevated baseline. A secondary cluster peak is also visible at ~3.92 s (~0.54 s after the m/z 63 peak), supporting the 3-OH classification.",
1506309469,42529,3-KNa,7.572900097806146e-14,1018,3-KNa,34590,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.88 BCs followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.37 BCs, which corresponds to the expected diagnostic spacing of 1.49 BCs (despite an intermediate K+ peak at ~2.56 BCs).",
1543798599,21697,3-OH,2.184520061588105e-13,1018,3-OH,34716,3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.04 Us, followed ~1.49 Us later by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.53 Us and a small Na(NaOH)2+ peak at ~4.57 Us (~2.53 Us after Na+). Despite the elevated baseline after the Na+ peak, this exact spacing matches the sodium hydroxide cluster rules for '3-OH'.",
1543799120,22218,3-P,6.385830178447932e-14,1018,3-P,34717,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ base peak at approximately 2.00 µs followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at approximately 3.47 µs, matching the required 1.49 µs time separation within the ±0.1 µs tolerance.",
1543799174,22272,3-OH,1.906669944541986e-13,1018,3-OH,34718,3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.05 s (preceded by a smaller H3O+ peak at ~1.80 s), followed ~1.49 s later by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.54 s. A secondary Na(NaOH)2+ peak at ~4.60 s (~2.55 s after Na+) further confirms the sodium hydroxide series despite the elevated baseline.",
1543799233,22331,3-P,2.546279972894666e-13,1018,3-P,34719,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although a main doublet peak appears around 2.00-2.12 Γs with a single peak about 1.44 Γs later at 3.56 Γs, the spectrum is dominated by an early peak at 0.25 Γs, a rising organic/mineral baseline, and late peaks at 5.88 Γs and 6.27 Γs rather than a clean sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1543799272,22370,1,1.5962100415847953e-14,1018,1,17781,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is a water-ice spectrum where the highest peak is H3O+ at ~1.60 µs (with a smaller Na+ peak at ~1.80 µs), followed by a regularly spaced hydronium-water cluster series at ~2.41 µs, ~3.05 µs, and ~3.58 µs rather than a Na(NaOH)+ peak 1.49 µs after Na+.",
1543799319,22417,2,2.610630082337112e-14,1018,2,17788,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because it shows a classic water-ice hydronium cluster series with major peaks at ~2.25 µs, ~3.05 µs (the highest peak), ~3.70 µs, and ~4.30 µs, rather than a dominant Na+ peak. Furthermore, the ~0.80 µs spacing between the initial peaks is inconsistent with the required 1.49 µs interval for a Na(NaOH)+ cluster.",
1543799384,22482,3-Car,1.3941899392778956e-13,1018,3-Car,34720,non-3-OH,3-OH,The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.12 bcms followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.61 bcms (1.49 bcms later). The sodium hydroxide progression is further confirmed by the second cluster peak Na(NaOH)2+ at ~4.62 bcms (2.50 bcms after Na+).,
1543799404,22502,Noise,4.4242401083839644e-14,1018,Noise,17796,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum consists of a noisy, continuously rising baseline from 0.1 to 6.4 s with an initial noise spike at ~0.15 s. It completely lacks a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 s and any subsequent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak 1.49 s later.",
1543799413,22511,5,2.8556201321769045e-14,1018,5,17799,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.94 s followed closely by a prominent K+ peak at ~2.63 s (a distance of ~0.69 s). It lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak expected ~1.49 s after Na+ (around 3.43 s), confirming a non-3-OH classification.",
1543799509,22607,3-Car,2.1530600381996362e-13,1018,3-Car,34721,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Instead of a single dominant Na+ peak, the spectrum shows a strong early peak at ~0.27 bc␀s, a broad multi-peak complex around 2.02–2.16 bc␀s, and another multi-peak complex at 3.50–3.67 bc␀s that reaches the same maximum amplitude of 1.0 upon an elevated baseline. This complex mineral-like profile lacks the clean Na+ and Na(NaOH)+ cluster progression required for a 3-OH classification.",
1543799747,22845,Noise,2.3353699548744715e-14,1018,Noise,17836,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum consists entirely of instrumental noise with a single narrow spike at ~0.14 5s, completely lacking a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 5s and any subsequent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 5s later.",
1543799804,22902,3-Car,1.5905000569620825e-13,1018,3-Car,34722,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because the highest ion peak is located at approximately 3.57 µs (with an initial artifact at 0.12 µs) rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 µs, violating Rule 1. Additionally, the double-peak structure at 1.80 µs and 2.08 µs followed by a doublet at 3.43 µs and 3.57 µs and an elevated baseline does not match the clean Na+ and Na(NaOH)+ hydroxide cluster progression.",
1543799886,22984,Noise,1.841659962552311e-13,1018,Noise,17852,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is dominated by a single very broad, asymmetric feature peaking around 2.53 5s rather than a sharp Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 5s. Furthermore, it completely lacks a distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak 1.49 5s later, showing only a decaying tail and noise.",
1543800078,23176,1,5.068049861614403e-14,1018,1,17877,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the highest peak lies near 1.82 µs, there is no Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak about 1.49 µs later at ~3.31 µs. Instead, the spectrum shows a mineral-rich pattern with prominent peaks at ~0.18 µs, ~2.60 µs, ~4.51 µs, and ~4.91 µs.",
1543800507,23604,3-Car,1.2183200141010347e-14,1018,3-Car,34723,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum features a very broad, Asymmetric main peak with a maximum at ~2.21 µs that tails heavily out to ~3.4 µs, rather than a sharp Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 µs. Although a minor peak appears at ~3.70 µs (~1.49 µs later), the anomalous shape and late position of the primary peak, along with an isolated peak at ~5.33 µs (~3.12 µs after the maximum), do not match the clean 3-OH sodium hydroxide cluster profile.",
1543800574,23671,3-K,7.600930112096685e-14,1018,3-K,34724,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum features a very broad main peak complex between 2.15 and 3.0 9s (peaking at ~2.35 9s) rather than a sharp Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 9s. Furthermore, the next broad peak at ~4.15 9s does not match the required 1.49 9s spacing for a Na(NaOH)+ cluster.",
1543800603,23700,1,1.2770000002912656e-14,1018,1,17944,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~1.62 Θ4s (likely H3O+ or Na+), but there is no Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 Θ4s later at ~3.11 Θ4s. Instead, the spectrum displays peaks at ~0.37 Θ4s, ~1.84 Θ4s, ~2.53 Θ4s, and ~4.36 Θ4s, which do not match the sodium hydroxide progression.",
1543800605,23702,2,1.6202700124515537e-14,1018,2,17945,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the highest peak is at ~1.61 µs, the spectrum completely lacks the diagnostic Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak expected ~1.49 µs later at ~3.10 µs. Instead, the subsequent peaks appear at ~1.81 µs, ~2.50 µs, and ~4.35 µs, which do not match the sodium hydroxide series.",
1543800692,23789,2,1.6010000129015184e-14,1018,2,17954,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the spectrum has a dominant peak at ~1.82 Ss, it is immediately followed by a dense series of broad peaks at ~2.03 Ss, ~2.25 Ss, and ~2.78 Ss (~0.96 Ss after the main peak), typical of water-ice or complex clusters rather than an isolated Na(NaOH)+ peak at ~3.31 Ss (1.49 Ss after Na+).",
1543800719,23816,3-Car,3.675849907661469e-14,1018,3-Car,34725,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.00 µs (forming a doublet with H3O+ at ~1.93 µs), followed ~1.47 µs later by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.47 µs. A secondary Na(NaOH)2+ cluster peak is also visible at ~4.49 µs (~2.49 µs after the Na+ peak), confirming the 3-OH classification.",
1543800978,24075,1,1.3307200156522595e-14,1018,1,17993,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the spectrum has a dominant peak at ~1.65 5s, it completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 5s later (around 3.14 5s). Instead, the subsequent major peaks appear at ~1.86 5s, ~2.55 5s, and ~4.38 5s, which does not match the sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1543801196,24292,1,1.5544599570212203e-14,1018,1,18018,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~1.60 s, but the characteristic Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak expected ~1.49 s later (around 3.09 s) is completely absent. Instead, the spectrum shows peaks at ~0.35 s, ~1.82 s, ~2.50 s, and ~4.35 s, which do not match the sodium hydroxide series.",
1543801234,24330,1,1.0512099850800653e-14,1018,1,18023,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the spectrum has a dominant peak at ~1.58 bcs (likely Na+), it completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 bcs later (around 3.07 bcs). Instead, the next prominent peak appears much later at ~4.32 bcs (a distance of ~2.74 bcs, likely Rh+ target ions), ruling out the 3-OH classification.",
1543801288,24384,2,1.910139933595026e-13,1018,2,18030,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum features a broad, double-humped main peak at ~2.22 s and ~2.35 s followed by a broad feature at ~3.10 s (only ~0.75-0.88 s later) on a heavily elevated, decaying baseline. It lacks a sharp Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 s and has no distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 s after the main peak.",
1543801543,24638,1,1.0768000362627438e-14,1018,1,18055,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the spectrum has a dominant peak at ~1.55 s (or a nearby secondary peak at ~1.77 s), it completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 s later (around 3.04–3.26 s). Instead, the subsequent major peaks appear at ~2.37 s, ~4.27 s, and ~4.68 s, which does not match the sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1543801596,24690,2,5.915819727532814e-14,1018,2,18061,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is located at approximately 0.22 bc	ext{s} (H+) rather than being a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 bc	ext{s}. Additionally, there is no Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak about 1.49 bc	ext{s} after the prominent peak at 1.80 bc	ext{s} (expected near 3.29 bc	ext{s}), with the next major peak appearing much later at 4.55 bc	ext{s}.",
1543801769,24861,1,2.9682999087106074e-14,1018,1,18077,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the spectrum has a dominant peak at ~1.72 s (consistent with Na+), it completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 s later at ~3.21 s. Instead, the subsequent major peaks appear at ~1.93 s, ~2.61 s, ~4.45 s, and ~4.87 s, which do not match the sodium hydroxide series.",
1543802106,25192,3-OH,1.494820028391866e-13,1018,3-OH,34727,3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum is dominated by a Na+ peak at ~1.97 µs, followed ~1.48 µs later by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ peak at ~3.45 µs (despite the elevated baseline). A secondary peak at ~4.50 µs (~2.53 µs after Na+) further supports the Na(NaOH)2+ hydroxide cluster series.",
1543802379,25461,2,1.2768699807338621e-14,1018,2,18137,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the spectrum has a dominant peak at ~1.65 5s, it completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 5s later (around 3.14 5s), showing only a flat baseline before a later peak at ~4.40 5s.",
1543802608,25685,3-Car,9.788690176351991e-14,1018,3-Car,34728,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.98 BCs, followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.45 BCs (a distance of 1.47 BCs, matching the expected 1.49 BCs spacing). This sodium hydroxide series is further confirmed by the second hydroxide cluster peak Na(NaOH)2+ at ~4.50 BCs (about 2.52 BCs after the Na+ peak).",
1543802725,25793,3-KNa,4.905700073053708e-14,1018,3-KNa,34729,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because its highest peak is a broad feature at ~2.69 µs rather than Na+ (which appears as a smaller peak at ~1.96 µs), violating Rule 1. Furthermore, it lacks a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at the expected ~1.49 µs interval (~3.45 µs), instead showing mineral or alternative salt peaks at ~0.16 µs, ~3.92 µs, ~4.35 µs, and ~4.73 µs.",
1543817721,29322,3-KNa,5.716090036196608e-14,1018,3-KNa,34730,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the spectrum has a highest peak at ~1.96 5s and a peak at ~3.45 5s (~1.49 5s later), the second largest peak is located at ~2.64 5s (~0.68 5s after the main peak), followed by a closely spaced series at ~3.95 5s, ~4.35 5s, and ~4.73 5s. This regular ~0.4-0.8 5s spacing is characteristic of a water-ice (hydronium cluster) or potassium-rich salt series rather than a clean sodium hydroxide pattern.",
1543820736,29790,3-Car,2.6347700131140912e-14,1018,3-Car,34731,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.93 s followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.42 s, exactly 1.49 s later. This sodium hydroxide series is further confirmed by the second hydroxide cluster peak Na(NaOH)2+ at ~4.47 s (~2.54 s after the Na+ peak).",
1543828209,30268,1,1.3119800046173212e-14,1018,1,34471,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a water-ice hydronium cluster progression with major peaks at ~1.43 s, ~2.24 s (the highest peak), and ~2.89 s. The peak spacing of ~0.81 s between the first two major peaks and the fact that the highest peak is at ~2.24 s without a subsequent peak 1.49 s later rules out the 3-OH sodium hydroxide pattern.",
1516086834,26354,3-Car,1.7480000397986604e-14,1018,3-Car,34647,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum features extremely broad, heavily tailing peaks with maxima at approximately 2.22 us, 3.68 us, and 5.33 us rather than a sharp Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 us. Furthermore, the third major peak at 5.33 us is 3.11 us after the main peak, which does not match the sodium hydroxide cluster series (where m/z 103 appears ~2.53 us after Na+).",
1516090316,29745,3-Car,3.064230116932125e-14,1018,3-Car,34648,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although a peak appears at ~3.67 s (approx. 1.50 s after the broad main peak at ~2.17 s), the spectrum is dominated by broad, heavily tailed peaks including an equally intense third major peak at ~5.28 s (~3.11 s after the main peak, which does not match m/z 81 or m/z 103). This broad, high-amplitude progression at 2.17, 3.67, and 5.28 s indicates another salt or mineral pattern rather than a sodium hydroxide series.",
1516093265,32579,5-Na,3.5481400396985066e-14,1018,5-Na,34780,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum features a single dominant Na+ peak at approximately 1.35 µs, followed by a featureless elevated baseline with no distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at the expected 1.49 µs interval (around 2.84 µs).",
1516105801,44680,3-KNa,3.083259897938319e-14,1018,3-KNa,34649,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is dominated by a primary peak at ~1.31 s followed closely by a major peak at ~2.01 s (a distance of ~0.70 s, typical of K+ or water-ice clusters), and lacks a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 s after the main peak ( shows only a minor bump near 2.81 s).",
1516106821,45369,4,6.41436028099053e-14,1018,4,4121,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because its highest peak is a broad feature at ~3.32 95s rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 95s, violating Rule 1. Instead of a sodium hydroxide cluster series, it displays a complex mineral or organic profile with multiple peaks at ~0.23 95s, ~1.33 95s, ~1.57 95s, ~2.32 95s, and ~4.59 95s.",
1516285014,24957,3-Cl,1.2500799549154673e-13,1018,3-Cl,34650,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.00 bcS followed by a clear Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.48 bcS (1.48 bcS later), satisfying both required rules for a 3-OH classification. This hydroxide series is further confirmed by a prominent hydrated cluster peak Na(NaOH)(H2O)+ at ~4.00 bcS (0.52 bcS after the m/z 63 peak).",
1516288425,25056,3-Cl,1.1965199610188687e-13,1018,3-Cl,34651,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at approximately 1.90 µs, followed about 1.48 µs later by a clear Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at 3.38 µs (superimposed on a rising baseline). A smaller hydrated cluster peak is also visible at around 3.90 µs (about 0.52 µs after the m/z 63 peak), confirming the 3-OH signature.",
1519489376,44970,5-Na,2.0208500197131836e-14,1018,5-Na,34840,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum features a single dominant Na+ peak at ~1.39 bcs, followed by an elevated, featureless baseline starting around 2.5 bcs. It completely lacks a distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at the required 1.49 bcs interval (~2.88 bcs), ruling out the 3-OH classification.",
1519522073,9704,3-Car,5.654450093372197e-14,1018,3-Car,34652,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.90 µs, followed ~1.48 µs later by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.38 µs. This signature is further supported by a secondary Na(NaOH)2+ cluster peak at ~4.42 µs (~2.52 µs after the Na+ peak), clearly matching the 3-OH hydroxide series.",
1519522204,9820,3-K,8.170210113924575e-14,1018,3-K,34653,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is located at approximately 2.57 µs (unusually late for Na+), and the next prominent peak appears at 4.65 µs, which is a time distance of ~2.08 µs rather than the ~1.49 µs spacing required for a Na(NaOH)+ cluster.",
1519522432,10024,3-KNa,3.043290107223283e-14,1018,3-KNa,34654,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although there is a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.66 µs followed by a smaller peak at ~3.12 µs (~1.46 µs later) and a target Rh+ peak at ~4.15 µs, the spectrum after Na+ is dominated by a stronger K+ peak at ~2.37 µs (~0.71 µs after Na+) along with an elevated baseline, indicating a potassium-rich salt grain rather than a clean sodium hydroxide series.",
1519537838,12034,3-Car,1.3249400491674446e-13,1018,3-Car,34655,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the highest peak is near 2.05 µs with a subsequent broad feature near 3.55 µs (~1.50 µs later), the spectrum is dominated by broad, sawtooth-shaped periodic oscillations repeating again at ~5.15 µs on a heavily elevated baseline (~0.75), rather than the sharp Na+ and Na(NaOH)+ cluster peaks characteristic of 3-OH spectra.",
1519552726,14957,3-OH,1.1673900236243429e-13,1018,3-OH,34656,3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.98 9cs followed by a clear Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.46 9cs (a time distance of ~1.48 9cs, matching the expected 1.49 9cs spacing), along with a weak secondary cluster peak near 4.50 9cs.",
1519553559,15667,3-Cl,2.710279917161884e-13,1018,3-Cl,34657,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.96 s followed by a clear Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.48 s later at ~3.44 s, despite the rising baseline. A small hydrated hydroxide cluster peak at ~3.95 s (~0.51 s after m/z 63) further supports the 3-OH classification.",
1519554583,16648,3-Car,1.1983999675859586e-13,1018,3-Car,34658,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum lacks a dominant, narrow Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 9cs; instead, the first peak at ~2.22 9cs is immediately overshadowed by a broad base peak at ~2.49 9cs. Even though broad peaks appear later at ~3.96 9cs and ~5.60 9cs, this wide, elevated-baseline profile with near-equal amplitudes (~0.97) does not match the clean Na+ and Na(NaOH)+ cluster progression of a 3-OH spectrum.",
1519555993,18005,4,4.753990170275335e-13,1018,4,4123,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as non-3-OH because the highest peak is a broad feature reaching maximum amplitude at approximately 3.62 s rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 s. Additionally, it displays a complex mineral-like profile with prominent peaks at ~0.38 s, ~1.42 s, ~1.65 s, ~2.33 s, and ~4.88 s, lacking the characteristic 1.49 s Na(NaOH)+ cluster spacing.",
1519556386,18385,4,1.7480000397986604e-14,1018,4,4124,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~1.93 s, preceded by peaks at ~1.22 s and ~1.48 s, and followed by a major peak at ~2.61 s (~0.68 s later). Regardless of whether the ~1.48 s or ~1.93 s peak is Na+, the spectrum lacks a prominent Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 s after the highest peak (expected at ~3.42 s).",
1519557444,19329,3-Cl,9.815709849743046e-14,1018,3-Cl,34659,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a very broad, complex main peak around 2.15 us with a long decaying tail, followed by broad peaks at ~3.61 us, ~4.15 us, and ~5.45 us (where the 4.15 us peak is higher than the 3.61 us peak, likely representing Na2Cl+ at m/z 81 rather than a sodium hydroxide series). This broad, chloride-dominated or mineral-like profile does not match the clean Na(NaOH)n+ cluster progression required for 3-OH.",
1519558100,19924,3-Car,5.215960042354029e-13,1018,3-Car,34660,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum exhibits a severe baseline step starting around 1.65 µs with the highest peak located late at ~2.20 µs, followed by weak peaks on the elevated baseline at ~2.89 µs, ~3.62 µs, and ~5.23 µs. Although the spacing from 2.20 µs to 3.62 µs is 1.42 µs, the gradual step-like rise from 1.65 µs to 2.20 µs and the prominent peak at 2.89 µs (~0.69 µs later) indicate a saturated salt/mineral or K+-rich profile rather than a clean 3-OH sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1519558970,20719,4,4.845279857673343e-14,1018,4,4125,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as non-3-OH because the highest peak is at ~0.21 5s (likely H+) rather than a dominant Na+ peak in the 1.4-2.0 5s range. Instead of a clean sodium hydroxide series, it displays a complex mineral/organic pattern with major peaks at ~1.33 5s, ~2.03 5s, ~3.28 5s, and ~4.55 5s.",
1519560464,22112,3-KNa,9.818900114635584e-14,1018,3-KNa,34661,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum has a dominant peak at ~1.64 µs followed by a prominent second peak at ~2.33 µs (0.69 µs later, likely K+), and then a high, rising baseline with only a very weak feature near ~3.13 µs. Because the main secondary peak is at 0.69 µs rather than a clear, isolated Na(NaOH)+ cluster series at ~1.49 µs after Na+, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1519563728,25194,3-KNa,4.868809890846981e-13,1018,3-KNa,34662,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.03 s (with K+ at ~2.68 s) followed ~1.45 s later by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.48 s and a hydrated Na(NaOH)(H2O)+ peak ~0.50 s after that at ~3.98 s, matching the 3-OH signature despite an elevated baseline.",
1519564769,26183,5-Na,7.672780190067299e-14,1018,5-Na,34781,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum features a single dominant Na+ peak at ~1.50 µs, followed by a gradually rising, featureless baseline that reaches ~0.7 amplitude by 3.5 µs. Because it completely lacks a distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at the required ~1.49 µs interval after Na+ (expected around 2.99 µs), it is classified as 'non-3-OH'.",
1519567049,28350,3-OH,2.568139928146862e-13,1018,3-OH,34663,3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the spectrum has a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.93 µs followed by a smaller K+ peak at ~2.68 µs, it lacks a distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at the expected ~3.42 µs position (1.49 µs after Na+), showing instead a featureless, elevated baseline starting near 3.38 µs.",
1519573094,34072,3-Cl,1.282960012099349e-13,1018,3-Cl,34664,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the spectrum displays a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.92 µs, it lacks a distinct, narrow Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at the expected ~1.49 µs interval (~3.41 µs). Instead, it shows only a broad, featureless baseline hump rising between 3.0 and 5.0 µs with no resolved hydroxide cluster series.",
1519575898,34793,3-Car,5.907940288244276e-14,1018,3-Car,34665,non-3-OH,3-OH,The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.93 s followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.42 s (1.49 s later). This sodium hydroxide series is further supported by a secondary Na(NaOH)2+ peak at ~4.45 s (~2.52 s after Na+).,
1519576247,35128,3-KNa,7.236249902238534e-14,1018,3-KNa,34666,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~2.73 µs (likely K+ or a water cluster) rather than the initial peak at ~2.09 µs, violating Rule 1. Even if the ~2.09 µs peak is Na+, the spectrum is dominated by the peak 0.64 µs later (~2.73 µs) rather than a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak 1.49 µs later.",
1519578741,37548,3-Cl,1.4158899747096498e-13,1018,3-Cl,34667,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because its highest peak is located at ~4.32 µs rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 µs, violating Rule 1. Furthermore, the complex series of broad peaks at ~2.41 µs, ~3.78 µs, ~4.32 µs, and ~5.61 µs does not match the clean sodium hydroxide cluster progression.",
1519580704,39457,3-K,2.284830040010649e-14,1018,3-K,34668,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~2.38 9cs, and the next major peaks appear at ~4.05 9cs (1.67 9cs later) and ~4.48 9cs (2.10 9cs later), which corresponds to a sodium chloride (Na(NaCl)+ at m/z 81) series rather than the required Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 9cs after Na+.",
1519580718,39471,3-K,1.2117599980344344e-14,1018,3-K,34365,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~0.15 s rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 s, with secondary peaks at ~1.7 s and ~2.18 s. Additionally, there is no Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak following ~1.49 s after any of the peaks in the 1.7–2.2 s region, with only baseline noise beyond 2.5 s.",
1519581683,40409,3-Cl,6.094379693824883e-14,1018,3-Cl,34669,non-3-OH,3-OH,The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.90 µs followed by a clear Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.47 µs later at ~3.37 µs. This sodium hydroxide pattern is further confirmed by the hydrated cluster peak Na(NaOH)(H2O)+ at ~3.88 µs (~0.51 µs after the m/z 63 peak).,
1519584354,43012,3-OH,6.963650305263219e-14,1018,3-OH,34670,3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at approximately 1.90 bc	ext{s} followed by a distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at approximately 3.38 bc	ext{s}, which matches the expected 1.49 bc	ext{s} separation.",
1519585197,43837,3-Car,1.0864800134872607e-13,1018,3-Car,34671,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum lacks a narrow, dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 6s, instead showing a broad maximum around 2.57 6s preceded by a shoulder at 2.35 6s. Furthermore, the next prominent peak at 3.83 6s does not match the required 1.49 6s spacing from the main peak (it is 1.26 6s after 2.57 6s) and the overall broad, tailing profile does not match the clean sodium hydroxide cluster pattern.",
1519585629,44257,3-OH,1.6481199814188247e-13,1018,3-OH,34672,3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the spectrum displays a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.98 µs and a small feature at ~3.45 µs, it is dominated by a severe baseline overshoot that remains elevated near 0.7-0.8 amplitude, lacking the well-resolved Na(NaOH)+ cluster pattern of a 3-OH spectrum.",
1519591581,49330,Noise,1.250710011902953e-13,1018,Noise,4185,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,The spectrum consists entirely of instrumental noise with a rising baseline and a single sharp spike at ~0.13 µs. It lacks both a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 µs and a subsequent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak 1.49 µs later.,
