1521629068,58543,3-Car,2.8489499171238664e-13,1018,3-Car,34681,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum exhibits a severe baseline overshoot after the peak at ~2.09 µs, causing the broad feature at ~3.53 µs to reach the maximum amplitude of 1.0 instead of a dominant, clean Na+ peak. Furthermore, the presence of a K+ peak at ~2.76 µs and the elevated, distorted baseline do not match the clean sodium hydroxide cluster progression of a '3-OH' grain.",
1521629346,58699,5,4.4019899081123096e-14,1018,5,10897,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is not the Na+ peak at ~1.88 s, but rather a dominant broad K+ peak at ~2.60 s (~0.72 s after Na+). Furthermore, the spectrum lacks the characteristic Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak expected ~1.49 s after Na+ (around 3.37 s).",
1521630166,59208,3-Car,2.7879799773607335e-14,1018,3-Car,34682,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum features a very broad, long-tailed primary peak at ~2.35 µs (outside the typical 1.4–2.0 µs range for a sharp Na+ peak), followed by broad, asymmetric peaks at ~3.83 µs and ~5.42 µs. Although the ~1.48 µs spacing to the second peak is close to 1.49 µs, the third peak appears ~3.07 µs after the main peak rather than at the expected ~2.53 µs for Na(NaOH)2+, indicating a non-3-OH composition.",
1521632381,60593,3-Car,1.8084099213770688e-14,1018,3-Car,34683,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum lacks a clean, narrow Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 s, instead showing a very broad feature peaking around 2.15 s (with a shoulder at ~1.85 s) and broad humps at ~3.63 s and ~5.25 s. This broad, overlapping peak profile does not match the well-resolved Na+ and Na(NaOH)+ cluster series required for a 3-OH classification.",
1521632601,60725,3-Car,1.7136799588418107e-14,1018,3-Car,34684,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although a dominant peak at ~2.20 s is followed ~1.42 s later by a peak at ~3.62 s, these peaks are extremely broad and heavily tailed, and the next major peak at ~5.22 s (a distance of ~3.02 s after the first peak) does not match the sodium hydroxide cluster series, indicating a different salt or mineral composition.",
1521633722,61416,3-KNa,1.953749933104182e-13,1018,3-KNa,34685,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum lacks a clean, dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 s, instead starting with a broad, complex feature reaching maximum amplitude at ~2.45 s and another equally high peak at ~4.40 s. If the main peak at ~2.45 s were Na+, a Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak would be expected at ~3.94 s (which shows a peak at ~3.90 s), but the overall profile is a broad, elevated mineral/organic or complex salt spectrum with intermediate features at ~3.10 s and a dominant peak at ~4.40 s that violates the 3-OH criteria.",
1521634679,61990,3-KNa,7.801659979937009e-14,1018,3-KNa,34686,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is not the initial peak at 1.98 s, but rather a dominant double peak at ~2.68 s (only 0.70 s later), which violates Rule 1 and is characteristic of a water-ice or potassium-rich spectrum. Although minor peaks follow at 3.48 s, 3.96 s, 4.35 s, and 4.75 s, the dominance of the 2.68 s peak rules out the '3-OH' sodium hydroxide classification.",
1521635331,62368,3-Car,4.6433898935084594e-14,1018,3-Car,34687,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.93 5s followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.41 5s (a time distance of 1.48 5s, matching the expected 1.49 5s interval). This sodium hydroxide series is further confirmed by the second cluster peak Na(NaOH)2+ at ~4.45 5s (~2.52 5s after Na+).",
1521635380,62399,3-Cl,5.387319957543893e-14,1018,3-Cl,34688,non-3-OH,3-OH,The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.98 s followed ~1.46 s later by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.44 s. This sodium hydroxide pattern is further confirmed by the hydrated cluster peak at ~3.97 s (~0.53 s after the 3.44 s peak) and the second hydroxide cluster peak at ~4.48 s.,
1521635983,62748,3-Cl,7.802120088233958e-14,1018,3-Cl,34689,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.90 5s followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.37 5s (a time distance of ~1.47 5s, matching the expected 1.49 5s rule). This signature is further confirmed by the hydrated hydroxide cluster peak at ~3.88 5s (~0.51 5s after the m/z 63 peak).",
1521636311,62934,3-Cl,1.7401299856351776e-13,1018,3-Cl,34690,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.98 5s followed by a distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.47 5s later at ~3.45 5s, and a subsequent hydrated hydroxide peak at ~3.95 5s (~0.50 5s after the m/z 63 peak), clearly matching the 3-OH signature despite the elevated baseline.",
1521637849,63776,3-Car,2.289029968176315e-14,1018,3-Car,34691,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is a broad feature at ~5.40 5s rather than a sharp Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 5s (violating Rule 1). Even if the broad first peak at ~2.18 5s is considered alongside the second peak at ~3.70 5s, the extreme peak widths and dominant ~5.40 5s peak do not match the sharp sodium hydroxide cluster progression.",
1521638150,63937,3-Car,2.3687098831860764e-13,1018,3-Car,34692,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.10 s followed by a distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.57 s, which matches the expected ~1.49 s time distance. A smaller secondary hydroxide cluster peak Na(NaOH)2+ is also visible at ~4.60 s (~2.50 s after Na+), confirming the 3-OH classification despite the elevated baseline.",
1521639166,64475,3-Cl,1.7900400129181038e-13,1018,3-Cl,34693,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The highest peak is Na+ at ~1.98 bcS, followed by the Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.42 bcS (a distance of 1.44 bcS, within the 1.49 b1 0.1 bcS rule). Additionally, a hydrated cluster peak at m/z 81 appears at ~3.97 bcS (~0.55 bcS after the m/z 63 peak), confirming the 3-OH classification despite the rising baseline.",
1521639305,64551,3-Car,7.485339930356216e-14,1018,3-Car,34694,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the spectrum has a broad highest peak at ~2.12 BCs and a large peak at ~3.53 BCs (1.41 BCs later), the profile is dominated by broad, asymmetric peaks with additional major peaks at ~3.00 BCs, ~4.12 BCs, and ~5.17 BCs, which do not match the narrow sodium hydroxide cluster series (expected at ~1.99 BCs and ~2.53 BCs after Na+).",
1521639622,64714,3-KNa,4.63856004388058e-13,1018,3-KNa,34695,non-3-OH,3-OH,"Despite the elevated baseline, the spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.15 s (split with H3O+ at ~2.04 s) followed ~1.49 s later by a sharp Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.64 s. The sodium hydroxide pattern is further supported by a subsequent peak at ~4.07 s (~0.43 s after m/z 63) and K+ at ~2.84 s.",
1521639847,64830,3-Car,5.083150087371695e-14,1018,3-Car,34696,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.01 BCs followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.48 BCs (a distance of 1.47 BCs, matching the expected 1.49 BCs rule). Additional hydroxide cluster peaks at ~4.06 BCs (m/z 81) and ~4.52 BCs (m/z 103) further confirm the 3-OH classification.",
1521639955,64893,5,2.1403699261091438e-14,1018,5,11018,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant peak at ~1.84 s (either H3O+ or Na+) followed closely by a very strong peak at ~2.50 s (a time distance of only ~0.66 s, corresponding to K+ or H3O+(H2O)+). Although there are tiny features near ~3.30 s and ~3.80 s, the spectrum after the main peak is dominated by the peak at ~2.50 s rather than a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster series.",
1521642075,334,3-KNa,1.19908003339865e-13,1018,3-KNa,34697,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak at ~1.98 s is followed by a major peak at ~2.66 s (only ~0.68 s later, characteristic of K+ or water-ice clusters rather than the required 1.49 s spacing for Na(NaOH)+). Although a minor feature appears near ~3.45 s, the spectrum is dominated by the peak at 2.66 s and an elevated baseline, ruling out a 3-OH classification.",
1521642257,408,3-P,5.913189859638179e-14,1018,3-P,34698,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although there is a broad peak complex with a maximum at ~2.00 us and another broad peak at ~3.42 us (1.42 us later), the spectrum is dominated by broad, split peaks (~1.85 and ~2.00 us) and late mineral/salt features (~4.98, ~5.76, and ~6.15 us) rather than a clean, narrow Na+ and sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1521642936,699,2,1.3206099998004216e-14,1018,2,11050,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~2.52 s rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 s, and the spectrum shows a dense series of water-ice or complex cluster peaks (at ~1.80, 2.20, 2.52, 3.15, and 3.70 s) instead of an isolated Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 s after Na+.",
1521645338,1513,5,2.4594899278003804e-14,1018,5,11077,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.83 µs followed closely by a strong K+ peak at ~2.50 µs (a distance of ~0.67 µs). It completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak expected ~1.49 µs after the Na+ peak (around 3.32 µs).,
1521648163,2283,3-Car,6.622140173457441e-14,1018,3-Car,34699,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is dominated by broad, heavily tailed peaks with maxima at approximately 2.38 s, 3.68 s (a distance of ~1.30 s), and 5.29 s (~2.91 s after the first peak). It lacks a narrow Na+ peak in the typical 1.4–2.0 s range and does not follow the characteristic 1.49 s spacing of the Na(NaOH)+ cluster series.",
1521649222,2510,3-KNa,1.5461400606001097e-13,1018,3-KNa,34700,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.00 s followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.47 s later at ~3.47 s, along with a hydrated cluster peak at ~3.98 s (~0.51 s after m/z 63). Even with a K+ peak present at ~2.68 s, this clear sodium hydroxide cluster series confirms the '3-OH' classification.",
1521650454,2743,5,1.484169944332859e-14,1018,5,11141,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum features two main peaks at approximately 0.93 µs and 1.62 µs (separated by only ~0.69 µs, consistent with an early-arriving Na+ and K+ pair) and completely lacks any subsequent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak 1.49 µs after either peak (expected at ~2.42 µs or ~3.11 µs).",
1521654821,3132,3-Car,4.19615005990779e-14,1018,3-Car,34702,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although there is a broad peak at ~2.03 s and another at ~3.53 s (~1.50 s later), the spectrum is dominated by unusually broad peaks including a massive peak at ~5.16 s (~3.13 s after the first peak), which is inconsistent with the narrow peak profile and cluster mass progression of a 3-OH sodium hydroxide series.",
1521655209,3239,3-Car,1.298940017097636e-14,1018,3-Car,34703,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the spectrum shows broad, heavily tailing peaks at ~1.90 µs and ~3.38 µs, the subsequent major peak appears at ~5.05 µs (~3.15 µs after the first peak) rather than following the sodium hydroxide cluster series at m/z 81 (~3.89 µs) or m/z 103 (~4.43 µs), indicating a different salt or non-3-OH composition.",
1521656862,3599,5,1.964599916938741e-14,1018,5,11283,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~2.38 µs (likely K+, appearing ~0.70 µs after the Na+ peak at ~1.68 µs), violating Rule 1. Furthermore, there is no Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 µs after the Na+ peak (around 3.17 µs).",
1521657297,3692,3-K,1.1815499750475467e-14,1018,3-K,34369,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum has a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.76 µs, but lacks a prominent Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 µs later (at ~3.25 µs). Instead, the main subsequent peaks appear at ~3.84 µs (Na(NaCl)+, ~2.08 µs after Na+) and ~4.22 µs, indicating a chloride-dominated salt pattern rather than sodium hydroxide.",
1521657682,3772,5,1.8235199727165488e-14,1018,5,11327,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because the highest peak is a dominant K+ peak at ~2.22 5s rather than the Na+ peak at ~1.52 5s (a separation of ~0.70 5s). Additionally, it completely lacks a Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at the expected distance of ~1.49 5s after the Na+ peak (around 3.01 5s).",
1521657688,3774,3-Cl,1.2196800102011462e-14,1018,3-Cl,34704,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.22 s followed ~1.49 s later by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.71 s. This sodium hydroxide signature is further confirmed by the hydrated cluster peak at ~4.27 s (~0.56 s after the 3.71 s peak), matching the 3-OH rules.",
1521658289,3903,3-KNa,2.0679299743940616e-13,1018,3-KNa,34705,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The highest peak is Na+ at approximately 2.01 µs (with a K+ peak at ~2.70 µs), followed by a distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.51 µs (a time distance of 1.50 µs). This hydroxide pattern is further supported by a hydrated cluster peak at ~4.05 µs (about 2.04 µs after Na+), confirming the 3-OH classification despite the elevated baseline.",
1521660414,4272,3-Car,7.245769874939315e-14,1018,3-Car,34706,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a broad highest peak at approximately 2.33 µs (outside the typical 1.4-2.0 µs range for sharp Na+) with subsequent broad peaks at ~3.80 µs and ~5.42 µs. Although the spacing between the first two peaks is ~1.47 µs, the third peak is ~3.09 µs after the first peak, which corresponds to a NaCl cluster series (m/z 81 at +1.99 µs or m/z 139 at +3.32 µs) or instrumental/mineral broadening rather than the narrow Na(NaOH)n+ hydroxide series.",
1521661907,4488,3-K,1.641879991340356e-13,1018,3-K,34707,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is a broad double-peaked feature around 2.67–2.75 5s (outside the typical 1.4–2.0 5s Na+ range), and the subsequent peaks at ~4.35 5s, ~4.82 5s, and ~5.23 5s (about 1.60–1.68 5s, 2.07–2.15 5s, and 2.48–2.56 5s later, with the 4.82 5s peak being much stronger than the 4.35 5s peak) represent other salts such as NaCl clusters rather than the characteristic 3-OH sodium hydroxide series.",
1521662347,4569,2,4.6282900065643465e-14,1018,2,11490,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a water-ice hydronium cluster series with major peaks at ~1.62 9s, ~2.50 9s (highest peak), ~3.18 9s, and ~3.73 9s. The highest peak is at ~2.50 9s and the ~0.88 9s spacing between the first two major peaks does not match the required 1.49 9s separation for a Na(NaOH)+ cluster.",
1521663276,4721,5-Na,2.365690109085161e-13,1018,5-Na,34783,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,The spectrum shows a single dominant Na+ peak at approximately 1.67 Δs followed by a severe baseline overshoot that climbs to ~0.9 amplitude. It is classified as 'non-3-OH' because it completely lacks a distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at the expected 1.49 Δs interval after the Na+ peak (around 3.16 Δs).,
1521663324,4726,3-KNa,2.365690109085161e-13,1018,3-KNa,34708,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at approximately 2.08 µs, followed about 1.47 µs later by a distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.55 µs (riding on an elevated baseline after a K+ peak at ~2.73 µs). A smaller hydrated cluster peak Na(NaOH)(H2O)+ is also visible at ~3.98 µs (~1.90 µs after Na+), confirming the sodium hydroxide series.",
1521663821,4797,5-Na,2.431359963622065e-13,1018,5-Na,34784,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum features a single dominant Na+ peak at ~1.88 5s followed by a broad, featureless baseline overshoot that remains elevated near 0.8 amplitude. It is classified as 'non-3-OH' because it completely lacks a distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at the expected ~3.37 5s position (1.49 5s after Na+).",
1521663943,4817,3-KNa,6.362620120440449e-14,1018,3-KNa,34709,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although there is a peak at ~1.90 5s and another at ~3.35 5s (1.45 5s later), the spectrum is dominated by a very strong secondary peak at ~2.58 5s (only ~0.68 5s after the first peak), which indicates a water-ice hydronium cluster series (H3O+(H2O)n) or a K+ dominated salt rather than a clean sodium hydroxide pattern.",
1521666363,5146,5-Na,1.3234300265917154e-13,1018,5-Na,34786,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at approximately 1.71 Scs, it is followed only by a broad, featureless baseline hump rising near 3.0 Scs rather than a distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak expected around 3.20 Scs (1.49 Scs later).",
1521667470,5276,2,5.372209906204413e-14,1018,2,11618,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a classic water-ice pattern dominated by a regularly spaced hydronium cluster series with major peaks at ~1.98 µs, ~2.68 µs, ~3.26 µs, ~3.80 µs, and ~4.33 µs. Because the peak spacing is ~0.6-0.7 µs rather than the diagnostic 1.49 µs interval required for Na(NaOH)+ after a dominant Na+ peak, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1521672105,5573,3-K,4.6131799552248665e-14,1018,3-K,34710,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The dominant peak appears late at approximately 2.62 s (split with a shoulder at 2.55 s), which is outside the typical 1.4–2.0 s range for Na+. Even if this main peak were shifted Na+, the subsequent cluster peaks at ~4.22 s (+1.60 s), ~4.66 s (+2.04 s), and ~5.08 s (+2.46 s) show a larger peak-to-peak spacing and inverted intensity profile characteristic of other salt clusters (such as chloride/potassium) rather than the 1.49 s Na(NaOH)+ pattern.",
1521673790,5712,3-Car,8.109790237357389e-14,1018,3-Car,34711,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.98 s followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.47 s (a time distance of 1.49 s), along with a secondary Na(NaOH)2+ cluster peak at ~4.51 s (2.53 s after Na+), matching the characteristic 3-OH signature.",
1521674679,5777,3-Car,1.368089940379652e-13,1018,3-Car,34712,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum lacks a sharp Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 s, instead showing a very broad maximum centered around 2.6 s followed by other wide, wave-like features at ~4.1 s and ~5.8 s. This broad profile does not match the narrow Na+ and Na(NaOH)+ cluster pattern required for a '3-OH' label.",
1521675396,5841,3-Car,4.832970097257486e-14,1018,3-Car,34713,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is dominated by broad, complex peaks starting with a main peak at ~2.30 µs (with a shoulder at ~2.12 µs), followed by major peaks at ~3.15 µs, ~3.73 µs, ~4.35 µs, and ~5.35 µs. This broad, multi-peak pattern (likely from other salts such as NaCl or carbonates/organics) does not match the sharp, clean Na+ and Na(NaOH)+ hydroxide cluster series.",
1521675967,5877,5,6.948550079505927e-14,1018,5,11734,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a strong Na+ peak at ~2.03 µs followed closely by a slightly higher K+ peak at ~2.71 µs (a distance of ~0.68 µs). It is classified as 'non-3-OH' because the highest peak is K+ rather than Na+, and it completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak about 1.49 µs after the Na+ peak (around 3.52 µs).",
1521684294,6284,3-KNa,7.21660009311495e-14,1018,3-KNa,34714,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is dominated by two co-equal major peaks at ~1.87 µs and ~2.53 µs (separated by only ~0.66 µs, typical of a K+ or water-ice peak rather than the 1.49 µs Na(NaOH)+ spacing), with the peak at ~2.53 µs reaching the maximum amplitude of 1.0. Because the highest peak is not an isolated Na+ peak followed predominantly by a sodium hydroxide series, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1521743571,6657,3-K,1.0405700145944483e-13,1018,3-K,34715,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is located at approximately 2.57 5s (outside the typical 1.4-2.0 5s range for Na+) and the next prominent peak appears at 4.70 5s, a distance of 2.13 5s rather than the required 1.49 5s for a Na(NaOH)+ cluster (expected around 4.06 5s).",
1524914473,11536,4,9.597979962888692e-13,1018,4,11880,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as non-3-OH because the highest peak is not a clean Na+ peak in the 1.4-2.0 µs range, but rather a broad mineral-like complex peaking around 2.2-2.4 µs, accompanied by prominent peaks at ~0.4 µs, ~1.45 µs, ~1.65 µs, ~3.15 µs, and ~5.0 µs without the characteristic 1.49 µs Na(NaOH)+ spacing.",
1524933597,28739,4,1.2372200296597094e-14,1018,4,11882,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~1.78 9cs, followed by major peaks at ~2.46 9cs (~0.68 9cs later) and ~3.01 9cs (~1.23 9cs later), which corresponds to a water-ice or potassium-rich series rather than a sodium hydroxide pattern. There is no Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at the required ~1.49 9cs interval (~3.27 9cs).",
1524940762,35594,4,2.2294200245132935e-14,1018,4,11883,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a complex mineral or organic pattern with early peaks at 0.18, 1.28, and 1.52 µs before the main peak at 1.98 µs, rather than a clean Na+ signature. Furthermore, there is no Na(NaOH)+ peak at ~3.47 µs (1.49 µs after the 1.98 µs peak), with major peaks instead appearing at 2.30, 2.65, and 3.20 µs.",
1524960965,41619,5-Na,4.3319101290014567e-14,1018,5-Na,34788,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the spectrum displays a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.48 5s, it lacks a distinct, well-resolved Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak expected ~1.49 5s later at ~2.97 5s. Instead, it only shows a broad, featureless baseline hump rising between 2.2 5s and 4.5 5s.",
1524974996,52385,5-Na,2.460459949931576e-14,1018,5-Na,34790,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a single dominant Na+ peak at approximately 1.62 µs, but completely lacks a distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak about 1.49 µs later (around 3.11 µs), displaying only a broad, featureless rise in the baseline starting near 2.8 µs.",
1524984069,61192,4,3.2105201608128783e-14,1018,4,11884,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~1.96 s, followed by a nearly equally prominent peak at ~2.60 s (only ~0.64 s later) and smaller peaks at ~3.15 s and ~3.55 s, characteristic of a water-ice or potassium-rich spectrum. It lacks a dominant, isolated Na(NaOH)+ peak at the required ~1.49 s interval (~3.45 s).",
1524989582,1049,5-Na,5.860320095949639e-14,1018,5-Na,34791,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum features a single dominant Na+ peak at approximately 1.62 µs followed by a broad, featureless baseline shift rising to ~0.75 amplitude. It is classified as 'non-3-OH' because it completely lacks a distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at the expected distance of 1.49 µs later (around 3.11 µs).",
1524992328,3729,5-Na,5.249439934389838e-14,1018,5-Na,34792,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum features a single dominant Na+ peak at ~1.53 5s followed by a broad, featureless baseline overshoot reaching ~0.8 amplitude. It is classified as non-3-OH because it completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak expected ~1.49 5s later (around 3.02 5s).",
1524999555,10554,5-Na,1.029409982819876e-13,1018,5-Na,34793,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum features a single dominant Na+ peak at ~1.55 cs followed by a severe baseline overshoot, completely lacking the diagnostic Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak expected ~1.49 cs later at ~3.04 cs.",
1526897072,4936,5,1.9111599306701095e-14,1018,5,34514,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.62 BCs followed closely by a K+ peak at ~2.29 BCs (~0.67 BCs later). It is classified as 'non-3-OH' because it completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak expected ~1.49 BCs after the Na+ peak (around 3.11 BCs).,
1530372952,28960,4,3.1364101311763537e-13,1018,4,11888,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as non-3-OH because the highest peak is a broad feature at ~2.27 s rather than a dominant, narrow Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 s. Furthermore, it displays a complex mineral/organic peak pattern (with major peaks at ~0.35 s, ~1.70 s, ~2.95 s, ~3.50 s, and ~4.75 s) instead of the clean 1.49 s spacing required for a Na(NaOH)+ cluster series.",
