1571902021,38568,4,1.7684600528769523e-13,1018,4,18854,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as non-3-OH because the highest peak is a broad feature at ~2.22 5s rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 5s, and it also contains strong mineral/organic peaks at ~0.33 5s, ~1.63 5s, ~2.90 5s, and ~4.70 5s. Furthermore, no prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak appears ~1.49 5s after either the ~1.63 5s peak (expected at ~3.12 5s) or the ~2.22 5s peak (expected at ~3.71 5s).",
1571905500,41331,4,2.859700120477239e-14,1018,4,18857,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is located at approximately 0.2 s rather than representing a dominant Na+ peak in the expected 1.4–2.0 s range, violating Rule 1. Furthermore, the subsequent peaks at ~1.31 s, ~2.35 s, ~3.26 s, and ~4.53 s do not exhibit the characteristic 1.49 s spacing of the Na(NaOH)+ cluster series.",
1571906897,42154,4,1.899090043208651e-12,1018,4,18859,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because the highest peak is a broad, saturated complex centered around 2.1–2.5 µs rather than a dominant, narrow Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 µs. Furthermore, it exhibits a complex mineral-like profile with prominent peaks at ~0.4 µs, ~1.6 µs, ~3.1–3.9 µs, and ~5.3 µs, lacking the clean 1.49 µs Na(NaOH)+ cluster progression.",
1571909521,43350,4,3.9555500801896626e-13,1018,4,18861,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is located at approximately 0.37 µs rather than in the expected 1.4 to 2.0 µs range for Na+, violating Rule 1. Furthermore, the spectrum exhibits broad, complex mineral or organic features around 1.67 µs, 2.24 µs, 3.53 µs, and 4.80 µs instead of a clean sodium hydroxide cluster progression.",
1571950412,9159,5,1.884769941572044e-14,1018,5,34530,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a smaller Na+ peak at ~1.48 BCs and is instead dominated by a highest K+ peak at ~2.18 BCs (0.70 BCs later). Furthermore, it completely lacks any Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 BCs after either peak (around 2.97 BCs or 3.67 BCs).",
1571951205,9752,5,1.8674799662395103e-14,1018,5,34531,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a prominent Na+ peak at ~1.40 9Δs (or a smaller peak before the dominant K+ peak at ~2.09 9Δs, which is ~0.69 9Δs later), violating the rule that Na+ must be the highest peak. Furthermore, no Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak is present ~1.49 9Δs after either major peak (expected at ~2.89 9Δs or ~3.58 9Δs).",
1571957389,14066,5,2.5232599890805466e-14,1018,5,34532,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.62 µs followed closely by a K+ peak at ~2.32 µs (0.70 µs later), but completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak expected ~1.49 µs after Na+ (around 3.11 µs).",
1571968815,20667,5,1.9176200815522286e-14,1018,5,34533,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.62 s and an equally high K+ peak at ~2.32 s (a distance of ~0.70 s), but completely lacks the diagnostic Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak expected ~1.49 s after Na+ (around 3.11 s).",
1571975703,23625,5-Na,1.3199200067615883e-14,1018,5-Na,34823,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a broad, dominant peak between 1.45 and 1.65 µs followed by a noisy, decaying tail. It completely lacks the distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak expected about 1.49 µs after the main peak (around 2.95 to 3.15 µs).",
1571976618,23972,5-Na,1.8767100842657404e-14,1018,5-Na,34847,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the spectrum displays a single dominant Na+ peak at ~1.44 s, it completely lacks a sharp, distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 s later (around 2.93 s), showing only a broad, featureless baseline hump.",
1571981313,25526,5-Na,2.2300700375970164e-14,1018,5-Na,34848,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.40 bcs (along with a smaller peak at ~0.12 bcs), but completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 bcs later around 2.89 bcs. Instead, the remainder of the spectrum consists only of a flat, slightly elevated baseline without any hydroxide cluster peaks.",
1572005273,29180,5,1.3457800073445568e-14,1018,5,34422,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is located extremely early at approximately 0.72 µs rather than in the typical 1.4–2.0 µs range for Na+, and there is no Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak 1.49 µs later (around 2.21 µs), with the next prominent peaks only appearing late at ~5.61 µs and ~6.22 µs.",
1573938597,8958,4,1.1485399491282383e-13,1018,4,18863,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is dominated by a broad highest peak at ~2.13 5s followed closely by another prominent peak at ~2.82 5s (a distance of ~0.69 5s), along with an early H+ peak at ~0.28 5s and smaller peaks at ~1.62 5s, ~3.39 5s, and ~4.61 5s. It lacks both a clean dominant Na+ peak in the typical 1.4-2.0 5s range and the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak 1.49 5s after the main peak.",
1573961637,16860,4,6.984700090442025e-14,1018,4,18866,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as non-3-OH because the highest peak is at ~0.26 us rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 us. Furthermore, the spectrum is dominated by broad mineral or organic peaks at ~2.38 us, ~3.36 us, and ~4.66 us, lacking the characteristic 1.49 us sodium hydroxide cluster spacing.",
1574044575,31276,4,1.0496100245459966e-14,1018,4,18871,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is located at approximately 3.06 BCs rather than being a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 BCs, violating Rule 1. Furthermore, the peaks at ~1.38 BCs, ~1.82 BCs, ~2.52 BCs, ~3.06 BCs, and ~4.31 BCs do not match the required 1.49 BCs sodium hydroxide cluster spacing.",
1575362369,64598,4,1.399449946117709e-13,1018,4,18914,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~0.28 µs rather than being a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 µs. Furthermore, the spectrum displays a complex mineral/organic pattern with broad peaks at ~1.35 µs, ~1.62 µs, ~2.12 µs, ~3.38 µs, and ~4.65 µs instead of a clean sodium hydroxide cluster progression.",
1575403577,2293,5,1.3351300079888443e-14,1018,5,34534,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because the highest peak is a broad K+ peak at ~2.12 bcs rather than the preceding Na+ peak at ~1.43 bcs (a separation of ~0.69 bcs). Furthermore, it completely lacks a Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at the expected 1.49 bcs distance after the Na+ peak (around 2.92 bcs) or after the main peak (around 3.61 bcs).",
1575413559,9477,4,1.571940006547118e-14,1018,4,18916,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~1.69 µs (likely Na+ or H3O+), followed by a second major peak at ~2.38 µs (a distance of ~0.69 µs, consistent with K+). There is no Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 µs after the main peak (expected around 3.18 µs), ruling out the 3-OH class.",
1575517569,19358,4,1.2495199644933785e-14,1018,4,18917,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the highest peak is at ~1.84 µs (with a prominent shoulder at ~1.98 µs and an earlier peak at ~1.13 µs), there is no Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at the required 1.49 µs interval later (~3.33 µs). Instead, the spectrum shows peaks at ~2.52 µs, ~3.05 µs, and ~4.30 µs, which do not match the sodium hydroxide series.",
1576721969,8467,4,5.1064800852445094e-14,1018,4,18918,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a complex mineral or organic pattern with a strong early peak at ~0.18 s, smaller peaks at ~1.28 s and ~1.52 s, and a broad highest peak at ~2.01 s. It lacks the diagnostic Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak expected ~1.49 s after the main peak (around ~3.50 s), instead showing peaks at ~2.68 s, ~3.25 s, and ~4.50 s.",
1576722377,8547,4,1.2109100343531826e-13,1018,4,18919,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is located at approximately 0.28 bc	ext{s} (H+) rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 bc	ext{s}, violating Rule 1. Furthermore, the spectrum displays a complex mineral/organic pattern with broad peaks at ~1.38 bc	ext{s}, ~1.63 bc	ext{s}, ~2.1–2.4 bc	ext{s}, ~3.38 bc	ext{s}, and ~4.65 bc	ext{s} instead of a clean sodium hydroxide cluster progression.",
1577254887,26611,4,1.99870000649853e-13,1018,4,18920,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because its highest peak is located at ~0.32 µs (H+) rather than being a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 µs. Instead of a sodium hydroxide cluster series, the spectrum displays a complex mineral/organic pattern with major peaks at ~1.40 µs, ~1.63 µs, ~2.20 µs, ~2.88 µs, ~3.43 µs, and ~4.70 µs.",
1577345280,27257,4,6.235690132652683e-13,1018,4,18921,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is located at approximately 0.40 bc	ext{s} (likely H+) rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 bc	ext{s}. Additionally, the spectrum displays a complex mineral/organic pattern with broad peaks at ~1.67 bc	ext{s}, ~2.37 bc	ext{s}, ~3.07 bc	ext{s}, ~3.62 bc	ext{s}, and ~4.90 bc	ext{s}, lacking the characteristic Na(NaOH)+ cluster progression.",
1546308438,27977,5,1.5393600700771073e-14,1018,5,34817,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.48 s followed closely by a strong K+ peak at ~2.17 s (a distance of ~0.69 s), and completely lacks the characteristic Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak expected ~1.49 s after Na+ (around 2.97 s).",
1554703620,41296,5,1.884769941572044e-14,1018,5,34522,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a smaller peak at ~1.28 µs (likely Na+) and a dominant peak at ~1.98 µs (0.70 µs later, likely K+), with a long decaying tail and no subsequent peaks. Even if the main peak at ~1.98 µs were Na+, it completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak about 1.49 µs later (at ~3.47 µs).",
1557518222,29313,3-Car,1.0777599787018671e-13,1018,3-Car,34733,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.01 s followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.48 s (a time distance of ~1.47 s, matching the expected 1.49 s rule). This sodium hydroxide series is further confirmed by the second cluster peak Na(NaOH)2+ at ~4.53 s (~2.52 s after Na+).",
1557518245,29336,3-KNa,1.5441200564274976e-13,1018,3-KNa,34734,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.05 ̂s (with a split/H3O+ peak at ~2.00 ̂s) followed ~1.49 ̂s later by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ peak at ~3.54 ̂s. This hydroxide series is further supported by optional cluster peaks at ~4.00 ̂s (m/z 81) and ~4.59 ̂s (m/z 103), despite also having a strong K+ peak at ~2.72 ̂s.",
1557518258,29349,2,6.870780257673542e-14,1018,2,18250,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This spectrum is dominated by a regularly spaced water-ice hydronium cluster series with major peaks at ~1.80 s, ~2.65 s (0.85 s later), ~3.25 s, and ~3.78 s, rather than the sodium hydroxide pattern.",
1557518357,29448,2,1.706549974305003e-14,1018,2,18257,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum features a complex double-peak structure around 1.98 bc	ext{s} and 2.18 bc	ext{s} (highest peak), followed by a broad feature at ~2.85 bc	ext{s}, completely lacking the isolated Na(NaOH)+ peak required ~1.49 bc	ext{s} after a dominant Na+ peak (around 3.47–3.67 bc	ext{s}).",
1557518578,29669,2,7.65357016044993e-14,1018,2,18272,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant peak at ~1.84 s (with a sub-peak at ~2.00 s) followed by major peaks at ~2.63 s (~0.79 s later) and ~3.24 s (~1.40 s later), which matches a water-ice H3O+(H2O)n cluster series rather than a clean sodium hydroxide pattern where Na(NaOH)+ is the primary feature 1.49 s after Na+.",
1557518664,29755,2,1.356100019604678e-13,1018,2,18277,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because the highest peak is at ~3.33 5s rather than a dominant, isolated Na+ peak in the 1.4–2.0 5s range. Instead of the clean sodium hydroxide series, it shows a complex, multi-peaked water-ice or mixed cluster pattern with major doublets and peaks at ~0.23 5s, ~1.92 5s, ~2.08 5s, ~2.73 5s, ~3.33 5s, and ~3.83 5s.",
1557518687,29778,2,6.51939982034e-14,1018,2,18279,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the highest peak is at ~1.84 µs, there is no Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at the required ~1.49 µs interval (around 3.33 µs). Instead, the spectrum displays a complex mineral or organic pattern with prominent peaks at ~0.22 µs, ~2.03 µs, ~2.61 µs, ~4.56 µs, and ~4.95 µs.",
1557518964,30055,3-OH,4.124550026063205e-14,1018,3-OH,34735,3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.84 BCs, followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.31 BCs (a diagnostic distance of ~1.47 BCs). This sodium hydroxide series is further supported by a secondary Na(NaOH)2+ peak at ~4.33 BCs (~2.49 BCs after Na+).",
1557518998,30089,3-OH,7.153299762426013e-13,1018,3-OH,34736,3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although there is a maximum peak at ~2.16 µs and a small feature ~1.44 µs later at ~3.60 µs, the spectrum is dominated by a massive baseline step-up after 2.0 µs and a prominent early H+/C+ peak at ~0.28 µs, which is characteristic of a high-impact mineral or saturated spectrum rather than a clean 3-OH sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1557519099,30190,3-Cl,2.885959835908017e-14,1018,3-Cl,34737,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.94 5s followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.35 5s (a time distance of ~1.41 5s, within the expected 1.49 5s +/- 0.1 5s window). A strong subsequent hydrated hydroxide/chloride peak at ~3.88 5s (~0.53 5s after the m/z 63 peak) further confirms the 3-OH classification.",
1557519141,30232,3-Car,2.1091399568691493e-13,1018,3-Car,34738,non-3-OH,3-OH,"Although the baseline rises slightly causing the Na(NaOH)+ peak at ~3.59 bc	ext{s} to reach 1.0, the spectrum clearly exhibits the diagnostic 3-OH sequence: a major Na+ peak at ~2.10 bc	ext{s}, followed ~1.49 bc	ext{s} later by Na(NaOH)+ at ~3.59 bc	ext{s}, and a second cluster Na(NaOH)2+ at ~4.63 bc	ext{s} (~2.53 bc	ext{s} after Na+).",
1557519144,30235,3-P,1.8588800407260374e-14,1018,3-P,34739,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.90 BCs followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.37 BCs, which is ~1.47 BCs later and matches the expected 1.49 BCs separation for '3-OH'. A secondary Na(NaOH)2+ peak is also visible at ~4.53 BCs, further supporting the sodium hydroxide series.",
1557519195,30286,2,1.31364998089481e-13,1018,2,18308,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a complex mineral or alternative salt pattern with major peaks at ~0.24 s, ~1.84 s, ~2.05 s, ~2.64 s, ~2.80 s, and a cluster between 4.55 and 5.70 s. Because the peaks following the highest peak at ~1.84 s are dominated by other ions at ~2.05 s and ~2.64 s rather than a clean sodium hydroxide cluster series, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1557519216,30307,3-Car,2.4232699180615214e-13,1018,3-Car,34740,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.09 BCs, followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.55 BCs (a distance of ~1.46 BCs, matching the expected 1.49 BCs interval). This sodium hydroxide series is further confirmed by the second hydroxide cluster Na(NaOH)2+ at ~4.60 BCs (~2.51 BCs after Na+).",
1557519416,30507,3-Car,2.1357300490306742e-14,1018,3-Car,34741,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a broad, dominant peak at ~2.18 µs (outside the typical sharp Na+ profile) followed by major peaks at ~3.67 µs (1.49 µs later) and ~5.27 µs (3.09 µs after the main peak, or 1.60 µs after the second peak). Because the third prominent peak at ~5.27 µs does not match the sodium hydroxide cluster progression (which expects peaks at ~0.50 µs or ~1.05 µs after the m/z 63 peak), this pattern comes from other salts or minerals rather than the 3-OH series.",
1557519439,30530,3-Car,4.804289900476634e-14,1018,3-Car,34742,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.93 s followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.42 s (1.49 s later), along with a secondary Na(NaOH)2+ peak at ~4.48 s (2.55 s after Na+).",
1557519627,30718,3-K,4.726309946710694e-13,1018,3-K,34743,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because its highest peak is a broad mineral/organic feature peaking near 3.00 s rather than a dominant, narrow Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 s. Additionally, it features prominent peaks at ~0.35 s, ~4.56 s, and ~5.03 s, completely lacking the diagnostic 1.49 s spacing of the sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1557519700,30790,3-OH,1.4797600536402278e-13,1018,3-OH,34744,3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum has its highest peak (Na+) at ~1.98 s, followed by a distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.45 s (a separation of ~1.47 s) and a secondary Na(NaOH)2+ peak at ~4.49 s (~2.51 s after Na+), fulfilling the criteria for '3-OH' despite the elevated baseline.",
1557519977,31067,1,1.2639300278052476e-14,1018,1,18354,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the highest peak is located at ~1.64 µs (compatible with Na+), the spectrum completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 µs later around 3.13 µs. Instead, the only prominent subsequent peak appears much later at ~4.36 µs (~2.72 µs after the main peak, likely Rh+ target ions), ruling out the 3-OH class.",
1557520036,31125,3-Car,1.4439599689552995e-13,1018,3-Car,34745,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at approximately 2.03 µs, followed about 1.48 µs later by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at 3.51 µs. This sodium hydroxide series is further confirmed by the second cluster peak Na(NaOH)2+ at approximately 4.55 µs (2.52 µs after Na+).",
1557520217,31305,3-OH,1.120169969693989e-13,1018,3-OH,34746,3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum is dominated by a Na+ peak at ~2.01 µs, followed ~1.48 µs later by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.49 µs. This sodium hydroxide pattern is further confirmed by a second hydroxide cluster peak, Na(NaOH)2+, at ~4.53 µs (~2.52 µs after Na+).",
1557520418,31505,3-OH,6.300750123467563e-14,1018,3-OH,34747,3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.01 µs, followed ~1.48 µs later by a clear Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.49 µs. A secondary Na(NaOH)2+ cluster peak is also visible at ~4.54 µs (~2.53 µs after Na+), confirming the sodium hydroxide series despite the elevated baseline.",
1557528598,34041,4,3.375129833276848e-14,1018,4,34412,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~0.32 bc	ext{s} rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 bc	ext{s}, and the subsequent major peaks at ~1.73 bc	ext{s}, ~3.52 bc	ext{s} (1.79 bc	ext{s} after the 1.73 bc	ext{s} peak), and ~4.83 bc	ext{s} do not match the required 1.49 bc	ext{s} Na(NaOH)+ spacing.",
1558903750,47150,4,1.0890799811188578e-14,1018,4,18390,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is a broad feature at ~3.05 s rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 s, violating Rule 1. Although there are sharp peaks at ~1.13 s and ~1.39 s, neither is the highest peak and the major subsequent peaks at ~3.05 s and ~4.32 s do not follow the required 1.49 s spacing for a Na(NaOH)+ cluster.",
1558905527,47194,4,1.6049299747262352e-13,1018,4,18391,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a complex mineral or organic pattern with a broad base peak at ~2.14 9cs preceded by strong peaks at ~0.30 9cs, ~1.39 9cs, and ~1.63 9cs, rather than a dominant Na+ peak. Furthermore, no characteristic Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak appears ~1.49 9cs after the ~1.63 9cs peak (expected around 3.12 9cs) or after the ~2.14 9cs peak (expected around 3.63 9cs).",
1558908926,47538,Noise,1.8224200157312444e-14,1018,Noise,18403,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum lacks a sharp dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 s, showing instead a sharp spike at ~0.14 s and a single broad hump peaking around 2.3 s. Furthermore, no Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak is present ~1.49 s after the broad feature (around 3.8 s), where only baseline noise is observed.",
1558908969,47571,1,2.0439399684487464e-14,1018,1,18405,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This is a water-ice spectrum dominated by a hydronium cluster series (peaks at ~1.63 s, 2.45 s, 3.06 s, 3.60 s, and 4.08 s) along with a smaller Na+ peak at ~1.84 s. Because the highest peak is H3O+ (~1.63 s) rather than Na+ and there is no Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 s after Na+ (at ~3.33 s), it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1558909011,47605,1,1.0516300287186087e-14,1018,1,18408,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the spectrum has a dominant peak at ~1.61 bc	ext{s} (which could be Na+ or H3O+), it completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 bc	ext{s} later at ~3.10 bc	ext{s}, showing instead smaller peaks at ~1.82 bc	ext{s}, ~2.52 bc	ext{s}, and ~4.35 bc	ext{s}.",
1558909873,48327,1,2.2300700375970164e-14,1018,1,18511,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a classic water-ice pattern dominated by a regularly spaced hydronium cluster series (H3O+(H2O)n) at ~1.63 5s, ~2.46 5s, ~3.11 5s, ~3.66 5s, ~4.13 5s, and ~4.54 5s, along with a secondary Na+ peak at ~1.86 5s. Because the highest peak is H3O+ (~1.63 5s) rather than Na+ (~1.86 5s) and there is no Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 5s after Na+ (around 3.35 5s), it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1558910548,48964,1,1.2447799681205435e-14,1018,1,18584,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This is a water-ice spectrum dominated by a regularly spaced series of hydronium cluster peaks at ~0.90 µs, ~1.73 µs (the highest peak), ~2.35 µs, ~2.90 µs, and ~3.38 µs. It lacks the characteristic Na(NaOH)+ peak expected ~1.49 µs after the main peak (around 3.22 µs), instead showing peaks at intervals of ~0.5 to 0.8 µs.",
1558910640,49054,1,1.7505099678279644e-14,1018,1,18590,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This is a water-ice spectrum dominated by a regularly spaced hydronium cluster series with major peaks at ~1.63 S3, ~2.45 S3 (the highest peak), ~3.07 S3, and ~3.60 S3. It is classified as 'non-3-OH' because the highest peak is not Na+ (which is only a minor peak at ~1.84 S3), and it lacks the diagnostic Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak 1.49 S3 after Na+ (at ~3.33 S3).",
1558910942,49351,1,1.1351999933606124e-14,1018,1,18627,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This spectrum shows a typical water-ice hydronium cluster series with major peaks at ~1.56 bc	ext{s}, ~2.38 bc	ext{s}, ~3.01 bc	ext{s}, and ~3.56 bc	ext{s}. The second major peak is only ~0.82 bc	ext{s} after the first peak, rather than the ~1.49 bc	ext{s} spacing required for a Na(NaOH)+ cluster.",
1558910953,49362,1,1.975470060157445e-14,1018,1,18631,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a water-ice hydronium cluster series starting with the highest peak at ~1.58 s (H3O+, accompanied by a smaller Na+ peak at ~1.79 s), followed by major cluster peaks at ~2.41 s, ~3.05 s, and ~3.60 s. It is classified as non-3-OH because the highest peak is not Na+, and the subsequent peak spacings do not match the required ~1.49 s interval for Na(NaOH)+.",
1558910989,49398,Noise,1.9885399479401683e-14,1018,Noise,18636,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,The spectrum consists entirely of instrumental noise with a single sharp spike at ~0.14 µs and no coherent ion peaks. It completely lacks a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 µs as well as the corresponding Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak 1.49 µs later.,
1558911110,49518,1,1.6343500717271725e-14,1018,1,18647,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a classic water-ice hydronium cluster series (H3O+(H2O)n) with major peaks at ~1.51 BCs, ~2.33 BCs (the highest peak, 0.82 BCs after the first), ~2.96 BCs, and ~3.48 BCs, while a smaller Na+ peak appears at ~1.71 BCs. Because Na+ is not the dominant peak and the main progression is driven by water-ice clusters rather than a sodium hydroxide series (which would require a dominant Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 BCs after Na+, around 3.20 BCs), it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1558911342,49750,Noise,1.2938800116773282e-14,1018,Noise,18665,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,The spectrum consists entirely of instrumental noise with a single sharp spike near 0.14 us and lacks both a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 us and a Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak 1.49 us later.,
1558911439,49846,1,1.2117599980344344e-14,1018,1,18678,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This spectrum is a water-ice pattern dominated by a regularly spaced hydronium cluster series with major peaks at ~1.48 9cs, ~2.30 9cs (the highest peak), ~2.92 9cs, ~3.45 9cs, ~3.90 9cs, and ~4.33 9cs. It lacks a dominant Na+ peak followed by a Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak 1.49 9cs later.",
1558911497,49904,1,2.0987099658511567e-14,1018,1,18686,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the spectrum has a dominant peak at ~1.67 bc	ext{s} (which could be Na+ or C+), it completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 bc	ext{s} later (around 3.16 bc	ext{s}). Instead, the next major peak appears at ~4.40 bc	ext{s} (likely Rh+ from the target, ~2.73 bc	ext{s} after the main peak), along with early peaks at ~0.14–0.44 bc	ext{s}.",
1558911540,49947,1,1.768610045471252e-14,1018,1,18695,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a regularly spaced water-ice cluster series with major peaks at ~1.53 µs, ~2.36 µs, ~2.98 µs, and ~3.53 µs (the highest peak, violating Rule 1). Furthermore, the first cluster spacing from the ~1.53 µs peak is ~0.83 µs rather than the required ~1.49 µs for a Na(NaOH)+ cluster.",
1558911632,49980,1,1.4208599913496413e-14,1018,1,18696,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a water-ice hydronium cluster series starting with the highest peak at ~1.58 s (H3O+), followed by major peaks at ~2.40 s (0.82 s later), ~3.03 s, and ~3.59 s. Even if the smaller peak at ~1.80 s is Na+, there is no Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 s later (at ~3.29 s).",
1558912263,50611,1,2.882270160389777e-14,1018,1,18718,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This is a water-ice spectrum dominated by a regularly spaced hydronium cluster series starting with the highest peak at ~1.68 µs, followed by major peaks at ~2.50 µs, ~3.13 µs, ~3.66 µs, and ~4.13 µs. The ~0.82 µs spacing to the second peak (and ~1.45 µs to the third peak as part of a continuous water cluster progression) does not match the isolated sodium hydroxide cluster pattern.",
1558918686,56132,2,3.306950118473276e-14,1018,2,34480,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the highest peak is at ~1.90 µs, it is immediately followed by a broad, closely spaced cluster progression with peaks at ~2.20 µs, ~2.85 µs, ~3.28 µs, and ~3.68 µs (typical of water-ice or organic-rich spectra), rather than an isolated Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 µs later at ~3.39 µs.",
1560296686,19623,4,5.518210129291934e-13,1018,4,18730,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because its highest peak is located at ~0.40 µs rather than being a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 µs. Furthermore, it exhibits a complex mineral or organic profile with broad peaks at ~1.45 µs, ~1.72 µs, ~2.30 µs, ~3.58 µs, and ~4.88 µs instead of a clean sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1561667697,36491,4,1.2826400098281399e-12,1018,4,18734,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is a complex mineral profile where the highest peaks are broad features at ~2.41 µs and ~3.18 µs rather than an isolated Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 µs. Furthermore, the cluttered sequence of peaks at ~0.42 µs, ~1.41 µs, ~1.67 µs, ~3.76 µs, and ~5.08 µs does not follow the required 1.49 µs sodium hydroxide cluster spacing.",
1561667772,36527,4,2.7725299269962256e-14,1018,4,18735,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is a broad mineral or organic peak at ~3.15 us rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 us. Furthermore, the earlier peaks at ~1.18 us and ~1.43 us are not followed by a Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 us later, with the spectrum instead showing peaks at ~2.22 us, ~3.15 us, and ~4.40 us.",
1561667909,36604,4,6.085020318570902e-14,1018,4,18736,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is located at approximately 0.22 s rather than representing a dominant Na+ peak in the 1.4–2.0 s range, violating Rule 1. Furthermore, the spectrum is dominated by broad mineral or organic peaks at ~1.32 s, ~2.30 s, ~3.31 s, and ~4.57 s rather than a sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1561667930,36614,4,4.0971200499125005e-14,1018,4,18737,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~0.20 bc	ext{s} (H+) rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 bc	ext{s}, violating Rule 1. Instead of a sodium hydroxide series, the spectrum shows a complex organic or mineral pattern with peaks at ~1.32 bc	ext{s}, ~1.55 bc	ext{s}, ~2.03 bc	ext{s}, ~3.28 bc	ext{s}, and ~4.56 bc	ext{s}.",
1561697848,54792,2,2.750909919237328e-14,1018,2,18770,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is located at approximately 2.90 s rather than being a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 s, and the spectrum shows a noisy, regularly spaced cluster progression (peaks at ~2.15 s, ~2.90 s, and ~3.60 s) typical of water-ice rather than the 1.49 s spacing of the Na(NaOH)+ series.",
1561698213,55155,1,1.2846000034105048e-14,1018,1,18795,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This spectrum is dominated by a water-ice hydronium cluster series (H3O+(H2O)n) starting with a main peak at ~1.50 s (with a minor Na+ peak at ~1.70 s), followed by a prominent second peak at ~2.31 s (a distance of ~0.81 s) and subsequent regularly spaced peaks at ~2.96 s and ~3.50 s. It lacks both a dominant Na+ peak and the required 1.49 s interval to an isolated Na(NaOH)+ cluster.",
1561722490,12935,5,1.6007399737867113e-14,1018,5,34525,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~2.19 bc	ext{s} (likely K+ following a smaller Na+ peak at ~1.48 bc	ext{s}, a distance of ~0.71 bc	ext{s}) rather than Na+ being the dominant peak. Furthermore, there is no Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 bc	ext{s} after the Na+ peak (around 2.97 bc	ext{s}) or after the main peak (around 3.68 bc	ext{s}).",
1561726488,16645,5-Na,2.0297099843414636e-14,1018,5-Na,34842,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a single dominant Na+ peak at approximately 1.40 bcS, followed by a flat baseline with no subsequent peaks. Because it completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak about 1.49 bcS later (expected around 2.89 bcS), it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1561726952,17070,5,1.8931000023885217e-14,1018,5,34490,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum features a broad dominant peak at ~1.86 µs followed by a secondary broad shoulder peak at ~2.53 µs (a separation of ~0.67 µs, likely K+). It completely lacks a distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at the required 1.49 µs interval (~3.35 µs), displaying only a decaying tail.",
1561729352,19237,5-Na,6.027390229718793e-14,1018,5-Na,34843,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum features a single dominant Na+ peak at approximately 1.38 Qs, but lacks any distinct Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at the expected distance of ~1.49 Qs later (around 2.87 Qs). Instead, it displays only a gradual, featureless rise in the baseline starting near 2.8 Qs, confirming a 'non-3-OH' label.",
1563677405,39049,4,5.795000303189177e-14,1018,4,18805,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as non-3-OH because the highest peak is at ~0.23 s rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 s, and it shows a complex mineral or organic profile with major peaks at ~2.35 s, ~3.32 s, and ~4.58 s instead of the sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1563678960,40329,4,4.072279893938685e-13,1018,4,18806,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peaks are located at ~0.37 µs and ~4.84 µs rather than being a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 µs. Additionally, the spectrum displays a complex mineral/organic pattern with broad peaks at ~2.38 µs and ~3.55 µs instead of the characteristic Na(NaOH)+ cluster series.",
1563684468,44417,4,1.0731700088046497e-13,1018,4,18817,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peaks are broad features at ~3.36 s and ~4.64 s along with a sharp peak at ~0.25 s, violating Rule 1 which requires Na+ (between 1.4 and 2.0 s) to be the highest peak. Furthermore, the peak at ~1.37 s is not followed by a Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak 1.49 s later (~2.86 s), displaying instead a complex mineral or organic pattern.",
1563685407,45006,4,2.5347200060437183e-14,1018,4,18818,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~2.03 s (preceded by smaller peaks at ~0.18 s and ~1.58 s), which is likely a mineral/organic or K+ peak rather than a dominant Na+ peak. Even if the peak at ~2.03 s were Na+, the subsequent minor peaks at ~2.71 s, ~3.25 s, ~3.51 s, and ~4.50 s do not show a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster signature.",
1563686798,45759,4,2.2927699235703036e-13,1018,4,18821,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is located at ~0.31 us rather than being a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 us. Furthermore, the spectrum displays a complex mineral or organic pattern with broad peaks at ~1.43 us, ~1.67 us, ~3.45 us, and ~4.72 us, lacking the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster spacing.",
1563687283,46024,4,2.3534600375289816e-13,1018,4,18822,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as non-3-OH because the highest peak is a broad feature at ~2.21 9cs rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 9cs, and the next major peak follows only ~0.68 9cs later at ~2.89 9cs instead of the required 1.49 9cs interval. Additionally, prominent mineral/organic peaks at ~0.33 9cs, ~1.42 9cs, ~1.69 9cs, and ~4.72 9cs confirm a non-hydroxide composition.",
1563688113,46575,4,2.8926700309161654e-14,1018,4,18823,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the highest peak is at ~1.96 s, it is preceded by early mineral/organic peaks at ~0.16, ~1.25, and ~1.50 s, and completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 s later (around 3.45 s). Instead, the spectrum displays major peaks at ~2.62, ~3.19, and ~4.45 s, which is characteristic of a mineral-rich grain rather than a 3-OH sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1563688819,47025,4,6.934370070342533e-14,1018,4,18824,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because its highest peak is a broad feature at ~3.35 us rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 us, violating Rule 1. Instead of a clean sodium hydroxide cluster progression, it displays a mineral or organic profile with multiple peaks at ~0.25 us, ~1.35 us, ~1.60 us, ~2.32 us, ~3.35 us, and ~4.62 us.",
1563690157,47861,4,2.610129994085053e-14,1018,4,18826,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"This spectrum shows a complex organic or mineral pattern with multiple early peaks at ~0.16 s, ~1.27 s, and ~1.51 s, rather than a clean salt-rich spectrum starting with a dominant Na+ peak. Even if the peak at ~1.98 s is considered Na+, the broad peak at ~3.23 s is only 1.25 s later, failing to match the required 1.49 s spacing for Na(NaOH)+.",
