1589068280,6736,3-K,8.869290122216072e-14,1018,3-K,34749,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is located at approximately 2.70 bc	ext{s} (well outside the typical 1.4–2.0 bc	ext{s} range for Na+), and the next major peaks at ~4.35 bc	ext{s} and ~4.78 bc	ext{s} follow at intervals of ~1.65 bc	ext{s} and ~2.08 bc	ext{s}, where the dominant secondary peak at 4.78 bc	ext{s} does not match the required 1.49 bc	ext{s} spacing for Na(NaOH)+.",
1589069314,7677,1,2.2244099940368738e-14,1018,1,19011,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~1.67 s, followed by prominent peaks at ~1.88 s (0.21 s later) and ~2.57 s (0.90 s later), while completely lacking the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 s after the main peak (expected around 3.16 s).",
1589070006,8339,3-OH,1.3538299713060364e-13,1018,3-OH,34750,3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.08 BCs followed ~1.49 BCs later by a strong Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.57 BCs. A smaller peak at ~4.60 BCs (~2.52 BCs after Na+, corresponding to Na(NaOH)2+ or Rh+) further supports the sodium hydroxide pattern.",
1589070222,8549,3-OH,2.613350074537335e-14,1018,3-OH,34751,3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.92 µs followed by a clear Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.38 µs, which corresponds to a time separation of ~1.46 µs. This closely matches the expected 1.49 µs spacing and satisfies the required criteria for the '3-OH' class.",
1589070814,9139,3-Cl,6.845939830649184e-14,1018,3-Cl,34752,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.98 s followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.46 s (a time distance of 1.48 s), which matches the required 1.49 s spacing. This 3-OH classification is further supported by a strong hydrated cluster peak Na(NaOH)(H2O)+ at ~3.97 s (0.51 s after the m/z 63 peak).",
1589071034,9359,2,2.5386900155861813e-13,1018,2,19077,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the highest peak is at ~1.88 9Εs, the spectrum lacks the characteristic Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak expected ~1.49 9Εs later (around 3.37 9Εs). Instead, it displays a complex mineral/organic pattern with strong early peaks at ~0.28, ~0.48, and ~0.62 9Εs, a doublet near 2.7–2.8 9Εs, and a broad peak around 4.62 9Εs.",
1589071078,9403,3-OH,3.42049014166821e-14,1018,3-OH,34753,3-OH,3-OH,The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.95 µs followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.44 µs (exactly 1.49 µs later). A secondary Na(NaOH)2+ peak at ~4.45 µs (~2.50 µs after Na+) further confirms the sodium hydroxide series.,
1589071300,9625,3-OH,2.1027800269253494e-13,1018,3-OH,34754,3-OH,non-3-OH,"Despite peaks appearing at ~2.12 Ws, ~3.61 Ws, and ~4.68 Ws, this is a mineral spectrum characterized by a prominent H+ peak at ~0.28 Ws, a broad multi-component peak around 2.12 Ws (likely Mg+/Si+ rather than a clean Na+ peak), and a split iron (54Fe+/56Fe+) doublet at 3.60/3.68 Ws.",
1589071317,9642,3-OH,8.066839839344919e-13,1018,3-OH,34755,3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows mineral features including a prominent H+ peak at ~0.35 5s, a smaller Na+ candidate at ~1.47 5s, and a broad base peak at ~2.22 5s (likely Mg+ or Fe+) rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 5s. Even though peaks at ~3.76 5s (Fe+) and ~4.84 5s (Rh+) have similar spacing to a hydroxide series relative to the 2.22 5s peak, the presence of the early H+ and 1.47 5s peaks confirms this is a mineral grain rather than a 3-OH ice grain.",
1589071599,9924,3-Car,3.4505999945387555e-13,1018,3-Car,34756,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a double peak near 2.13-2.20 s followed by a severely elevated, saturated baseline with sharp dips around 3.55 s and 4.65 s rather than a clean sodium hydroxide cluster progression. Because there is no well-resolved Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak 1.49 s after a dominant Na+ peak, it is classified as non-3-OH.",
1589071652,9977,3-OH,2.694380092302384e-13,1018,3-OH,34757,3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as non-3-OH because the highest peak is a split feature around 3.55-3.65 µs riding on a broad, elevated baseline hump rather than a clean, dominant Na+ peak. Furthermore, despite the initial peak complex at ~2.1 µs, the heavily distorted baseline and split peaks do not represent a clean sodium hydroxide cluster progression.",
1589071776,10101,3-Cl,1.896629961374227e-13,1018,3-Cl,34758,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The highest peak is Na+ at ~2.01 µs, followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.48 µs (a distance of ~1.47 µs, matching the expected 1.49 µs spacing). This classification is further supported by a secondary hydrated cluster peak Na(NaOH)(H2O)+ at ~4.00 µs (~0.52 µs after the m/z 63 peak).",
1589071924,10249,3-OH,1.5826600555275683e-13,1018,3-OH,34759,3-OH,3-OH,The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.03 µs followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.51 µs (a separation of ~1.48 µs). A secondary Na(NaOH)2+ peak at ~4.55 µs (~2.52 µs after Na+) further confirms the sodium hydroxide series despite the arched baseline.,
1589072056,10381,3-OH,1.9627100509081452e-13,1018,3-OH,34760,3-OH,non-3-OH,"This appears to be a mineral or target-dominated spectrum with a strong H+ peak at ~0.27 9s, a broad split feature around 2.04-2.14 9s, and a Rh+ target peak at ~3.60 9s. Although the spacing from 2.1 9s to 3.6 9s is ~1.5 9s, the prominent early H+/C+ peaks (0.27-0.62 9s), the split shape of the 2.1 9s peak, and the broad baseline hump are characteristic of a mineral/target impact rather than a clean 3-OH ice grain.",
1589072262,10587,1,1.6062800774815228e-14,1018,1,19152,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~1.65 5s, but there is no Na(NaOH)+ peak ~1.49 5s later at ~3.14 5s. Instead, the spectrum shows peaks at ~0.41 5s, ~1.86 5s, ~2.55 5s, and ~4.38 5s, which do not match the sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1589072333,10658,3-OH,1.9537000598042475e-13,1018,3-OH,34761,3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum represents a mineral grain rather than a sodium-hydroxide-rich ice grain, featuring a prominent early H+ peak at ~0.27 bc, a broad split peak at ~2.04–2.14 bc (typically Mg+/Si+/Fe+), and a sharp peak at ~3.60 bc sitting atop a broad hump from ~2.6 to 4.8 bc rather than a clean Na+ and Na(NaOH)+ cluster series.",
1589072351,10676,3-Car,2.4851100994746633e-13,1018,3-Car,34762,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum lacks a clean, dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 s, instead showing a broad double peak at ~2.28 s and ~2.48 s (the highest peak). Furthermore, the subsequent broad peaks at ~3.80 s and ~5.48 s do not match the diagnostic 1.49 s sodium hydroxide cluster spacing.",
1589072533,10858,2,8.348190032054364e-14,1018,2,19169,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~0.25 µs rather than Na+, and even considering the strong candidate Na+ peak at ~1.84 µs, there is no Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at the required ~1.49 µs interval (~3.33 µs), with the next major peak appearing much later at ~4.56 µs.",
1589072572,10897,3-OH,5.623970256510291e-13,1018,3-OH,34763,3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a complex mineral or organic profile with a sharp early peak at ~0.35 µs, a small peak at ~1.43 µs, and a broad, split maximum at ~2.1–2.27 µs rather than a clean dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 µs. Although broad complex features appear later at ~3.75 µs and ~4.78 µs, the presence of strong early ions (H+/C+) and split broad peaks rules out the clean sodium hydroxide cluster pattern.",
1589072824,11149,3-Car,8.645710015964259e-14,1018,3-Car,34764,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is dominated by a broad, asymmetric peak with a shoulder at ~2.20 5s and a maximum at ~2.33 5s, rather than a clean, narrow Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 5s. Additionally, the subsequent peaks at ~3.75 5s and ~5.38 5s do not match the characteristic sodium hydroxide cluster progression (which would require a secondary cluster at ~4.80 5s if the ~3.75 5s peak were Na(NaOH)+).",
1589073025,11349,2,1.6202999974178865e-14,1018,2,19197,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~1.64 µs, but the spectrum completely lacks a Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at the required ~1.49 µs interval later (around 3.13 µs). Instead, it displays early peaks at ~0.26 and ~0.40 µs and a later peak at ~4.37 µs (likely Rh+ target material), ruling out the 3-OH signature.",
1589073259,11582,3-OH,4.766759903462869e-13,1018,3-OH,34765,3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a double peak near 2.08 µs and 2.18 µs (typical of H3O+ and Na+ or mineral ions) followed by a broad baseline hump with a single sharp peak at ~3.62 µs (likely Rh+ from the target, which is ~2.53 µs after m/z 23, not 1.49 µs), lacking a genuine sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1589073391,11712,3-OH,1.2537800658796172e-13,1018,3-OH,34766,3-OH,non-3-OH,"This is a mineral/target spectrum rather than a salt-rich 3-OH grain: it displays a strong early peak at ~0.27 s (H+), a split/multi-peak complex between ~1.95 and 2.30 s (likely Mg+/Si+/Fe+ rather than a clean Na+ peak), and a sharp Rh+ target peak at ~3.57 s.",
1589073472,11792,3-Car,3.135939926246674e-14,1018,3-Car,34767,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.88 BCs, followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.36 BCs (a separation of ~1.48 BCs) and a secondary Na(NaOH)2+ peak at ~4.40 BCs (~2.52 BCs after Na+), matching the characteristic 3-OH signature.",
1589073584,11902,2,5.79288001031561e-14,1018,2,19230,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is located at approximately 0.22 µs rather than being a dominant Na+ peak in the 1.4 to 2.0 µs range. Furthermore, assuming the peak at ~1.78 µs is Na+, there is no Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak about 1.49 µs later (near 3.27 µs); instead, the next major peak appears much later at ~4.52 µs.",
1589073587,11905,3-OH,2.1807000107586239e-13,1018,3-OH,34768,3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows prominent early peaks at ~0.30 bc	ext{s} and ~1.38 bc	ext{s}, and a broad multi-peak complex reaching maximum amplitude at ~2.08 bc	ext{s}, rather than a clean, isolated Na+ peak in the typical 1.4–2.0 bc	ext{s} range. This mineral/organic-rich profile does not follow the characteristic sodium hydroxide cluster series and is classified as non-3-OH.",
1589073610,11928,3-OH,3.715060079229407e-14,1018,3-OH,34769,3-OH,3-OH,The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at approximately 1.96 µs followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at approximately 3.45 µs. The time separation of 1.49 µs matches the characteristic sodium hydroxide cluster spacing required for the 3-OH class.,
1589073689,12005,3-OH,2.520699916700765e-14,1018,3-OH,34770,3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.90 µs, followed ~1.47 µs later by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.37 µs. A secondary Na(NaOH)2+ cluster peak is also visible at ~4.42 µs (~2.52 µs after Na+), confirming the 3-OH classification.",
1589073743,12059,1,2.88317004819294e-14,1018,1,19238,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the spectrum has a dominant peak at ~1.71 µs in the Na+ region, it completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 µs later (at ~3.20 µs). Instead, it shows peaks at ~0.48 µs, ~1.93 µs, ~2.61 µs, and ~4.49 µs, indicating a mineral or non-hydroxide composition.",
1589073762,12077,3-OH,3.506990162681356e-14,1018,3-OH,34771,3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.00 µs followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.48 µs, corresponding to the diagnostic ~1.48 µs separation. A smaller secondary hydroxide cluster peak Na(NaOH)2+ is also visible at ~4.50 µs (~2.50 µs after Na+), confirming the 3-OH classification.",
1589073815,12129,3-OH,3.867760129641802e-14,1018,3-OH,34772,3-OH,3-OH,The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.93 s followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.40 s (a distance of ~1.47 s). This sodium hydroxide series is further confirmed by the secondary Na(NaOH)2+ peak at ~4.45 s (~2.52 s after Na+).,
1589073821,12135,2,3.6691698670262424e-14,1018,2,19243,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the highest peak is at ~1.73 us (with a nearly equal peak at ~1.95 us), the spectrum completely lacks a Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 us later (around 3.22 us or 3.44 us). Instead, it displays a mineral/organic-like profile with prominent early peaks at ~0.16 us and ~0.50 us, as well as later peaks at ~2.63 us and ~4.48 us.",
1589073901,12213,2,1.0516300287186087e-14,1018,2,19254,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although there is a dominant peak at approximately 1.62 µs, the spectrum completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak 1.49 µs later (expected around 3.11 µs). Instead, it only shows minor peaks near 0.38 µs and 1.83 µs along with a late target peak (Rh+) at approximately 4.35 µs.",
1589073937,12249,1,1.5515800450005557e-14,1018,1,19257,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~0.22 µs rather than Na+, and although there is a strong peak at ~1.78 µs, it completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 µs later (around 3.27 µs), showing instead a major peak much later at ~4.50 µs.",
1589074021,12331,3-Cl,6.295779734133075e-14,1018,3-Cl,34773,non-3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~2.01 bc	ext{s} followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.48 bc	ext{s} (a time distance of ~1.47 bc	ext{s}, matching the expected 1.49 bc	ext{s}). This classification is further supported by the hydrated hydroxide cluster peak at ~3.99 bc	ext{s} (~0.51 bc	ext{s} after the m/z 63 peak).",
1589074827,13117,3-Car,6.745939798522699e-14,1018,3-Car,34774,non-3-OH,3-OH,The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.94 s followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.43 s (a time distance of 1.49 s). This sodium hydroxide cluster series is further confirmed by the second cluster peak Na(NaOH)2+ at ~4.48 s (2.54 s after Na+).,
1589078675,16097,3-OH,5.977499853600243e-13,1018,3-OH,34775,3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because the highest peak is a broad, split mineral/organic feature at ~2.16-2.27 µs alongside a strong H+ peak at ~0.36 µs, rather than a clean Na+ peak (a minor peak is at ~1.44 µs). Although a sharp peak sits at ~3.70 µs atop a massive broad hump, the overall profile is a mineral-rich pattern rather than a sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1589078838,16247,3-OH,4.932910159451305e-14,1018,3-OH,34776,3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.88 s followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.37 s (exactly 1.49 s later), matching the core criteria for 3-OH. This sodium hydroxide pattern is further confirmed by a secondary Na(NaOH)2+ cluster peak at ~4.40 s (~2.52 s after the Na+ peak).",
1589078882,16286,3-OH,2.79234995586089e-13,1018,3-OH,34777,3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a mineral or organic profile with a sharp H+ peak at ~0.31 µs and a broad, split base peak reaching maximum amplitude at ~2.18 µs rather than a clean, dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 µs. Although a peak appears at ~3.63 µs, the presence of the strong ~0.31 µs peak, a minor feature at ~1.40 µs, and the broad multi-component structure around 2.0–2.2 µs is inconsistent with a 3-OH sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1589079064,16449,2,2.1303300445853386e-14,1018,2,19388,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~0.16 9cs rather than Na+ (which appears at ~1.73 9cs with an amplitude of ~0.81), and there is no Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 9cs after the Na+ peak (around 3.22 9cs), with the next prominent peak appearing much later at ~4.45 9cs.",
1589079435,16745,3-OH,2.904400081982922e-14,1018,3-OH,34778,3-OH,3-OH,"The spectrum features a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.93 s followed by a prominent Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at ~3.42 s (1.49 s later), satisfying both required rules for a '3-OH' label. Additionally, the second hydroxide cluster Na(NaOH)2+ is clearly visible at ~4.46 s (2.53 s after Na+), further confirming the sodium hydroxide series.",
1589079573,16838,1,1.0434599724258673e-14,1018,1,19394,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although there is a dominant peak at ~1.58 5s, there is no Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak at the required ~1.49 5s interval later (around 3.07 5s). Instead, the spectrum exhibits other peaks at ~0.35 5s, ~1.80 5s, and ~4.30 5s, ruling out the 3-OH pattern.",
1589080514,17420,2,5.022870140647395e-14,1018,2,19411,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is located at approximately 0.22 µs rather than being Na+ at ~1.82 µs, violating Rule 1. Furthermore, there is no Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak about 1.49 µs after the 1.82 µs peak (expected around 3.31 µs), with the next major peak appearing much later at ~4.55 µs.",
1589080870,17612,1,4.253559920193613e-14,1018,1,19413,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is located at approximately 0.23 µs rather than being a dominant Na+ peak in the 1.4–2.0 µs range, violating Rule 1. Furthermore, the peak near 1.81 µs is not followed by a Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak about 1.49 µs later (around 3.30 µs), with the next major peak instead appearing much later at ~4.55 µs.",
1589081115,17735,2,7.237239914347285e-14,1018,2,19418,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~0.28 µs rather than being a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 µs. Furthermore, the peak complex near ~1.85 µs is not followed by a Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak 1.49 µs later (at ~3.34 µs), instead showing mineral or organic peaks at ~2.42 µs and ~4.61 µs.",
1589081570,17981,1,1.3899699703126978e-14,1018,1,19425,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the spectrum has a dominant peak at ~1.70 BCs (possibly Na+ or a mineral/organic ion), it completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak about 1.49 BCs later (around 3.19 BCs). Instead, the spectrum features other peaks at ~0.46 BCs, ~1.91 BCs, and ~4.43 BCs, which is characteristic of a mineral or target-ion (Rh+) pattern rather than 3-OH.",
1589081777,18115,1,1.278290031469934e-14,1018,1,19434,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the spectrum has a dominant peak at ~1.62 Γs (likely Na+), it completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ peak about 1.49 Γs later at ~3.11 Γs, showing instead only early peaks at ~0.22 and ~0.37 Γs and a late peak at ~4.36 Γs.",
1589082046,18271,2,3.050619991535643e-14,1018,2,19441,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is at ~1.76 µs (with other prominent peaks at ~0.18 µs, ~1.98 µs, and ~4.50 µs), but there is no Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak located ~1.49 µs later around 3.25 µs. Instead, the spectrum displays a mineral or organic-like peak pattern lacking the sodium hydroxide series.",
1589082053,18274,2,4.958460061272284e-14,1018,2,19442,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"Although the spectrum has a highest peak at ~1.82 µs (and a nearly equal light ion peak at ~0.24 µs), it completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak about 1.49 µs later (around 3.31 µs). Instead, the spectrum shows peaks at ~2.03 µs, ~2.72 µs, and a prominent rhodium target peak (Rh+) at ~4.55 µs.",
1595940640,5152,4,1.6603799498499106e-12,1018,4,19466,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum is classified as 'non-3-OH' because its highest peaks are at ~0.41 9s (likely H+) and ~2.48 9s, rather than a dominant Na+ peak between 1.4 and 2.0 9s. Furthermore, it displays a complex mineral-like profile with broad peaks at ~1.65 9s, ~3.28 9s, ~3.90 9s, and ~5.20 9s instead of a clean sodium hydroxide cluster series.",
1600364561,264,4,1.4704500434664126e-14,1018,4,19468,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The spectrum shows a dominant Na+ peak at ~1.81 6s followed by a secondary peak at ~2.52 6s (a distance of ~0.71 6s, corresponding to K+), and it completely lacks the required Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak ~1.49 6s after Na+ (expected around 3.30 6s).",
1600364642,271,4,4.963499771783175e-13,1018,4,19469,non-3-OH,non-3-OH,"The highest peak is a broad feature centered at approximately 2.02 5s preceded by earlier peaks at ~1.05 5s and ~1.28 5s, and there is no Na(NaOH)+ cluster peak about 1.49 5s later (around 3.51 5s). Instead, the next major peaks appear at ~2.78 5s (~0.76 5s later) and ~4.69 5s, which is characteristic of a mineral or non-hydroxide spectrum.",
